  ('EN-7L-1-10', 'EN-7L-1', 'dialogue-detail', 'What does the mother want?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "A newspaper and some bread."}, {"key": "B", "text": "A book and some milk."}, {"key": "C", "text": "A newspaper and some milk."}, {"key": "D", "text": "A magazine and some juice."}]'::jsonb, 'C', '媽媽說「Please buy me a newspaper. Oh, and some milk from the store next to it.」，她要一份報紙和一些牛奶。', '["媽媽一共要了幾樣東西？", "注意 Oh, and... 後面又補充了什麼。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "男孩要去 bookstore（書店），但媽媽要的是報紙，不是書。", "A": "媽媽要的是 milk，不是 bread，第二樣東西聽錯了。", "D": "雜誌和果汁都沒有出現在對話中。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'M: Mom, I''m going to the bookstore. Do you need anything?
W: Yes, please buy me a newspaper. Oh, and some milk from the store next to it.
M: No problem.
N: Question: What does the mother want?', null),
  ('EN-7L-1-11', 'EN-7L-1', 'dialogue-detail', 'What color is the boy''s umbrella?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Blue."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Red."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Green."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Yellow."}]'::jsonb, 'C', '男孩說「It''s not mine. Mine is green.」，他的傘是綠色的；紅色的傘是 Lisa 的。', '["題目問的是誰的傘？", "男孩說 Mine is... 的時候，後面說的是什麼顏色？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "紅色是 Lisa 的傘，也是桌子底下那把傘的顏色，不是男孩的。", "A": "對話中沒有提到藍色。", "D": "對話中沒有提到黃色。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'W: Whose umbrella is this? It''s under my desk.
M: It''s not mine. Mine is green. I think it''s Lisa''s. She has a red one.
W: This one is red, so it must be Lisa''s.
N: Question: What color is the boy''s umbrella?', null),
  ('EN-7L-1-12', 'EN-7L-1', 'dialogue-detail', 'When will they play tennis?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "On Tuesday."}, {"key": "B", "text": "On Thursday."}, {"key": "C", "text": "On Monday."}, {"key": "D", "text": "On Wednesday."}]'::jsonb, 'D', '男孩提議今天放學打網球，Amy 說星期一有鋼琴課，星期二也忙，問「How about Wednesday?」，男孩回答「Wednesday is fine with me.」，所以他們星期三打網球。', '["Amy 哪幾天沒有空？", "最後兩個人同意的是哪一天？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "星期一 Amy 要上鋼琴課（I have a piano lesson on Mondays），所以不能打球。", "A": "Amy 說 I''m busy on Tuesday, too，星期二也不行。", "B": "對話中沒有提到星期四。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', 'M: Amy, let''s play tennis after school today.
W: Sorry, I have a piano lesson on Mondays. How about Wednesday? I''m busy on Tuesday, too.
M: OK. Wednesday is fine with me.
N: Question: When will they play tennis?', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-01', 'EN-8L-1', 'basic-response', '請聽一句話，選出最適當的回應。（週五放學）', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Yes, I usually do."}, {"key": "B", "text": "I often go hiking with my family."}, {"key": "C", "text": "It''s on the weekend."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Last weekend was very fun."}]'::jsonb, 'B', '聽力原文是「What do you usually do on weekends?」（你週末通常做什麼？），用現在簡單式問習慣，要回答平常的活動：I often go hiking with my family.', '["問句裡的 usually 表示在問一次的事，還是平常的習慣？", "What do you do...? 要回答「做什麼事」。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "只說上週末很好玩，沒有說平常做什麼事，也不是在回答習慣。", "C": "It''s on the weekend. 是回答某件事在什麼時候，沒有說做什麼。", "A": "What 開頭的問句不能用 Yes 或 No 回答。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', 'W: What do you usually do on weekends?', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-02', 'EN-8L-1', 'basic-response', '請聽一句話，選出最適當的回應。（開學第一天）', '[{"key": "A", "text": "It was great. The views were beautiful."}, {"key": "B", "text": "It''s in eastern Taiwan."}, {"key": "C", "text": "I''m going there next month."}, {"key": "D", "text": "I went there by train."}]'::jsonb, 'A', '聽力原文是「How was your trip to Hualien?」（你的花蓮之旅如何？），How was...? 問感想，所以回答 It was great. The views were beautiful.（很棒，風景很美）。', '["How was...? 是問方法還是問感覺？", "旅行已經結束了，對方想知道你覺得怎麼樣。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "By train 是回答 How did you go there?（怎麼去的），不是問感想。", "C": "旅行已經發生了（問句用 was），不能回答「下個月要去」。", "B": "這是回答 Where is Hualien?（花蓮在哪裡）。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', 'M: How was your trip to Hualien?', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-03', 'EN-8L-1', 'basic-response', '請聽一句話，選出最適當的回應。（在教室裡）', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Not at all. Go ahead."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Yes, please. It''s too hot."}, {"key": "C", "text": "The window is very big."}, {"key": "D", "text": "No, it''s closed."}]'::jsonb, 'A', '聽力原文是「Do you mind if I open the window?」（你介意我開窗嗎？），mind 是「介意」，同意對方開窗要說「不介意」：Not at all. Go ahead.（一點也不，請開吧）。', '["mind 是什麼意思？", "如果你同意對方開窗，是「介意」還是「不介意」？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "Yes 表示「我介意」，後面卻說請開、太熱了，前後矛盾，這是 Do you mind...? 最常見的陷阱。", "C": "聽到 window 就選有 window 的句子，但沒有回應對方的請求。", "D": "No, it''s closed. 是回答 Is the window open?，不是回答介不介意。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'M: Do you mind if I open the window?', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-04', 'EN-8L-1', 'basic-response', '請聽一句話，選出最適當的回應。（出門前）', '[{"key": "A", "text": "My cellphone is newer than yours."}, {"key": "B", "text": "I found the test very easy."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Sure, you can use it anywhere."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Did you look in your schoolbag?"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '聽力原文是「I can''t find my cellphone anywhere.」（我到處都找不到我的手機），最適當的回應是幫忙想可能放在哪裡：Did you look in your schoolbag?（你看過書包裡了嗎？）', '["說話的人遇到了什麼問題？", "朋友找不到東西時，你可以怎麼幫他？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "聽到 find 就選有 found 的句子，但 find...easy 是「覺得……很簡單」，和找手機無關。", "A": "聽到 cellphone 就選，但比較誰的手機比較新，沒有回應對方找不到手機的問題。", "C": "聽到 anywhere 就選，但對方不是在借東西，說「你可以在任何地方用」不合理。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'W: I can''t find my cellphone anywhere.', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-05', 'EN-8L-1', 'dialogue-detail', 'Why is Jenny tired?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "She played computer games all night."}, {"key": "B", "text": "She ran in a race this morning."}, {"key": "C", "text": "She took a math test last night."}, {"key": "D", "text": "She went to bed late to study."}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Jenny 說「I stayed up late last night. I was studying for the math test.」，她昨晚熬夜讀書準備數學考試，所以很累。', '["男孩說 Jenny 看起來怎麼樣？Jenny 接著說了什麼原因？", "stay up late 是什麼意思？她熬夜在做什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "對話中沒有提到玩電腦遊戲。", "B": "對話中沒有提到賽跑。", "C": "數學考試在今天下午（This afternoon），昨晚是在準備考試，不是考試。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', 'M: Hi, Jenny. You look tired.
W: I stayed up late last night. I was studying for the math test.
M: When is the test?
W: This afternoon.
N: Question: Why is Jenny tired?', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-06', 'EN-8L-1', 'dialogue-detail', 'How much will the woman pay?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "300 dollars."}, {"key": "B", "text": "600 dollars."}, {"key": "C", "text": "800 dollars."}, {"key": "D", "text": "500 dollars."}]'::jsonb, 'D', '店員說一件 300 元，但「if you buy two, they''re five hundred」（買兩件 500 元），女士說「I''ll take two.」，所以她要付 500 元。', '["一件多少錢？買兩件有什麼優惠？", "女士最後決定買幾件？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "300 元是一件的價錢，但她買了兩件。", "B": "直接用 300 × 2 計算，忽略了買兩件只要 500 元的優惠。", "C": "把 300 和 500 加起來，誤會了兩個價錢的意思。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'W: Excuse me. How much is this T-shirt?
M: It''s three hundred dollars. But if you buy two, they''re five hundred.
W: Great. I''ll take two.
N: Question: How much will the woman pay?', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-07', 'EN-8L-1', 'dialogue-detail', 'How will the girl go to school today?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "By car."}, {"key": "B", "text": "By bus."}, {"key": "C", "text": "By bike."}, {"key": "D", "text": "On foot."}]'::jsonb, 'B', '女孩想請爸爸開車送她，但爸爸說「My car is broken. Why don''t you take the bus?」，女孩回答「OK.」，所以她今天搭公車上學。', '["爸爸可以開車送她嗎？為什麼？", "爸爸建議她怎麼去？她同意了嗎？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "女孩一開始想坐爸爸的車，但爸爸的車壞了（My car is broken）。", "D": "對話中沒有說要走路去，公車站就在大樓前面，她要去搭公車。", "C": "對話中沒有提到腳踏車，而且下大雨也不適合騎車。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'W: Dad, can you drive me to school today? It''s raining hard.
M: Sorry, honey. My car is broken. Why don''t you take the bus? The bus stop is right in front of our building.
W: OK. I''ll take my umbrella.
N: Question: How will the girl go to school today?', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-08', 'EN-8L-1', 'announcement', 'Why will the library close early today?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "The library will be cleaned."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Today is a holiday."}, {"key": "C", "text": "There is a teachers'' meeting."}, {"key": "D", "text": "The weather is very bad."}]'::jsonb, 'C', '廣播說「The school library will close early today, at three thirty, because of a teachers'' meeting.」，because of 後面說出原因：有教師會議。', '["廣播一開始說圖書館今天會怎麼樣？", "注意 because of 後面接的內容。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "廣播中沒有提到天氣。", "B": "廣播中沒有說今天放假，明天八點還會照常開。", "A": "廣播中沒有提到打掃圖書館。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', 'N: Attention, please. The school library will close early today, at three thirty, because of a teachers'' meeting. It will open again tomorrow at eight. Thank you.
N: Question: Why will the library close early today?', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-09', 'EN-8L-1', 'announcement', 'Until what time can people buy fruit at half price today?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Until 9 a.m."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Until 10 p.m."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Until 6 p.m."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Until 12 noon."}]'::jsonb, 'C', '廣播說「Today all fruit is half price, but only until six p.m.」，水果半價只到下午六點；晚上十點是商店的打烊時間。', '["廣播裡出現了好幾個時間，各是什麼事情的時間？", "注意 but only until... 後面接的時間。"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "早上九點是商店開門的時間，不是特價結束的時間。", "B": "晚上十點是商店打烊的時間，特價只到六點。", "D": "廣播中沒有提到中午。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'N: Good morning, shoppers. Welcome to Happy Market. We are open from nine a.m. to ten p.m. every day. Today all fruit is half price, but only until six p.m. Come and get some fresh apples and bananas!
N: Question: Until what time can people buy fruit at half price today?', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-10', 'EN-8L-1', 'announcement', 'What do we know about the train to Kaohsiung?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "It will arrive at Platform 1 at ten fifteen."}, {"key": "B", "text": "It will arrive at Platform 2 at ten o''clock."}, {"key": "C", "text": "It is late because of an accident."}, {"key": "D", "text": "It will arrive at Platform 2 at ten fifteen."}]'::jsonb, 'D', '廣播說「The train to Kaohsiung will arrive at Platform 2 at ten fifteen, not ten o''clock. It is fifteen minutes late because of heavy rain.」，火車會在 10:15 到達第 2 月臺，誤點原因是大雨。', '["火車原本幾點到？現在改成幾點？", "注意月臺號碼和誤點的原因，選項只要有一個地方不對就不能選。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "廣播特別說 not ten o''clock，十點是原本的時間，現在誤點了。", "A": "時間對了，但月臺是 Platform 2，不是 1。", "C": "誤點的原因是 heavy rain（大雨），不是意外事故。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', 'N: Attention, please. The train to Kaohsiung will arrive at Platform 2 at ten fifteen, not ten o''clock. It is fifteen minutes late because of heavy rain. We are sorry for the trouble.
N: Question: What do we know about the train to Kaohsiung?', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-11', 'EN-8L-1', 'message', 'Why did Grace leave this message?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "To invite Kevin to her house for dinner."}, {"key": "B", "text": "To change the time of their plan."}, {"key": "C", "text": "To tell Kevin she lost her museum ticket."}, {"key": "D", "text": "To ask Kevin to visit her grandmother."}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'Grace 說「I can''t go to the museum with you tomorrow morning... Can we go on Sunday afternoon instead?」，她明天早上不能去，想改成星期天下午，所以留言是為了更改計畫的時間。', '["Grace 原本和 Kevin 約好做什麼？", "她為什麼不能去？她提出了什麼新的時間？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "是 Grace 的奶奶要來拜訪她（my grandmother is coming to visit），不是請 Kevin 去看奶奶。", "A": "留言中沒有邀請 Kevin 來家裡吃晚餐。", "C": "留言中沒有提到門票遺失。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'W: Hi, Kevin. This is Grace. I can''t go to the museum with you tomorrow morning because my grandmother is coming to visit. Can we go on Sunday afternoon instead? Please call me back. Thanks.
N: Question: Why did Grace leave this message?', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-12', 'EN-8L-1', 'message', 'What do we know from the message?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "The bike shop isn''t open tomorrow."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Ms. Lee must get her bike before seven tonight."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Ms. Lee needs to pay 300 dollars more than she first thought."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Ms. Lee''s bike won''t be ready until tomorrow."}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'Sam 說「it''s eight hundred dollars, not five hundred」，原本說 500 元，現在要 800 元，所以李小姐要比原本多付 300 元（800 − 500 = 300）。其他選項都和「Your bike is ready」「we''re open all day tomorrow」不符。', '["原本說的價錢和現在的價錢各是多少？", "再注意：腳踏車修好了沒？店明天有沒有開？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "留言一開始就說 Your bike is ready（已經修好了）。", "A": "留言說 we''re open all day tomorrow，明天整天都有開。", "B": "店今晚七點關門，但明天整天都有開，所以不是一定要今晚拿。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', 'M: Hello, Ms. Lee. This is Sam from Fast Bike Shop. Your bike is ready, but the price is a little higher than we said. We had to change some parts, so it''s eight hundred dollars, not five hundred. We close at seven tonight, but we''re open all day tomorrow.
N: Question: What do we know from the message?', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-01', 'EN-9L-1', 'basic-response', '請聽一句話，選出最適當的回應。（認識新朋友）', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Yes, I went there two years ago."}, {"key": "B", "text": "It takes about three hours by plane."}, {"key": "C", "text": "No, I''ve visited it twice."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Yes, I''ll go there next summer."}]'::jsonb, 'A', '聽力原文是「Have you ever been to Japan?」（你曾經去過日本嗎？），問經驗，回答 Yes 後補充去的時間：Yes, I went there two years ago.', '["Have you ever been to...? 是在問什麼？", "回答 Yes 或 No 之後，後面的內容要和前面一致。"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "說 No（沒去過）卻又說去過兩次，前後矛盾。", "D": "next summer 是還沒發生的事，說 Yes（去過）卻講未來，意思矛盾。", "B": "這是回答 How long does it take...?（要花多久時間），不是問經驗。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', 'M: Have you ever been to Japan?', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-02', 'EN-9L-1', 'basic-response', '請聽一句話，選出最適當的回應。（在街上）', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Sure. It''s next to the bank."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Yes, I could tell you a story."}, {"key": "C", "text": "It opens at nine in the morning."}, {"key": "D", "text": "I sent a letter yesterday."}]'::jsonb, 'A', '聽力原文是「Could you tell me where the post office is?」（你可以告訴我郵局在哪裡嗎？），這是間接問句，真正問的是地點，所以回答 It''s next to the bank.（在銀行旁邊）。', '["這句話真正想知道的是什麼？", "注意 tell me 後面的 where..."]'::jsonb, '{"B": "聽到 Could you tell me 就回答「我可以講故事」，沒有聽懂真正問的是地點。", "D": "聽到 post office 想到寄信，但對方沒有問你寄了什麼。", "C": "這是回答郵局幾點開門（When does it open?），不是在哪裡。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', 'W: Could you tell me where the post office is?', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-03', 'EN-9L-1', 'basic-response', '請聽一句話，選出最適當的回應。（在家裡）', '[{"key": "A", "text": "I''ve finished my homework, too."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Let me finish my homework first."}, {"key": "C", "text": "The TV show was boring last night."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Sure, but turn it off before nine."}]'::jsonb, 'D', '聽力原文是「I''ve finished my homework. Can I watch TV now?」（我功課寫完了，現在可以看電視嗎？），孩子在請求允許，媽媽回答 Sure, but turn it off before nine.（可以，但九點前要關掉）最適當。', '["說話的人最後問的是什麼？", "Can I...? 是請求允許，回答要表示可不可以。"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "聽到 finished my homework 就跟著說「我也寫完了」，但沒有回答能不能看電視。", "B": "要寫功課的是孩子，而且他已經寫完了，回答的人不需要寫功課。", "C": "聽到 TV 就選有 TV 的句子，但昨晚節目好不好看和現在能不能看無關。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'M: I''ve finished my homework. Can I watch TV now?', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-04', 'EN-9L-1', 'basic-response', '請聽一句話，選出最適當的回應。（放學路上）', '[{"key": "A", "text": "I left my wallet on the bus."}, {"key": "B", "text": "You''re right. The answer is wrong."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Yes, I''m very happy today."}, {"key": "D", "text": "I''m worried about you, too."}]'::jsonb, 'A', '聽力原文是「You look worried. What''s wrong?」（你看起來很擔心，怎麼了？），要說出讓自己擔心的事：I left my wallet on the bus.（我把錢包忘在公車上了）。', '["對方覺得你看起來怎麼樣？", "What''s wrong? 是問「怎麼了」，要說出發生了什麼事。"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "對方說你看起來很擔心，回答「我今天很開心」不合理，而且 What 問句不用 Yes 回答。", "B": "聽到 wrong 就選有 wrong 的句子，但 What''s wrong? 是「怎麼了」，不是在問答案對不對。", "D": "聽到 worried 就選有 worried 的句子，但對方是在關心你，你沒有說明發生了什麼事。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'W: You look worried. What''s wrong?', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-05', 'EN-9L-1', 'dialogue-inference', 'Where are the speakers?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "In a bookstore."}, {"key": "B", "text": "In a supermarket."}, {"key": "C", "text": "In a classroom."}, {"key": "D", "text": "In a restaurant."}]'::jsonb, 'D', '女士說「Can I have the menu, please?」，男士介紹「Today''s special is beef noodles.」，女士點了「the vegetable fried rice」，有菜單、今日特餐和點餐，可推論他們在餐廳。', '["對話中出現了哪些和吃東西有關的字？", "menu、today''s special 通常在哪裡會聽到？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "書店不會有菜單和點餐。", "B": "超市可以買食物，但不會拿菜單點今日特餐和炒飯。", "C": "對話中沒有和上課有關的內容。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', 'W: Excuse me, sir. Can I have the menu, please?
M: Here you are. Today''s special is beef noodles.
W: Hmm, I don''t eat meat. I''ll have the vegetable fried rice.
N: Question: Where are the speakers?', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-06', 'EN-9L-1', 'dialogue-inference', 'What will the boy probably do?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Wear his old soccer shoes."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Stay home and miss the game."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Buy new shoes at the store."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Wash his soccer shoes again."}]'::jsonb, 'A', '球鞋昨天洗了還沒乾（Maybe they aren''t dry yet），比賽三十分鐘後就開始，男孩說「I''ll have to wear my old ones then.」，ones 指 soccer shoes，所以他會穿舊的足球鞋。', '["男孩的足球鞋為什麼不能穿？", "最後一句 I''ll have to wear my old ones 的 ones 指的是什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "鞋子昨天已經洗過了，問題是還沒乾，不是要再洗一次。", "B": "男孩說要穿舊鞋去，並沒有說不去比賽。", "C": "比賽三十分鐘後就開始，對話中也沒有提到要買新鞋。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'M: Mom, have you seen my soccer shoes? The game starts in thirty minutes!
W: I washed them yesterday. They''re still outside in the sun. Maybe they aren''t dry yet.
M: Oh no! I''ll have to wear my old ones then.
N: Question: What will the boy probably do?', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-07', 'EN-9L-1', 'dialogue-inference', 'How did Jason feel about the concert?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "He didn''t like the singer at all."}, {"key": "B", "text": "He liked the singer but was unhappy about other things."}, {"key": "C", "text": "He thought everything was perfect."}, {"key": "D", "text": "He was sorry that he didn''t go."}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'Jason 說「the singer was great, but we sat in the last row, and I couldn''t see anything」，還說旁邊的人一直講話。but 前面是優點（歌手很棒），後面是缺點（座位差、旁人吵），所以他喜歡歌手，但對其他事情不滿意。', '["Jason 先說了什麼優點？", "注意 but 後面說的內容，是開心還是不開心的事？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "Jason 說 the singer was great，他很喜歡歌手。", "C": "他抱怨坐最後一排看不到、旁邊的人一直講話，並不是一切都很完美。", "D": "Jason 昨晚有去演唱會，才會知道座位和旁邊的人的狀況。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'W: Did you enjoy the concert last night, Jason?
M: Well, the singer was great, but we sat in the last row, and I couldn''t see anything. Also, the people next to me talked the whole time.
W: That''s too bad.
N: Question: How did Jason feel about the concert?', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-08', 'EN-9L-1', 'dialogue-inference', 'What can we infer about Linda?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "She has decided not to go on the trip."}, {"key": "B", "text": "She can get enough money for the trip before Monday."}, {"key": "C", "text": "She will work at her aunt''s shop for only one day."}, {"key": "D", "text": "She has already paid two thousand dollars."}]'::jsonb, 'B', '旅行要 2000 元，Linda 說「I''ve saved only twelve hundred so far.」，還差 800 元。她說這個週末的星期六和星期日兩天都要去阿姨店裡幫忙，「She''ll pay me five hundred dollars a day.」，可以賺 500 × 2 = 1000 元，1200 + 1000 = 2200 元，超過 2000 元，而且週末在星期一報名截止之前，所以她能在星期一前湊到旅費。', '["旅行要多少錢？Linda 已經存了多少？還差多少？", "週末有幾天？一天可以賺多少？算算看夠不夠，而且來不來得及在報名截止前。"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "Linda 說 I really want to，還打算週末打工賺錢，並沒有決定不去。", "D": "她只存了 1200 元，還沒有付 2000 元。", "C": "她說 both Saturday and Sunday，是兩天，不是只有一天。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', 'M: Linda, are you joining the school trip to Kenting next Friday?
W: I really want to, but it costs two thousand dollars. I''ve saved only twelve hundred so far.
M: The last day to sign up is next Monday, right?
W: Yes. This weekend I''ll help at my aunt''s shop on both Saturday and Sunday. She''ll pay me five hundred dollars a day.
N: Question: What can we infer about Linda?', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-09', 'EN-9L-1', 'announcement', 'What should students do after their last class today?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Go home."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Go to the playground."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Go to their clubs."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Stay in the classroom."}]'::jsonb, 'A', '廣播說颱風要來，今天沒有社團活動，並提醒「Please go home right after your last class.」，所以最後一堂課後要直接回家。', '["廣播一開始說了什麼天氣狀況？", "注意 Please... 後面要學生做的事。"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "廣播說 there will be no after-school club activities today，今天沒有社團活動。", "D": "廣播沒有要學生留在教室。", "B": "颱風要來，廣播要學生回家，沒有提到操場。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', 'N: Good afternoon, students. Because a typhoon is coming, there will be no after-school club activities today. Please go home right after your last class. Be careful on your way home.
N: Question: What should students do after their last class today?', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-10', 'EN-9L-1', 'announcement', 'Which of the following is allowed at the zoo?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Talking loudly in the Night Animal House."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Giving food to the animals."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Having lunch in the picnic area near the main gate."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Eating snacks while walking around the zoo."}]'::jsonb, 'C', '廣播說「Lunch is only allowed in the picnic area near the main gate.」，在大門附近的野餐區吃午餐是允許的；餵動物、在夜行動物館大聲說話、邊走邊吃都不符合規定。', '["廣播一共說了幾條規定？", "注意 only allowed 後面說的地點。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "廣播說 Please do not feed the animals，不可以餵動物。", "A": "廣播說 please be quiet in the Night Animal House，要保持安靜。", "D": "吃東西只能在野餐區（only allowed in the picnic area），不能邊走邊吃。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'N: Welcome to Green Mountain Zoo. Here are some rules for your visit. Please do not feed the animals because they have special food. Please be quiet in the Night Animal House. Lunch is only allowed in the picnic area near the main gate. Enjoy your day!
N: Question: Which of the following is allowed at the zoo?', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-11', 'EN-9L-1', 'message', 'What does Uncle Ben want Sara to do?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Call him before six o''clock."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Tell him what kind of food she wants."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Cook dinner for him on Tuesday."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Pick him up at the train station."}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'Ben 叔叔說要請 Sara 和弟弟吃晚餐，最後說「Send me a message and tell me what kind of food you want.」，他要 Sara 告訴他想吃什麼。', '["Ben 叔叔打電話來是要做什麼？", "留言最後他請 Sara 做什麼事？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "留言中沒有提到去車站接他。", "C": "是叔叔要請他們出去吃晚餐（take you out for dinner），不是要 Sara 煮飯。", "A": "six 是叔叔有空的時間（I''ll be free after six），他是要 Sara 傳訊息，不是六點前打電話。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'M: Hi, Sara. It''s Uncle Ben. I''m coming to Taipei for work next Tuesday. I''d love to take you and your brother out for dinner on Tuesday night. I''ll be free after six. Send me a message and tell me what kind of food you want. See you soon!
N: Question: What does Uncle Ben want Sara to do?', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-12', 'EN-9L-1', 'message', 'When will the class have the speech contest?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "On Wednesday."}, {"key": "B", "text": "On Friday."}, {"key": "C", "text": "On Thursday."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Next Thursday."}]'::jsonb, 'B', '黃老師說演講比賽原本在「this Thursday」，但那天禮堂要開會，所以「we''ll have the contest one day later, at the same time」。星期四的後一天是星期五，所以比賽在星期五。', '["比賽原本是星期幾？為什麼要改？", "one day later 是往後延幾天？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "星期四是原本的日期，因為禮堂要開會已經改期了。", "A": "one day later 是往後一天，不是提前一天。", "D": "只延後一天，不是延到下星期四。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', 'W: Hi, Mike. This is Ms. Huang, your English teacher. Our class''s speech contest was planned for this Thursday, but the school hall will be used for a meeting that day. So we''ll have the contest one day later, at the same time. Please tell the other students in your group. Thanks.
N: Question: When will the class have the speech contest?', null),
  ('EN-7A-1-13', 'EN-7A-1', 'be-verb', 'Hi, I''m Rick. Welcome to my classroom! It is big and clean. Mr. Chen and Ms. Lee (1)＿＿＿ our teachers. Mr. Chen is our math teacher, and Ms. Lee is our English teacher. Mr. Chen is in the classroom now, but Ms. Lee (2)＿＿＿ here. She is in the teachers'' office with some students.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "is; isn''t"}, {"key": "B", "text": "are; isn''t"}, {"key": "C", "text": "are; aren''t"}, {"key": "D", "text": "is; is"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '(1) 主詞 Mr. Chen and Ms. Lee 是兩個人，屬於複數，be 動詞用 are。(2) 前面說陳老師在教室，用 but 轉折，後面又說 She is in the teachers'' office（她在教師辦公室），所以李老師「不在這裡」，主詞 Ms. Lee 是單數，否定用 isn''t。', '["(1) 的主詞有幾個人？", "but 前後的意思相同還是相反？李老師現在在哪裡？", "單數主詞的 be 動詞否定是 isn''t 還是 aren''t？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "只看到靠近空格的 Ms. Lee，忽略 (1) 的主詞是 Mr. Chen and Ms. Lee 兩個人，要用複數 are。", "C": "(2) 的主詞 Ms. Lee 只有一個人，否定要用單數的 isn''t。", "D": "(1) 主詞是兩個人要用 are；而且 but 表示轉折，後面又說她在辦公室，(2) 應該是「不在這裡」的否定。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-1-14', 'EN-7A-1', 'be-verb', 'Amy: Who are the people in this photo, Jack?
Jack: They''re my grandparents. And the girl with the dog is my cousin, Nina.
Amy: Are your grandparents from Taichung?
Jack: My grandfather (1)＿＿＿, but my grandmother (2)＿＿＿. She is from Hualien.
Amy: Is Nina from Hualien, too?
Jack: No, she isn''t. She''s from Taipei.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "isn''t; is"}, {"key": "B", "text": "is; is"}, {"key": "C", "text": "is; isn''t"}, {"key": "D", "text": "are; aren''t"}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'Amy 問爺爺奶奶是不是台中人。Jack 用 but 連接兩句，表示爺爺和奶奶的情況相反；下一句 She is from Hualien. 說明奶奶來自花蓮，所以奶奶「不是」台中人，爺爺「是」台中人。主詞 my grandfather、my grandmother 都是單數，所以 (1) 用 is（= is from Taichung），(2) 用 isn''t。', '["She is from Hualien. 的 She 指的是誰？", "那麼爺爺和奶奶，誰是台中人？", "每一格的主詞是一個人還是兩個人？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "把順序弄反了；Jack 說奶奶來自花蓮，所以不是台中人的是奶奶，不是爺爺。", "D": "(1) 的 my grandfather 和 (2) 的 my grandmother 各自都只有一個人，要用單數 is / isn''t。", "B": "but 表示前後相反，而且下一句說奶奶來自花蓮，所以 (2) 要用否定。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-1-15', 'EN-7A-1', 'pronoun', 'Ben: Is this your cap, Amy? It''s on your desk.
Amy: No, it isn''t (1)＿＿＿. Mine is blue, and it''s in my bag. Is it Mike''s?
Ben: I don''t think so. (2)＿＿＿ cap is red, and this one is green.
Amy: Oh, then it''s Jenny''s. Jenny''s seat is next to mine, and her cap is green.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "mine; His"}, {"key": "B", "text": "my; His"}, {"key": "C", "text": "mine; He"}, {"key": "D", "text": "me; Him"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '(1) 空格後面沒有名詞，要用所有格代名詞 mine（= my cap），而且下一句 Mine is blue 也用同一個字。(2) 空格後面接名詞 cap，要用所有格形容詞；指的是 Mike（男生），所以是 His cap（他的帽子）。', '["(1) 空格後面還有名詞嗎？下一句用了哪個字表示「我的帽子」？", "(2) 空格後面接了什麼名詞？指的是男生還是女生？", "所有格形容詞後面要接名詞，所有格代名詞後面不接名詞。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "my 是所有格形容詞，後面一定要接名詞；(1) 後面沒有名詞，要用所有格代名詞 mine。", "C": "He 是主格，不能放在名詞 cap 前面表示「他的」。", "D": "me、Him 是受格，不能表示「我的」「他的」。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-1-16', 'EN-7A-1', 'pronoun', 'Hi, I''m Paul. These are my neighbors, Mr. and Mrs. Hill. They are from the U.S. Their son, Jack, is ten. He is a student at my sister''s school. Jack and my sister are good friends. Their teacher is Ms. Lin. She is young and very funny, and her class is always fun.

Who is Ms. Lin?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Paul''s teacher"}, {"key": "B", "text": "The teacher of Jack and Paul''s sister"}, {"key": "C", "text": "Jack''s mother"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Mr. and Mrs. Hill''s daughter"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '文中有兩個 Their。第一個 Their son 的 Their 指 Mr. and Mrs. Hill；第二個 Their teacher is Ms. Lin. 緊接在 Jack and my sister are good friends. 之後，所以 Their 指 Jack 和 Paul 的姊姊（妹妹）。因此林老師是 Jack 和 Paul 姊妹的老師。', '["文中出現了兩次 Their，分別在哪兩句？", "Their teacher is Ms. Lin. 的前一句提到了哪兩個人？", "代名詞通常指最靠近、而且數量相符的名詞。"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "第二個 Their 指的是前一句的 Jack and my sister，文中沒有說 Paul 也是林老師的學生。", "D": "把第一個 Their（Hill 夫婦）和第二個 Their 搞混了；Hill 夫婦的孩子是兒子 Jack。", "C": "Jack 的媽媽是 Mrs. Hill，不是林老師。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-1-17', 'EN-7A-1', 'reading-detail', 'Our school''s sports day is this Friday. The running race is at 9:00 in the morning, and the basketball game is at 1:00 in the afternoon. My brother Ken is in the running race. My sister and I aren''t in the race; we are on the basketball team. Mom and Dad are at work in the morning, but in the afternoon, they are at school with us.

Where are Mom and Dad at 1:00 on Friday?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "At work"}, {"key": "B", "text": "At the running race"}, {"key": "C", "text": "At home"}, {"key": "D", "text": "At the basketball game"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '文中說 Mom and Dad are at work in the morning, but in the afternoon, they are at school with us.（爸媽早上上班，下午和我們在學校）。下午 1 點學校進行的是籃球賽（the basketball game is at 1:00 in the afternoon），作者和姊妹都在籃球隊，所以爸媽下午 1 點在看籃球賽。', '["1:00 是上午還是下午？那時學校在比什麼？", "爸媽上午和下午分別在哪裡？", "with us 的 us 是誰？他們參加哪一項比賽？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "爸媽只有早上在上班，下午 1 點已經到學校了。", "B": "賽跑在早上 9 點，那時爸媽還在上班；下午 1 點是籃球賽。", "C": "文中說下午 they are at school with us，他們在學校，不在家。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-1-18', 'EN-7A-1', 'reading-detail', 'Hi, I''m Tina. Lily, Rose, and I are classmates in Class 703. Lily is twelve. Rose and I aren''t twelve; we are thirteen. Rose and Lily are in the dance club, and I am in the music club. Rose is tall, and her hair is long. Lily is short, and her hair is short, too.

Who is thirteen and in the dance club?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Rose"}, {"key": "B", "text": "Lily"}, {"key": "C", "text": "Lily and Rose"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Tina"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '先找 13 歲的人：Rose and I aren''t twelve; we are thirteen.，I 是 Tina，所以 Rose 和 Tina 是 13 歲。再找舞蹈社：Rose and Lily are in the dance club。兩個條件都符合的只有 Rose。', '["題目有兩個條件，先找出誰是 13 歲。", "we are thirteen 的 we 指誰？", "再看誰在舞蹈社，兩個條件都符合的是誰？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "Tina 是 13 歲沒錯，但她在音樂社，不是舞蹈社。", "B": "Lily 在舞蹈社，但她只有 12 歲。", "C": "她們兩人都在舞蹈社，但 Lily 是 12 歲，不符合「13 歲」這個條件。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-1-13', 'EN-7B-1', 'present-progressive', 'Kate: Where''s Dad? He usually (1)＿＿＿ the newspaper on the sofa after dinner.
Mom: Not tonight. Look! He (2)＿＿＿ the dishes in the kitchen.
Kate: Really? Why?
Mom: I''m not feeling well tonight, so he is helping me. Let''s help him, too.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "read; is washing"}, {"key": "B", "text": "is reading; washes"}, {"key": "C", "text": "reads; is washing"}, {"key": "D", "text": "reads; washes"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '(1) 有 usually（通常），說的是爸爸平常晚餐後的習慣，用現在簡單式；主詞 He 是第三人稱單數，所以是 reads。(2) 媽媽說 Not tonight. Look!，表示今晚和平常不同，而且動作正在發生，用現在進行式 is washing。', '["(1) 的句子裡有哪個頻率副詞？它說的是習慣還是現在？", "Look! 提示 (2) 的動作是什麼時候發生的？", "主詞 He 用現在簡單式時，動詞要不要變化？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "把兩格顛倒了：usually 說的是平常習慣，要用現在簡單式；Look! 才是正在發生。", "D": "Look! 表示動作此刻正在進行，(2) 要用現在進行式。", "A": "主詞 He 是第三人稱單數，現在簡單式的動詞要加 s。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-1-14', 'EN-7B-1', 'present-progressive', 'It''s a hot Sunday afternoon at the swimming pool. Look at the three boys over there. Two of them (1)＿＿＿ in the water, and the other one (2)＿＿＿ on a chair under a big umbrella. He is drinking some juice and reading a comic book. Their mothers are talking near the pool.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "swim; sits"}, {"key": "B", "text": "are swiming; is siting"}, {"key": "C", "text": "are swimming; is sitting"}, {"key": "D", "text": "is swimming; are sitting"}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'Look at... 表示正在看的畫面，要用現在進行式 be + V-ing（下一句 He is drinking 也是）。(1) 主詞 Two of them 是複數，用 are；swim 要重複 m 再加 ing。(2) 主詞 the other one 是單數，用 is；sit 要重複 t 再加 ing。', '["Look at... 和下一句 He is drinking 提示要用什麼時態？", "Two of them 和 the other one 各是幾個人？", "swim、sit 加 ing 時，字尾子音要不要重複？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "Two of them 是兩個人，要用 are；the other one 只有一個人，要用 is。", "B": "swim、sit 都是「短母音 + 單一子音」結尾，加 ing 前要重複字尾子音：swimming、sitting。", "A": "Look at... 表示眼前正在發生的動作，要用現在進行式，而且下一句也用 is drinking。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-1-15', 'EN-7B-1', 'imperative', 'City Library Rules
1. Don''t eat or drink near the computers.
2. Talk quietly. People are reading.
3. Put the books on the front desk after reading.

A girl is drinking juice at a computer. She isn''t talking, and her books are already on the front desk. What is the librarian probably saying to her?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Please take your juice outside."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Please talk quietly."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Please sit at the computer and drink."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Please put the books on the front desk."}]'::jsonb, 'A', '女孩正在電腦旁喝果汁（is drinking juice at a computer），違反第 1 條 Don''t eat or drink near the computers.。她沒有講話、書也已經放好，所以館員最可能用祈使句請她把果汁拿到外面：Please take your juice outside.', '["女孩現在正在做哪些事？", "把她的行為和三條規則一一對照，她違反了哪一條？", "館員要她做的事，應該能解決她違反的那條規則。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "題目說她沒有在講話，沒有違反第 2 條規則。", "D": "她的書已經放在服務台上了，沒有違反第 3 條規則。", "C": "第 1 條規則說不可以在電腦旁邊吃喝，這句話剛好和規則相反。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-1-16', 'EN-7B-1', 'imperative', 'It''s the first class of the day, and the students are noisy.
Ms. Wang: Good morning, class. Please be quiet and (1)＿＿＿ your books to page 20. Tim, you are talking to Joe again. (2)＿＿＿ talk in class. Listen to me, please.
Tim: Sorry, Ms. Wang. I''m listening now.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "open; Doesn''t"}, {"key": "B", "text": "opens; Don''t"}, {"key": "C", "text": "opening; Not"}, {"key": "D", "text": "open; Don''t"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '老師在下指令，用祈使句（原形動詞開頭）。(1) and 連接 be quiet 和另一個指令，兩者都是原形，所以是 open your books。(2) 老師要 Tim 不要在課堂上說話，否定祈使句是 Don''t + 原形動詞：Don''t talk in class.', '["老師說這些話是在描述事情，還是在要求學生做事？", "and 前面的 be quiet 是什麼形式？後面的動詞要和它一樣嗎？", "否定的祈使句要用哪個字開頭？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "祈使句用原形動詞，and 前面的 be quiet 是原形，後面的動詞也要用原形 open。", "A": "祈使句沒有主詞，否定時用 Don''t，不用第三人稱單數的 Doesn''t。", "C": "祈使句不能用 V-ing；否定祈使句也不能只用 Not 開頭。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-1-17', 'EN-7B-1', 'reading-detail', 'Dear Andy,
I''m at Grandma''s house now. She is sick, and I am taking care of her. Dad is working late tonight, so please make some noodles for dinner. Feed the cat at six, and don''t open the door for strangers. Do your homework first, and then you can play video games. See you tomorrow morning!
Love,
Mom

Which is NOT something Mom asks Andy to do?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Visit Grandma tonight"}, {"key": "B", "text": "Do homework before playing games"}, {"key": "C", "text": "Feed the cat at six"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Cook noodles for dinner"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '媽媽用祈使句交代 Andy：煮麵當晚餐、六點餵貓、不要幫陌生人開門、先寫功課再玩遊戲。媽媽自己在奶奶家照顧奶奶，並沒有要 Andy 去探望奶奶，所以「今晚去看奶奶」不是媽媽要他做的事。題目問 NOT，選這一項。', '["題目問的是「沒有」要 Andy 做的事。", "把紙條裡以原形動詞開頭的句子都圈出來。", "在奶奶家的人是誰？媽媽有叫 Andy 過去嗎？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "媽媽寫了 please make some noodles for dinner，這是她交代的事。", "C": "媽媽寫了 Feed the cat at six，這是她交代的事。", "B": "Do your homework first, and then you can play video games. 就是先寫功課再玩遊戲，是媽媽交代的事。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-1-18', 'EN-7B-1', 'reading-detail', 'Dad: Hi, Jenny. Where are you?
Jenny: I''m at the bookstore with Lucy. We''re looking for a dictionary for our English class.
Dad: Is your brother with you?
Jenny: No. He''s at the park. He and his friends are playing basketball there.
Dad: OK. Please come home before six. We''re having dinner at Grandma''s house tonight. Don''t be late!

Which is TRUE?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Jenny''s brother is at the bookstore."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Lucy is buying a dictionary for Dad."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Jenny is playing basketball with Lucy."}, {"key": "D", "text": "The family is having dinner at Grandma''s house tonight."}]'::jsonb, 'D', '爸爸說 We''re having dinner at Grandma''s house tonight.，現在進行式也可以表示已經安排好的計畫，意思是今晚全家要去奶奶家吃晚餐。其他選項：Jenny 和 Lucy 在書店、哥哥（弟弟）在公園打籃球、字典是英文課要用的。', '["Jenny 和 Lucy 在哪裡？在做什麼？", "Jenny 的兄弟在哪裡？", "爸爸最後提到今晚的什麼安排？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "Jenny 和 Lucy 在書店找字典；打籃球的是 Jenny 的哥哥（弟弟）和他的朋友。", "A": "Jenny 說 No. He''s at the park.，哥哥（弟弟）在公園。", "B": "字典是她們英文課要用的，和爸爸無關。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-2-13', 'EN-7A-2', 'simple-present', 'My cousin Leo (1)＿＿＿ in Kaohsiung. He and his parents (2)＿＿＿ near a big park, so they often go jogging there in the morning. Leo''s sister, Mia, doesn''t go with them. She always sleeps late on weekends, and she doesn''t like sports.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "lives; lives"}, {"key": "B", "text": "living; live"}, {"key": "C", "text": "lives; live"}, {"key": "D", "text": "live; lives"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '這段話描述長期的事實和習慣，用現在簡單式。(1) 主詞 My cousin Leo 是第三人稱單數，動詞加 s：lives。(2) 主詞 He and his parents 是複數，動詞用原形 live。', '["這段文章說的是現在正在發生的事，還是平常的事實？", "(1) 和 (2) 的主詞分別是單數還是複數？", "He and his parents 一共有幾個人？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "把兩格顛倒了：(1) 主詞 Leo 是第三人稱單數要加 s，(2) 主詞是複數不加 s。", "A": "(2) 的主詞是 He and his parents（三個人），是複數，動詞不加 s。", "B": "living 前面沒有 be 動詞，不能當句子的動詞。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-2-14', 'EN-7A-2', 'simple-present', 'Sue: (1)＿＿＿ you and your brother go to the same school?
Tom: No. I go to Sunshine Junior High School, but he (2)＿＿＿. He is only nine, so he goes to Hope Elementary School.
Sue: How does he get there?
Tom: My dad drives him there every morning.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Do; doesn''t"}, {"key": "B", "text": "Do; don''t"}, {"key": "C", "text": "Do; isn''t"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Does; doesn''t"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '(1) 句中有一般動詞 go，疑問句要用助動詞；主詞 you and your brother 是複數，用 Do。(2) but he doesn''t 是 but he doesn''t go to Sunshine Junior High School 的省略，主詞 he 是第三人稱單數，用 doesn''t。後面說他去 Hope Elementary School，可以印證是否定。', '["(1) 句子的動詞 go 是一般動詞還是 be 動詞？主詞有幾個人？", "(2) 省略了哪些字？他到底有沒有去 Sunshine Junior High？", "he 用的助動詞否定是哪一個？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "(1) 的主詞是 you and your brother 兩個人，是複數，要用 Do。", "B": "(2) 的主詞 he 是第三人稱單數，否定要用 doesn''t。", "C": "(2) 要代替前面的一般動詞 go（他不去那所學校），要用助動詞 doesn''t，不能用 be 動詞。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-2-15', 'EN-7A-2', 'frequency', 'Here is Amy''s after-school plan:
Monday: swimming
Tuesday: piano lesson
Wednesday: swimming
Thursday: piano lesson
Friday: swimming
Saturday: piano lesson and swimming
Sunday: nothing; she stays home with her family

Which is TRUE about Amy?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "She never swims on weekends."}, {"key": "B", "text": "She always goes swimming on Sundays."}, {"key": "C", "text": "She has piano lessons four times a week."}, {"key": "D", "text": "She swims four times a week."}]'::jsonb, 'D', '游泳的日子有星期一、三、五、六，共 4 天，所以一週游泳 4 次（four times a week）。鋼琴課是星期二、四、六，共 3 次；星期六有游泳，所以週末不是從不游泳；星期天在家。', '["分別數一數游泳和鋼琴課各有幾天。", "週末指的是哪兩天？", "never 和 always 的意思分別是什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "星期六也有游泳，所以不是週末從不游泳。", "C": "鋼琴課只有星期二、四、六，一週三次。", "B": "星期天她什麼都不安排，待在家裡陪家人。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-2-16', 'EN-7A-2', 'frequency', 'Joe likes reading very much. He goes to the library on Mondays, Wednesdays, Thursdays, and Fridays. But he doesn''t like sports. He goes to the gym only once a month with his father. So Joe (1)＿＿＿ goes to the library, but he (2)＿＿＿ goes to the gym.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "always; never"}, {"key": "B", "text": "often; seldom"}, {"key": "C", "text": "never; usually"}, {"key": "D", "text": "seldom; often"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'Joe 一週有四天去圖書館，是「常常」去，用 often；健身房一個月只去一次，是「很少」去，用 seldom。always 表示每次都，never 表示從不，都和文章不符。', '["Joe 一週去幾次圖書館？一個月去幾次健身房？", "but 前後的意思相同還是相反？", "比較 always、often、seldom、never 的頻率高低。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "把兩格顛倒了：一週去四天圖書館是常常去，一個月才去一次健身房是很少去。", "A": "Joe 不是每天都去圖書館，不能用 always；一個月去一次健身房也不是 never（從不）。", "C": "Joe 一週去四次圖書館，不能說從不去；一個月一次健身房也不是「通常」。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-2-17', 'EN-7A-2', 'reading-detail', 'Hi, I''m Kenji. I live in Osaka with my parents and my grandma. My father works at a bank, and my mother teaches art at a high school. Every morning, my grandma gets up at five and takes a walk in the park. I get up at six thirty and have breakfast with my parents. On weekends, my father and I often go fishing, but my mother never goes with us. She doesn''t like fish! She usually paints at home.

Which is TRUE about Kenji''s family?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Kenji''s father is an art teacher."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Kenji''s mother often goes fishing on weekends."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Kenji''s grandma gets up before Kenji."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Kenji goes fishing with his mother on weekends."}]'::jsonb, 'C', '奶奶每天早上 5 點起床，Kenji 6 點半起床，所以奶奶比 Kenji 先起床。媽媽從不去釣魚（never goes with us）、教美術的是媽媽、和 Kenji 去釣魚的是爸爸。', '["奶奶和 Kenji 各是幾點起床？", "週末誰和 Kenji 去釣魚？媽媽做什麼？", "誰在銀行工作？誰教美術？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "文中說 my mother never goes with us，媽媽從不去釣魚。", "A": "爸爸在銀行工作，教美術的是媽媽。", "D": "週末和 Kenji 去釣魚的是爸爸，媽媽在家畫畫。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-2-18', 'EN-7A-2', 'reading-detail', 'Bus 25: City Hall to Sunny Zoo
Weekdays: every 30 minutes, from 6:00 a.m. to 9:00 p.m.
Weekends: every 20 minutes, from 7:00 a.m. to 10:00 p.m.
The trip takes 40 minutes.

It is Saturday. Amy gets to City Hall at 7:10 a.m. and takes the next Bus 25. What time does she get to Sunny Zoo?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "7:40 a.m."}, {"key": "B", "text": "8:10 a.m."}, {"key": "C", "text": "8:00 a.m."}, {"key": "D", "text": "7:50 a.m."}]'::jsonb, 'C', '星期六是週末，公車從 7:00 開始每 20 分鐘一班：7:00、7:20、7:40……。Amy 7:10 到站，下一班是 7:20。車程 40 分鐘，7:20 + 40 分鐘 = 8:00，所以她 8:00 a.m. 到動物園。', '["星期六要看平日還是週末的時刻？", "週末的公車幾點開始、多久一班？7:10 之後的下一班是幾點？", "搭上車以後還要再坐多久？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "以為 7:10 剛好有車，直接加 40 分鐘；但週末的車是 7:00、7:20……，7:10 沒有車。", "B": "用了平日每 30 分鐘一班的時刻（7:30），但今天是星期六。", "A": "只算到搭上 7:20 的車再加 20 分鐘，把車程 40 分鐘看錯了。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-2-13', 'EN-7B-2', 'past-tense', 'Every Sunday, my parents and I (1)＿＿＿ breakfast at home. Dad makes eggs, and Mom makes tea. But last Sunday was different. We (2)＿＿＿ to a new restaurant near the station, and we ate sandwiches there. The food was good, but it was a little expensive.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "have; go"}, {"key": "B", "text": "had; go"}, {"key": "C", "text": "have; went"}, {"key": "D", "text": "had; went"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '(1) Every Sunday 表示平常的習慣，用現在簡單式；主詞 my parents and I 是複數，用 have。(2) But last Sunday was different. 說明上星期天和平常不同，是過去的事，go 的過去式是 went；後面的 ate 也是過去式。', '["(1) 和 (2) 各有什麼時間詞？", "Every Sunday 說的是習慣還是過去某一天？", "go 的過去式是什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "(1) 有 Every Sunday，說的是每週的習慣，要用現在簡單式，後一句 Dad makes eggs 也是現在式。", "A": "(2) 有 last Sunday，是過去發生的事，要用過去式 went。", "B": "兩格的時態都弄反了：習慣用現在式，上星期天的事用過去式。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-2-14', 'EN-7B-2', 'past-tense', 'Lily: (1)＿＿＿ you at Mark''s birthday party last night? I didn''t see you there.
Joe: No. I (2)＿＿＿ go. I had a fever, so I stayed in bed all night.
Lily: Oh, I''m sorry to hear that. Are you OK now?
Joe: Yes, I''m fine today. Thanks.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Did; didn''t"}, {"key": "B", "text": "Was; didn''t"}, {"key": "C", "text": "Were; wasn''t"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Were; didn''t"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '(1) Were you at the party? 問「你昨晚在不在派對上」，句中沒有一般動詞，用 be 動詞；last night 是過去，主詞 you 用 Were。(2) 空格後面是原形動詞 go，一般動詞的過去式否定是 didn''t + 原形：I didn''t go.', '["(1) 句子裡有一般動詞嗎？「在某地」要用哪一種動詞？", "you 的 be 動詞過去式是什麼？", "(2) 空格後面的 go 是什麼動詞？否定要借什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "(1) 句中沒有一般動詞（at the party 是「在」派對），要用 be 動詞發問。", "C": "(2) 後面接的是一般動詞 go，否定要用 didn''t，不能用 be 動詞。", "B": "主詞 you 的 be 動詞過去式是 were，不是 was。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-2-15', 'EN-7B-2', 'irregular-verb', 'Yesterday morning, Jack (1)＿＿＿ his bike to school as usual. On the way, a dog suddenly ran into the street, and Jack (2)＿＿＿ off his bike. He hurt his leg, so his teacher took him to the nurse''s office. Luckily, it wasn''t serious.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "rode; fell"}, {"key": "B", "text": "rode; falled"}, {"key": "C", "text": "rided; fell"}, {"key": "D", "text": "rides; falls"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Yesterday morning 是過去時間，兩格都要用過去式。ride（騎）是不規則動詞，過去式是 rode；fall（跌落）也是不規則動詞，過去式是 fell，fall off one''s bike 是「從腳踏車上摔下來」。', '["文章第一個時間詞是什麼？", "ride 和 fall 是規則動詞還是不規則動詞？", "它們的過去式分別怎麼寫？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "ride 是不規則動詞，過去式是 rode，不是加 d。", "B": "fall 是不規則動詞，過去式是 fell，不是加 ed。", "D": "Yesterday morning 是過去時間，要用過去式，文中的 ran、hurt、took 也都是過去式。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-2-16', 'EN-7B-2', 'irregular-verb', 'Read Tom''s diary.
Monday, June 3
This morning I woke up late. I ran to the bus stop, but I didn''t catch the bus. So Mom drived me to school. At lunch, I bought a sandwich and ate it with my friends. In the afternoon, I felt tired, but I was happy because we won the basketball game.

Which verb in the diary is NOT correct?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "woke"}, {"key": "B", "text": "bought"}, {"key": "C", "text": "felt"}, {"key": "D", "text": "drived"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'drive（開車）是不規則動詞，過去式是 drove，不能加 d 寫成 drived。woke（wake）、bought（buy）、felt（feel）都是正確的不規則動詞過去式。另外 didn''t catch 的 catch 在 didn''t 後面用原形，也是正確的。', '["日記寫的是過去的事，每個動詞都應該是過去式。", "逐一想出每個選項的原形動詞。", "drive、wake、buy、feel 哪一個的過去式不是這樣寫？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "wake 的過去式就是 woke，是正確的。", "B": "buy 的過去式就是 bought，是正確的。", "C": "feel 的過去式就是 felt，是正確的。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-2-17', 'EN-7B-2', 'reading-detail', 'Last Saturday was a busy day for Mia. After lunch, she went to the bookstore and bought a birthday card for her friend Rose. Before that, she cleaned her room and washed her clothes in the morning. In the evening, she went to Rose''s birthday party and gave her the card. Rose loved it.

What is the right order of the things Mia did?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "bought a card → cleaned her room → went to a party"}, {"key": "B", "text": "cleaned her room → went to a party → bought a card"}, {"key": "C", "text": "went to a party → bought a card → cleaned her room"}, {"key": "D", "text": "cleaned her room → bought a card → went to a party"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '文中的時間線索：in the morning 打掃房間、洗衣服；After lunch 去書店買卡片；In the evening 去派對。Before that 指「在買卡片之前」，所以順序是：打掃房間 → 買卡片 → 去派對。', '["文章的敘述順序就是事情發生的順序嗎？", "Before that 的 that 指的是哪件事？", "把 in the morning、after lunch、in the evening 對應的事情排好。"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "照文章出現的先後排列，沒注意 Before that（在那之前）表示打掃是更早的事。", "C": "把整個順序顛倒了；派對是在晚上。", "B": "卡片是在派對上送給 Rose 的，一定是先買卡片再去派對。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-2-18', 'EN-7B-2', 'reading-detail', 'Ben: How was your trip to Hualien, Amy?
Amy: Not so good. It rained for the first three days, so we stayed in the hotel most of the time.
Ben: Oh, no! Did you go to Taroko?
Amy: Yes, but only on the last day. The sun finally came out that day, and we took a lot of pictures there.
Ben: Well, at least you saw Taroko.

Which is TRUE about Amy''s trip?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "She didn''t take any pictures in Hualien."}, {"key": "B", "text": "It rained every day during the trip."}, {"key": "C", "text": "She enjoyed every day of the trip."}, {"key": "D", "text": "She visited Taroko when the weather was good."}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Amy 說只有最後一天去了太魯閣，而且 The sun finally came out that day（那天終於出太陽），所以她是在天氣好的時候去太魯閣。前三天下雨，所以不是每天都下雨，她也不是每天都玩得開心。', '["Amy 覺得這趟旅行怎麼樣？", "雨下了幾天？最後一天天氣如何？", "她哪一天去太魯閣？那天她做了什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "Amy 一開始就說 Not so good，前三天下雨只能待在飯店。", "B": "只有前三天下雨，最後一天出太陽了。", "A": "她說在太魯閣 took a lot of pictures（拍了很多照片）。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-1-13', 'EN-8A-1', 'future-tense', 'Dad: Look at the sky! It''s so dark.
Amy: Yes, and the wind is getting strong. It (1)＿＿＿ rain soon.
Dad: Then we (2)＿＿＿ take our umbrellas with us. I don''t want to get wet.
Amy: OK. I''ll get them. They''re next to the door.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "is going; should"}, {"key": "B", "text": "goes to; should"}, {"key": "C", "text": "is going to; shouldn''t"}, {"key": "D", "text": "is going to; should"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '(1) 天色很暗、風變大，根據眼前跡象判斷「快要下雨」，用 be going to + 原形：It is going to rain soon.。(2) 爸爸不想淋濕，所以建議「應該帶傘」，給建議用 should + 原形。', '["(1) 說話者根據什麼判斷天氣？soon 表示什麼時候？", "be going to 的三個部分是什麼？", "爸爸說不想淋濕，他會建議帶傘還是不帶？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "be going to 表示未來時三個部分缺一不可，少了 to。", "C": "爸爸說不想淋濕，「不應該帶傘」前後矛盾。", "B": "goes to 是「去到某地」，不能表示「即將下雨」。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-1-14', 'EN-8A-1', 'future-tense', 'Ken: Are you free tomorrow, Rose? Let''s go to the movies.
Rose: Sorry, I can''t. I (1)＿＿＿ my grandparents in Tainan tomorrow. I (2)＿＿＿ the train ticket last week.
Ken: That''s OK. Have a good time there!
Rose: Thanks. Maybe we can go next weekend.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "visited; bought"}, {"key": "B", "text": "am going to visit; bought"}, {"key": "C", "text": "going to visit; bought"}, {"key": "D", "text": "am going to visit; will buy"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '(1) tomorrow 是未來，而且是已經計畫好的事，用 be going to + 原形：I am going to visit。(2) last week 是過去，車票上週已經買了，用過去式 bought（buy 的過去式）。', '["(1) 和 (2) 的時間詞分別是什麼？", "明天要做的事用什麼時態？上週做的事呢？", "be going to 需要哪三個部分？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "(1) 有 tomorrow，是未來的事，不能用過去式。", "D": "(2) 有 last week，車票是上週已經買好的，要用過去式。", "C": "be going to 少了 be 動詞 am。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-1-15', 'EN-8A-1', 'modal-verb', 'Swimming Pool Rules
- You must take a shower before you swim.
- You must wear a swimming cap.
- Children under 10 must swim with an adult.
- You don''t have to bring a towel. We have towels for you.
- You can''t eat in the pool area.

Ted is 12 years old. He wants to swim here. What must he do?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Eat his lunch in the pool area"}, {"key": "B", "text": "Take a shower before swimming"}, {"key": "C", "text": "Bring his own towel"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Swim with his father"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '規則第一條 You must take a shower before you swim.，所有人游泳前都必須淋浴。毛巾是 don''t have to（不必）帶；和大人一起游只限 10 歲以下；泳池區 can''t（不可以）吃東西。', '["題目問的是 Ted「必須」做的事，要找 must 的規則。", "Ted 12 歲，哪一條 must 的規則不適用於他？", "don''t have to 和 can''t 分別是什麼意思？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "規則說 You don''t have to bring a towel，是「不必」帶，游泳池有提供。", "D": "只有 10 歲以下的小孩必須和大人一起游，Ted 已經 12 歲。", "A": "規則說 You can''t eat in the pool area，是禁止的事。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-1-16', 'EN-8A-1', 'modal-verb', 'Visitor: Excuse me. Is the museum still open?
Clerk: Yes, it is. You can look at the paintings, but you (1)＿＿＿ touch them. They are very old.
Visitor: I see. How much is a ticket for my son? He''s five.
Clerk: Oh, you (2)＿＿＿ buy a ticket for him. Children under six get in free.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "mustn''t; must"}, {"key": "B", "text": "must; have to"}, {"key": "C", "text": "don''t have to; mustn''t"}, {"key": "D", "text": "mustn''t; don''t have to"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '(1) 畫作很古老，可以看但「不可以」摸，表示禁止用 mustn''t。(2) Children under six get in free.（六歲以下免費），兒子五歲，所以「不必」買票，用 don''t have to。注意 mustn''t 是禁止，don''t have to 是不必。', '["(1) 畫很古老，參觀者可以摸嗎？", "(2) 兒子幾歲？幾歲以下可以免費入場？", "「禁止」和「不必」在英文裡分別怎麼說？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "把兩格弄反了：古畫「禁止」觸摸用 mustn''t；小孩免費是「不必」買票，用 don''t have to。", "B": "畫很古老，「必須摸」不合理；小孩免費也不需要買票。", "A": "店員說六歲以下免費入場，「必須買票」前後矛盾。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-1-17', 'EN-8A-1', 'reading-detail', 'Hi Jason,
Next Saturday is Grandpa''s 70th birthday. We''re going to have a party at his house. Mom will make a big cake, and Dad will cook Grandpa''s favorite fish. Can you come at 5:00 and help me put up the balloons? The party will start at 6:30. Don''t tell Grandpa about it! It''s a surprise.
Kelly

Which is TRUE?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Kelly wants Jason to come before the party starts."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Grandpa knows about the party."}, {"key": "C", "text": "The party will be at Kelly''s house."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Kelly''s dad will make the birthday cake."}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Kelly 請 Jason 5:00 來幫忙掛氣球，而派對 6:30 才開始，所以她希望 Jason 在派對開始前就到。爺爺不知道派對（這是驚喜）、蛋糕由媽媽做、派對在爺爺家。', '["Kelly 請 Jason 幾點來？派對幾點開始？", "at his house 的 his 指誰？", "誰做蛋糕？誰煮魚？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "Kelly 說 Don''t tell Grandpa... It''s a surprise.，這是給爺爺的驚喜，爺爺不知道。", "D": "做蛋糕的是媽媽，爸爸負責煮魚。", "C": "派對在爺爺家（at his house）舉行。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-1-18', 'EN-8A-1', 'reading-detail', 'Weather report for this weekend:
Saturday: sunny and hot, 32°C
Sunday: heavy rain all day, 21°C

Tina: Let''s go to the beach this weekend!
Ray: Good idea. But we should go on the sunny day.
Tina: Right. It will be very hot, so we must bring something for our heads.

When will they probably go to the beach, and what will they bring?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "On Saturday, with hats"}, {"key": "B", "text": "On Sunday, with umbrellas"}, {"key": "C", "text": "On Sunday, with hats"}, {"key": "D", "text": "On Saturday, with jackets"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Ray 說 we should go on the sunny day，氣象報告中晴天是星期六；Tina 說天氣會很熱，must bring something for our heads（必須帶戴在頭上的東西），最合理的是帽子。所以他們會在星期六帶帽子去海邊。', '["哪一天是晴天？", "Tina 說要帶「給頭用的東西」，是哪一種物品？", "天氣 32°C 時需要外套嗎？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "星期天整天大雨，Ray 說要在晴天去。", "D": "星期六 32°C 很熱，不需要外套，而且 Tina 說要帶的是戴在頭上的東西。", "C": "星期天下大雨，不是晴天。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-1-13', 'EN-8B-1', 'gerund', 'Amy had a lot of homework last night. She started her science report at seven. She finished (1)＿＿＿ it at ten, and she felt very tired. Then she decided (2)＿＿＿ a short walk in the park near her home before going to bed.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "writing; taking"}, {"key": "B", "text": "to write; to take"}, {"key": "C", "text": "writing; to take"}, {"key": "D", "text": "to write; taking"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '(1) finish（完成）後面接動名詞：finished writing it。(2) decide（決定）後面接不定詞：decided to take a short walk。句末的 before going to bed 也是介系詞 before 後面接 V-ing。', '["finish 後面的動詞要用什麼形式？", "decide 和 want、hope 是同一類動詞嗎？", "這兩個動詞一個接 V-ing，一個接 to V。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "把兩個動詞的用法弄反了：finish 接 V-ing，decide 接 to V。", "A": "decide 後面要接不定詞 to V，不接 V-ing。", "B": "finish 後面要接動名詞 V-ing，不接不定詞。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-1-14', 'EN-8B-1', 'gerund', 'Do you want to learn new English words? Here''s a fun way. (1)＿＿＿ English songs is a good way to learn new words. My brother is good at (2)＿＿＿ them, and he learns five or six new words from every song. He also enjoys watching English cartoons.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Singing; to sing"}, {"key": "B", "text": "Singing; singing"}, {"key": "C", "text": "Sing; sing"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Sings; singing"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '(1) 空格在句首，是句子的主詞（動詞是 is），動詞當主詞要改成動名詞 Singing。(2) be good at（擅長）的 at 是介系詞，介系詞後面接動名詞：good at singing them。', '["(1) 這句話的主要動詞是什麼？空格是在當主詞嗎？", "(2) 空格前面的 at 是什麼詞性？", "動詞要當主詞或放在介系詞後面時，要怎麼改？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "原形動詞不能當主詞；介系詞 at 後面也不能接原形動詞。", "A": "be good at 的 at 是介系詞，後面要接 V-ing，不接 to V。", "D": "Sings 是動詞，不能當句子的主詞。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-1-15', 'EN-8B-1', 'infinitive', 'Mia: Can you help me with this math problem? It''s too hard for me.
Dan: Sure. Let me see... Oh, it''s not difficult (1)＿＿＿ this problem. I can teach you (2)＿＿＿ do it.
Mia: Thank you! You''re so good at math. I hope to be like you someday.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "to solve; how to"}, {"key": "B", "text": "to solve; what to"}, {"key": "C", "text": "solving; how"}, {"key": "D", "text": "solve; how to"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '(1) It''s + 形容詞 + to + 原形動詞 表示「做某事是……的」，It 是虛主詞，真正的主詞是 to solve this problem。(2) teach someone how to + 原形 表示「教某人如何做」，how to do it 就是「怎麼做這題」。', '["(1) 句子 it''s not difficult ＿ this problem 中，It 代替的是什麼？", "(2)「教你怎麼做」要用哪個疑問詞 + 不定詞？", "what to do 和 how to do 後面可以再接 it 嗎？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "teach you how 後面直接接原形 do 不合文法，要用 how to + 原形。", "B": "what to do 已經有 do 的受詞 what，後面再加 it 就重複了。", "D": "It''s + 形容詞 + to V 的句型，不能省略 to。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-1-16', 'EN-8B-1', 'infinitive', 'Kevin was late for school three times last week. This morning, he was late again. His teacher, Ms. Lin, was not happy. She told him (1)＿＿＿ late again, and she wants everyone in the class (2)＿＿＿ at school before 7:30 every day.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "to not being; arriving"}, {"key": "B", "text": "not to be; to arrive"}, {"key": "C", "text": "not being; to arrive"}, {"key": "D", "text": "don''t be; arrive"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '(1) tell + 人 + to V 表示「叫某人做某事」，否定是 tell + 人 + not to V，所以是 told him not to be late again。(2) want + 人 + to V 表示「要某人做某事」，所以是 wants everyone to arrive。', '["tell someone 和 want someone 後面的動詞要用什麼形式？", "不定詞的否定，not 要放在 to 的前面還是後面？", "(1) 老師是叫 Kevin 做什麼還是不要做什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "tell someone 後面接不定詞 to + 原形，不能接 being；want someone 後面也要接 to V。", "D": "tell someone 後面不能直接接祈使句 don''t be；want someone 後面要加 to。", "C": "tell someone 後面要接不定詞，否定是 not to + 原形，不是 not being。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-1-17', 'EN-8B-1', 'reading-main-idea', 'Many students spend hours playing computer games every day. Some parents think playing games is a waste of time, but games are not always bad. Some games teach players to work with others, and some help them practice thinking fast. The real problem is not playing games, but playing too long. Students should learn to stop after an hour and save time for homework, sports, and sleep.

What is the writer''s main point?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Students should never play computer games."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Playing games is OK if students don''t play too long."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Students should stop doing homework to play games."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Parents should play games with their children."}]'::jsonb, 'B', '作者先說遊戲不一定是壞事，並舉例：可以學習合作、練習快速思考；接著點出重點 The real problem is not playing games, but playing too long.（真正的問題不是玩遊戲，而是玩太久），最後建議玩一小時就要停下來。所以主旨是：只要不玩太久，玩遊戲是可以的。', '["作者對玩電腦遊戲的態度是完全反對嗎？", "找出 The real problem is not..., but... 這一句。", "最後一句的建議和哪個選項的意思最接近？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "作者說 games are not always bad，還舉出遊戲的好處，並不反對玩遊戲。", "D": "文中沒有提到父母要陪孩子玩遊戲。", "C": "作者剛好相反，要學生留時間給功課、運動和睡眠。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-1-18', 'EN-8B-1', 'reading-main-idea', 'Dear neighbors,
Do you have books that you don''t read anymore? Please don''t throw them away! Bring them to the community center before May 20. We are planning to send them to children in the mountains. We also need some people to help pack the books on May 21. If you''d like to help, please call Ms. Lee at 2345-6789.

What is the purpose of this letter?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "To sell old books at the community center"}, {"key": "B", "text": "To invite children to a party in the mountains"}, {"key": "C", "text": "To tell people where to buy new books"}, {"key": "D", "text": "To ask people to give old books and help pack them"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '信一開頭問大家有沒有不再讀的書，請大家不要丟掉，在 5 月 20 日前送到社區中心，要送給山區的孩子；還徵求 5 月 21 日幫忙打包的人。所以寫信的目的是請鄰居捐出舊書並幫忙打包。', '["這封信是寫給誰的？請他們做哪些事？", "書最後要送去哪裡？", "Ms. Lee 的電話是給什麼人打的？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "信中是請大家「捐」書給山區的孩子，不是要賣書。", "B": "書是要送給山區的孩子，信中沒有提到派對。", "C": "信中談的是不再讀的舊書，不是買新書。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-2-13', 'EN-8A-2', 'comparative', 'Ted wants to buy a new phone. Here are three phones in the store:
Phone A: NT$8,000, 150 grams
Phone B: NT$12,000, 180 grams
Phone C: NT$10,000, 130 grams
Ted doesn''t have much money, but he also wants a light phone.

Which is TRUE about the three phones?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Phone B is cheaper than Phone C."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Phone A is heavier than Phone C."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Phone A is lighter than Phone C."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Phone C is the most expensive."}]'::jsonb, 'B', '比較重量：Phone A 150 公克，Phone C 130 公克，150 > 130，所以 Phone A 比 Phone C 重（heavier）。價格由高到低是 B（12,000）> C（10,000）> A（8,000），所以 B 不比 C 便宜，C 也不是最貴的。', '["先把三支手機的價格和重量分別排順序。", "公克數越大表示越重還是越輕？", "cheaper、heavier、lighter、the most expensive 分別是什麼意思？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "Phone B 要 NT$12,000，比 Phone C 的 NT$10,000 貴。", "D": "最貴的是 Phone B（NT$12,000），Phone C 排第二。", "C": "Phone A 150 公克，Phone C 130 公克，A 比較重，把輕重弄反了。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-2-14', 'EN-8A-2', 'comparative', 'Kevin and I walk to school together every day. Kevin''s bag is heavy, but my bag is even (1)＿＿＿. There are five books in my bag, and there are only three in his. So my bag is (2)＿＿＿ of the two. I think I should take some books out.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "heaviest; the heavier"}, {"key": "B", "text": "heavier; the heavier"}, {"key": "C", "text": "more heavy; the heaviest"}, {"key": "D", "text": "heavier; heavier"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '(1) even 用來加強比較級，表示「甚至更……」，heavy 字尾是「子音 + y」，比較級是 heavier。(2) of the two 是在兩者之中比較，要用 the + 比較級：the heavier of the two（兩個之中較重的）。', '["even 後面要接原級、比較級還是最高級？", "heavy 字尾是 y，變比較級時怎麼改？", "of the two 是幾個東西在比較？前面要不要加 the？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "heavy 的比較級是 heavier，不是 more heavy；而且只有兩個書包。", "D": "「兩者之中較……的那一個」要用 the + 比較級，不能少了 the。", "A": "even（更加）要修飾比較級，不能接最高級。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-2-15', 'EN-8A-2', 'superlative', 'Four students are in a class photo. Cathy is the tallest of the four, and she is 170 cm. Amy is the shortest; she is 150 cm. Dan is 162 cm. Ben is taller than Dan, but he isn''t as tall as Cathy.

How tall could Ben be?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "168 cm"}, {"key": "B", "text": "160 cm"}, {"key": "C", "text": "172 cm"}, {"key": "D", "text": "148 cm"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Ben is taller than Dan，所以 Ben 超過 162 公分；he isn''t as tall as Cathy，而且 Cathy 是 the tallest of the four，所以 Ben 不到 170 公分。只有 168 公分在 162 和 170 之間。', '["Ben 和 Dan 比，誰比較高？", "isn''t as tall as Cathy 是什麼意思？", "Ben 的身高要在哪兩個數字之間？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "160 公分比 Dan 的 162 公分矮，但文中說 Ben 比 Dan 高。", "C": "172 公分比 Cathy 還高，但 Cathy 是四個人中最高的。", "D": "148 公分比 Amy 還矮，但 Amy 是四個人中最矮的。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-2-16', 'EN-8A-2', 'superlative', 'Ann: What''s your favorite season, Joe?
Joe: Of all the seasons, I like summer (1)＿＿＿ because I love swimming in the sea.
Ann: My sister is different. She likes winter (2)＿＿＿ than summer because she hates hot weather.
Joe: Really? I think winter is too cold!

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "best; better"}, {"key": "B", "text": "better; best"}, {"key": "C", "text": "best; best"}, {"key": "D", "text": "good; better"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'like 的程度用副詞 well 表示，比較級是 better，最高級是 best。(1) Of all the seasons（在所有季節中）是三者以上的比較，用最高級：like summer best。(2) 後面有 than summer，是兩者比較，用比較級：likes winter better than summer。', '["(1) Of all the seasons 是在幾個季節裡比較？", "(2) 空格後面出現了哪個字？", "「最喜歡」和「比較喜歡」英文分別怎麼說？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "把兩格弄反了：Of all the seasons 是在所有季節中比較，用最高級；有 than 才用比較級。", "D": "Of all the seasons 要用最高級；而且 good 是形容詞，不能修飾動詞 like。", "C": "(2) 後面有 than，要用比較級 better。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-2-17', 'EN-8A-2', 'as-as', 'Last week, Mr. Lin gave his class a math test. Tom got 85 points. Mia got the same score as Tom. Joe got 5 points more than Mia, and he was very happy about it. Mr. Lin said all three of them did a good job.

Which is TRUE?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Mia''s score was as high as Tom''s."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Tom''s score was not as high as Mia''s."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Mia''s score was higher than Joe''s."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Joe''s score was as high as Mia''s."}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Tom 85 分，Mia got the same score as Tom，也是 85 分；Joe 比 Mia 多 5 分，是 90 分。兩人分數相同用 as + 原級 + as，所以 Mia''s score was as high as Tom''s. 正確。', '["先算出三個人各考幾分。", "the same score as 是什麼意思？", "as high as 和 not as high as 分別表示什麼關係？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "Mia 和 Tom 分數相同，不能說 Tom 沒有 Mia 高。", "D": "Joe 比 Mia 多 5 分，兩人分數不一樣。", "C": "Joe 比 Mia 多 5 分，是 Joe 的分數比較高。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-2-18', 'EN-8A-2', 'as-as', 'Last month, my family moved to a new house. The new house is not as big as our old one, and it doesn''t have a garden. But I like it more because it is closer to my school. Now I can walk to school in five minutes. Before, I took the bus for thirty minutes every day.

Which is TRUE about the new house?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "It is as far from school as the old house."}, {"key": "B", "text": "It is smaller than the old house."}, {"key": "C", "text": "It has a bigger garden than the old house."}, {"key": "D", "text": "It is bigger than the old house."}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'The new house is not as big as our old one. 表示新房子沒有舊房子大，也就是新房子比較小（smaller）。新家比較靠近學校，而且沒有花園。', '["not as big as 是「一樣大」還是「沒那麼大」？", "新家離學校近還是遠？", "新房子有花園嗎？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "not as big as 是「沒有那麼大」，新房子比較小。", "A": "新家比較靠近學校，走路五分鐘；以前要搭三十分鐘公車。", "C": "文中說新房子 doesn''t have a garden（沒有花園）。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-2-13', 'EN-8B-2', 'conjunction', 'Sam saw a pair of cool shoes in a store last month. He wanted to buy them, (1)＿＿＿ he didn''t have enough money. (2)＿＿＿ he saved his pocket money for two months, he finally bought them last Sunday. Now he wears them every day.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "or; Before"}, {"key": "B", "text": "but; Although"}, {"key": "C", "text": "so; After"}, {"key": "D", "text": "but; After"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '(1) 想買鞋子，但是錢不夠，前後語意相反，用 but。(2) 存了兩個月的零用錢「之後」，終於買到鞋子，表示事情的先後順序，用 After；finally（終於）也提示存錢在先、買鞋在後。', '["(1) 「想買」和「錢不夠」是什麼關係？", "(2) 存錢和買到鞋子，哪件事先發生？", "finally 這個字給了你什麼線索？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "so 表示結果，「想買所以錢不夠」不合理；想買和錢不夠是轉折關係。", "B": "存了兩個月的錢，終於買到鞋子，是順理成章的事，不是相反關係。", "A": "or 表示「或者」不合句意；而且「存錢之前就終於買到」不合理。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-2-14', 'EN-8B-2', 'conjunction', 'Mom: What are we going to do this weekend?
Dad: Let''s go hiking on Sunday morning. But the weather report says it may rain.
Mom: Then here''s our plan. If it (1)＿＿＿ on Sunday, we (2)＿＿＿ at home and watch movies.
Kids: Great! We love movies.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "will rain; will stay"}, {"key": "B", "text": "rains; will stay"}, {"key": "C", "text": "rained; will stay"}, {"key": "D", "text": "rains; stayed"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '這是對星期天的假設計畫。if 引導的條件子句用現在簡單式表示未來：If it rains on Sunday；主要子句用未來式：we will stay at home。主詞 it 是第三人稱單數，所以 rain 要加 s。', '["這個計畫是過去還是未來的事？", "if 子句裡可以用 will 嗎？", "主要子句要用什麼時態表示未來？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "if 引導的條件子句要用現在式表示未來，不能用 will rain。", "C": "星期天是未來的事，條件子句不能用過去式 rained。", "D": "主要子句說的是未來的計畫，要用 will stay，不能用過去式。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-2-15', 'EN-8B-2', 'tag-question', 'Ella: Your brother can speak Japanese, (1)＿＿＿?
Ken: (2)＿＿＿ He only speaks Chinese and English. But he wants to learn Japanese next year.
Ella: Oh, I see. My aunt teaches Japanese. Maybe she can help him.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "doesn''t he; No, he doesn''t."}, {"key": "B", "text": "can he; No, he can''t."}, {"key": "C", "text": "can''t he; No, he can''t."}, {"key": "D", "text": "can''t he; Yes, he can."}]'::jsonb, 'C', '(1) 前句是肯定句，用助動詞 can，附加問句用否定的 can''t，主詞 Your brother 換成 he：can''t he。(2) Ken 說 He only speaks Chinese and English.（只會說中文和英文），所以哥哥不會日文，要回答 No, he can''t.。', '["(1) 前句用的是哪個助動詞？是肯定還是否定？", "Ken 的哥哥會說哪些語言？", "回答附加問句時，只看事實決定用 Yes 還是 No。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "附加問句要「前肯後否」，前句是肯定的 can speak，附加問句要用否定 can''t he。", "D": "Ken 說哥哥只會說中文和英文，所以他不會日文，不能回答 Yes。", "A": "前句用助動詞 can，附加問句和回答都要用 can，不能改用 does。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-2-16', 'EN-8B-2', 'tag-question', 'Amy: Mr. and Mrs. Chen live next to you, (1)＿＿＿?
Ben: (2)＿＿＿ They moved to Taichung last month. A new family lives there now.
Amy: Oh, I didn''t know that. I wanted to give this book back to Mrs. Chen.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "aren''t they; No, they aren''t."}, {"key": "B", "text": "don''t they; No, they don''t."}, {"key": "C", "text": "doesn''t he; No, he doesn''t."}, {"key": "D", "text": "don''t they; Yes, they do."}]'::jsonb, 'B', '(1) 前句是肯定的現在簡單式，動詞 live 是一般動詞，主詞 Mr. and Mrs. Chen 是複數，附加問句用 don''t they。(2) 他們上個月搬到台中，現在住在隔壁的是新的一家人，所以事實是「沒有住在隔壁」，回答 No, they don''t.。', '["(1) 前句的動詞是 be 動詞還是一般動詞？主詞有幾個人？", "陳先生夫婦現在還住在 Ben 隔壁嗎？", "事實是否定時，回答要用 Yes 還是 No？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "前句的動詞 live 是一般動詞，附加問句要用助動詞 don''t，不能用 be 動詞。", "D": "陳先生夫婦上個月已經搬到台中，現在不住在 Ben 隔壁，不能回答 Yes。", "C": "主詞 Mr. and Mrs. Chen 是兩個人，要用 they 和 don''t。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-2-17', 'EN-8B-2', 'reading-detail', 'Ryan and his twin brother, Sean, look the same, but they have very different habits. Ryan gets up early, while Sean always stays up late and gets up at the last minute. Ryan walks to school because he likes exercise. Sean takes the bus, so he can sleep a little longer. However, they both enjoy cooking, and they often make dinner together when their parents work late.

Which is TRUE?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Sean walks to school to get exercise."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Ryan gets up later than Sean."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Sean takes the bus because he doesn''t like walking."}, {"key": "D", "text": "The twins both like cooking."}]'::jsonb, 'D', '前面用 but、while 說明兄弟倆習慣不同，接著用 However 轉折：they both enjoy cooking（他們都喜歡做菜），還常常一起煮晚餐。所以「雙胞胎都喜歡做菜」正確。', '["文中哪一個連接詞把「不同」轉到「相同」？", "Ryan 和 Sean 誰早起？誰走路上學？", "Sean 搭公車的原因，文中用哪個連接詞說明？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "走路上學、喜歡運動的是 Ryan，Sean 搭公車。", "B": "Ryan 早起，Sean 總是最後一刻才起床，是 Sean 起得比較晚。", "C": "Sean 搭公車是為了可以多睡一點（so he can sleep a little longer），文中沒說他不喜歡走路。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-2-18', 'EN-8B-2', 'reading-detail', 'Sports Day Notice
- Sports Day is on Friday, October 20. If it rains that day, it will be moved to the next Monday.
- Students must wear sports clothes, or they can''t join the games.
- Lunch is free for students, but parents need to pay NT$100 for lunch.
- Please arrive before 7:40 because the opening starts at 8:00.

Kevin''s mom wants to have lunch with Kevin on Sports Day. On Friday, October 20, it rains hard all day. What should she do?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Come on Monday and pay NT$100 for lunch"}, {"key": "B", "text": "Come on Friday and pay nothing for lunch"}, {"key": "C", "text": "Come on Friday and pay NT$100 for lunch"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Come on Monday and pay nothing for lunch"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '通知第一條：If it rains that day, it will be moved to the next Monday.，星期五下大雨，運動會改到下星期一。第三條：Lunch is free for students, but parents need to pay NT$100.，媽媽是家長，要付 100 元。所以她應該星期一來，並付 100 元午餐費。', '["星期五下雨的話，運動會會怎麼樣？", "午餐對學生和家長的規定有什麼不同？", "這題要同時用到通知中的兩條規定。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "星期五下雨，運動會會延到下星期一；而且只有學生免費，家長要付錢。", "D": "日子對了，但通知說 parents need to pay NT$100，家長的午餐要付 100 元。", "C": "星期五下大雨，運動會改到下星期一，星期五不會舉行。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-1-13', 'EN-9A-1', 'present-perfect', 'Judy: Your photos are beautiful! (1)＿＿＿ to Japan?
Leo: Yes. I (2)＿＿＿ there with my family two years ago. We visited Tokyo and Kyoto.
Judy: Lucky you! I''ve never been there. I hope to go someday.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Have you ever went; went"}, {"key": "B", "text": "Have you ever been; have been"}, {"key": "C", "text": "Did you ever been; went"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Have you ever been; went"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '(1) 問對方「曾經去過」日本嗎，用現在完成式 Have you ever been to...?。(2) two years ago 是明確的過去時間，要用過去簡單式 went；現在完成式不能和 ago、last year 這類明確的過去時間連用。', '["(1) Judy 想問的是「曾經」去過嗎？要用什麼時態？", "(2) 的句子裡有什麼時間詞？", "現在完成式可以和 two years ago 一起用嗎？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "(2) 有 two years ago，是明確的過去時間，不能用現在完成式。", "C": "Did 後面要接原形動詞，不能接過去分詞 been。", "A": "have 後面要接過去分詞 been 或 gone，went 是過去式。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-1-14', 'EN-9A-1', 'present-perfect', 'Mom: Is your sister home, Tom?
Tom: No, she (1)＿＿＿ to the supermarket. She''ll be back in ten minutes.
Mom: OK. Have you finished your homework (2)＿＿＿?
Tom: Not yet. I''m still working on my English report.
Mom: Please finish it before dinner.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "has gone; ago"}, {"key": "B", "text": "has been; yet"}, {"key": "C", "text": "has been; since"}, {"key": "D", "text": "has gone; yet"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '(1) 姊姊（妹妹）不在家，十分鐘後才回來，表示她「已經去了超市、人還在那裡」，用 has gone to。(2) 現在完成式的疑問句問「已經……了嗎」，句尾用 yet；Tom 回答 Not yet 也可以印證。', '["(1) 姊姊（妹妹）現在在家嗎？", "have gone to 和 have been to 的差別是什麼？", "Tom 回答 Not yet，問句句尾應該用哪個字？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "has been to 表示「曾經去過、已經回來」，但姊姊（妹妹）現在不在家。", "A": "ago 要接在一段時間後面，而且不能用在現在完成式的問句裡。", "C": "since 後面要接時間起點；而且 has been to 不合「人還沒回來」的情境。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-1-15', 'EN-9A-1', 'since-for', 'My parents bought their car in 2018, and they still drive it today. The car is old, but it still runs well. Dad washes it every weekend, and Mom says it''s like a member of our family. It''s 2026 now, so my parents (1)＿＿＿ the car (2)＿＿＿.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "have had; since eight years"}, {"key": "B", "text": "have had; for eight years"}, {"key": "C", "text": "had; since 2018"}, {"key": "D", "text": "have bought; for eight years"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '車子 2018 年買的，到 2026 年仍在使用，表示「從過去持續到現在」，用現在完成式。買（buy）是瞬間動作不能持續，要用表示擁有的 have，過去分詞是 had：have had。2018 到 2026 年是一段時間八年，用 for eight years（也可以說 since 2018，但要搭配 have had）。', '["從 2018 年到 2026 年，一共是幾年？", "「買」這個動作可以持續八年嗎？哪個動詞表示「擁有」？", "for 和 since 後面分別接什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "buy 是一瞬間就完成的動作，不能持續八年；要表示「擁有」八年，用 have had。", "A": "since 後面要接時間起點（例如 since 2018），eight years 是一段時間，要用 for。", "C": "since 表示「從那時到現在」，要搭配現在完成式，不能用過去式 had。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-1-16', 'EN-9A-1', 'since-for', 'Mr. Wu came to Tainan in 2010. At first, he worked in a bookstore for four years. Then he became a teacher, and he has taught at Sunny Junior High School since then. He loves his job, and his students love him, too.

It is 2026 now. How long has Mr. Wu taught at Sunny Junior High School?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "For sixteen years"}, {"key": "B", "text": "For four years"}, {"key": "C", "text": "For twelve years"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Since 2010"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '吳老師 2010 年到台南，先在書店工作四年，所以 2014 年才開始在 Sunny 國中教書（since then 指書店工作結束之後）。2014 年到 2026 年是 12 年，所以他已經教了十二年（for twelve years）。', '["吳老師來台南後先做什麼工作？做了幾年？", "since then 的 then 指的是哪一年？", "從那一年到 2026 年是幾年？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "從 2010 年算起，但他前四年在書店工作，不是在學校教書。", "B": "四年是他在書店工作的時間。", "D": "2010 年是他來台南的年份，那時他還在書店工作，不是開始教書的時間。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-1-17', 'EN-9A-1', 'reading-detail', 'Dear Grandma,
We have lived in our new apartment for a month now. I like it here. I have already made two new friends, Lisa and Joy. They live on the fifth floor. I have also joined the school band, but I haven''t found a piano teacher yet. Mom has looked for one on the Internet. For now, I practice on the old piano in the living room.
Love,
Amy

What has Amy NOT done yet?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Joined the school band"}, {"key": "B", "text": "Moved to a new apartment"}, {"key": "C", "text": "Made new friends"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Found a piano teacher"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '信中說 I haven''t found a piano teacher yet.（我還沒找到鋼琴老師），haven''t... yet 表示「還沒」。交新朋友、加入樂隊、搬新家都是已經完成的事（have already made、have joined、have lived）。', '["題目問的是 Amy「還沒」做的事。", "信中哪一句用了 haven''t... yet？", "already 和 yet 分別用在什麼樣的句子？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "Amy 說 I have already made two new friends，她已經交到新朋友了。", "A": "Amy 說 I have also joined the school band，她已經加入樂隊了。", "B": "信的第一句就說他們已經在新公寓住了一個月。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-1-18', 'EN-9A-1', 'reading-detail', 'Ken: Mom, have you seen my glasses? I''ve looked everywhere in my room.
Mom: Have you checked your schoolbag?
Ken: Yes, I''ve already checked it twice. They''re not there.
Mom: What about the bathroom? You took a shower an hour ago.
Ken: Oh! I haven''t looked there yet. I''ll go and check.

Where will Ken probably look for his glasses next?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "In the kitchen"}, {"key": "B", "text": "In the bathroom"}, {"key": "C", "text": "In his schoolbag"}, {"key": "D", "text": "In his room"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'Ken 已經找遍房間、書包也找了兩次。媽媽提醒他一小時前洗過澡，Ken 說 I haven''t looked there yet.（我還沒找那裡），there 指浴室，而且他說要去看看，所以他接下來最可能去浴室找。', '["Ken 已經找過哪些地方？", "I haven''t looked there yet. 的 there 指哪裡？", "還沒找過的地方，就是他接下來要去的地方。"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "Ken 說書包已經找過兩次了（already checked it twice）。", "D": "Ken 一開始就說已經找遍了房間（looked everywhere in my room）。", "A": "對話中完全沒有提到廚房。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-2-13', 'EN-9A-2', 'passive-voice', 'Look at this beautiful cake! It (1)＿＿＿ by my sister. She (2)＿＿＿ it for Mom''s birthday yesterday. It has strawberries on top, and it tastes great. Mom was so happy that she took a picture of it before we ate it.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "was made; made"}, {"key": "B", "text": "was made; was made"}, {"key": "C", "text": "made; was made"}, {"key": "D", "text": "is made; was made"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '(1) 主詞 It（蛋糕）是被做出來的，後面又有 by my sister，要用被動語態；昨天做的，用過去式被動 was made。(2) 主詞 She 是動作的執行者，後面接受詞 it，用主動語態的過去式 made。', '["(1) 蛋糕是做的人還是被做的東西？", "(2) 的主詞 She 是做動作的人嗎？後面有沒有受詞？", "yesterday 提示兩格要用什麼時態？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "把兩格弄反了：蛋糕是「被做」的要用被動；姊姊（妹妹）是做蛋糕的人要用主動。", "B": "(2) 的主詞 She 是做蛋糕的人，要用主動語態，而且後面有受詞 it。", "D": "蛋糕昨天做好的，(1) 要用過去式；(2) 的 She 是做動作的人，不能用被動。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-2-14', 'EN-9A-2', 'passive-voice', 'The new park near my home opened last year. Many trees (1)＿＿＿ there before it opened, and now the park is green and beautiful. People (2)＿＿＿ there every evening, and children play on the grass. It has become my favorite place in town.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "were planted; walk"}, {"key": "B", "text": "planted; are walked"}, {"key": "C", "text": "were planted; are walked"}, {"key": "D", "text": "are planted; walked"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '(1) 樹不會自己種，是「被種植」，要用被動；開幕前種的，用過去式被動 were planted（trees 是複數）。(2) People 是自己去散步的人，用主動；every evening 表示現在的習慣，用現在簡單式 walk。', '["(1) 樹是種的人，還是被種的東西？", "(2) People 是做動作的人嗎？", "兩格的時間線索分別是什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "樹是被種的，(1) 要用被動；人是自己去散步的，(2) 要用主動。", "C": "(2) 的主詞 People 是散步的人，是動作的執行者，要用主動。", "D": "樹是公園開幕前種的，要用過去式；(2) 有 every evening，表示現在的習慣，不能用過去式。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-2-15', 'EN-9A-2', 'passive-tense', 'Music in the Park!
A free concert (1)＿＿＿ in Central Park next Sunday at 7 p.m. You don''t need a ticket. Please come early to get a good seat. Drinks can (2)＿＿＿ at the front gate, and food will be sold near the lake. See you there!

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "will hold; be bought"}, {"key": "B", "text": "will be held; be bought"}, {"key": "C", "text": "is held; bought"}, {"key": "D", "text": "will be held; buy"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '(1) 音樂會是被舉辦的，next Sunday 是未來，未來式被動是 will be + 過去分詞：will be held（hold 的過去分詞是 held）。(2) 飲料是被買的，助動詞 can 後面的被動是 can + be + 過去分詞：can be bought。', '["(1) 音樂會是舉辦的人，還是被舉辦的活動？next Sunday 是什麼時態？", "(2) 飲料是被買的嗎？can 後面要接什麼形式？", "未來式和助動詞的被動都是「助動詞 + be + 過去分詞」。"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "音樂會是「被舉辦」的，不會自己舉辦東西，要用被動 will be held。", "D": "飲料是「被買」的，can 後面的被動要用 be + 過去分詞。", "C": "next Sunday 是未來，不能用現在式；can 後面不能直接接過去分詞。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-2-16', 'EN-9A-2', 'passive-tense', 'The Ocean Museum was opened in 1995. Every year, it is visited by about one million people. Many of the fish in the museum were brought from other countries. Last year, the shark area was damaged by an earthquake, so it was closed. Workers are repairing it now, and it will be opened again next spring.

Which is TRUE?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "All the fish in the museum were brought from other countries."}, {"key": "B", "text": "The museum was opened last year."}, {"key": "C", "text": "The museum was damaged by an earthquake in 1995."}, {"key": "D", "text": "The shark area will be opened again next spring."}]'::jsonb, 'D', '文中最後說 Workers are repairing it now, and it will be opened again next spring.，it 指關閉的鯊魚區，未來式被動 will be opened 表示明年春天會重新開放。博物館 1995 年開幕、很多（不是全部）魚來自國外、地震發生在去年。', '["文中出現了哪些年份或時間？各發生了什麼事？", "最後一句的 it 指什麼？", "Many 和 All 的意思一樣嗎？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "博物館 1995 年開幕；去年發生的是鯊魚區被地震損壞。", "A": "文中說 Many of the fish（很多魚），不是全部。", "C": "1995 年是開幕的年份，地震是去年發生的，損壞的是鯊魚區。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-2-17', 'EN-9A-2', 'reading-detail', 'Our school garden was started by the science club three years ago. Now vegetables are grown there by students in every grade. Last month, some of the vegetables were sold at the school fair, and the money was given to a children''s hospital. This year, the garden will be made bigger, so more students can join.

What happened to the money from the vegetables?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "It was used to make the garden bigger."}, {"key": "B", "text": "It was kept by the science club."}, {"key": "C", "text": "It was given to a children''s hospital."}, {"key": "D", "text": "It was used to buy new seeds."}]'::jsonb, 'C', '文中說 some of the vegetables were sold at the school fair, and the money was given to a children''s hospital.，賣菜的錢被捐給了兒童醫院。', '["找到 money 出現的句子。", "the money was given to... 是誰「被給」了錢？", "其他選項的內容，文中有說到嗎？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "花園今年會擴大，但文中沒有說是用賣菜的錢。", "B": "自然社是三年前開闢花園的社團，錢並沒有留給他們。", "D": "文中沒有提到買種子。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-2-18', 'EN-9A-2', 'reading-detail', 'Every October, the Moon Lake Kite Festival is held in our town. Kites of all shapes are flown by people from many countries. This year, the biggest kite was made by a group of high school students in our town; it was 20 meters long. Sadly, on the second day, the festival was stopped because of strong winds. The prizes will be given out next week.

Which is TRUE?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "The biggest kite was made by people from other countries."}, {"key": "B", "text": "The festival is held every spring."}, {"key": "C", "text": "The festival was stopped because of rain."}, {"key": "D", "text": "The winners will get their prizes later."}]'::jsonb, 'D', '文中最後說 The prizes will be given out next week.（獎品下週才會頒發），所以得獎者之後才會拿到獎品。風箏節在十月、最大的風箏是本地高中生做的、停辦原因是強風。', '["風箏節在哪個月舉行？", "最大的風箏是誰做的？", "最後一句 will be given out next week 說明獎品什麼時候頒發？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "風箏節在每年十月舉行，是秋天，不是春天。", "A": "最大的風箏是本鎮的一群高中生做的。", "C": "風箏節第二天停辦是因為強風（strong winds），不是下雨。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-1-13', 'EN-9B-1', 'relative-person', 'Look at the boy (1)＿＿＿ is talking to Ms. Lin. He is my cousin, Sam. He just moved here from Taichung. His sister, (2)＿＿＿ name is Amy, is in my class. Amy and I sit next to each other, and we often eat lunch together.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "who; who"}, {"key": "B", "text": "which; whose"}, {"key": "C", "text": "who; whose"}, {"key": "D", "text": "whose; which"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '(1) 先行詞 the boy 是人，關係代名詞在子句中當主詞（後面接 is talking），用 who。(2) 先行詞 His sister 是人，空格後面接名詞 name，表示「她的名字叫 Amy」，用所有格關係代名詞 whose。', '["(1) 先行詞是人還是物？空格後面接的是動詞還是名詞？", "(2) 空格後面接了什麼名詞？", "表示「……的」的關係代名詞是哪一個？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "先行詞 the boy 是人，(1) 不能用 which。", "A": "(2) 空格後面接名詞 name，表示「她的名字」，要用所有格 whose。", "D": "(1) 空格後面直接接動詞 is talking，要用主格 who；(2) 的先行詞是人，也不能用 which。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-1-14', 'EN-9B-1', 'relative-person', 'In this photo, there are four people. The woman who is holding a baby is my aunt. The man who is standing next to her is my uncle; he is a pilot. The baby, whose name is Ella, is their first child. The old man who is sitting in the chair is my grandpa.

Who is Ella?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "The writer''s aunt"}, {"key": "B", "text": "The writer''s sister"}, {"key": "C", "text": "The writer''s grandpa''s wife"}, {"key": "D", "text": "The writer''s cousin"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'The baby, whose name is Ella, is their first child.，their 指前面的 my aunt 和 my uncle，所以 Ella 是作者阿姨（姑姑）和叔叔（姑丈）的第一個孩子，也就是作者的表（堂）妹，英文是 cousin。', '["whose name is Ella 描述的是照片中的哪一個人？", "their first child 的 their 指誰？", "阿姨（姑姑）的孩子，要怎麼稱呼？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "作者的阿姨（姑姑）是抱著嬰兒的那位女士，不是 Ella。", "B": "Ella 是阿姨（姑姑）和叔叔（姑丈）的孩子，不是作者父母的孩子。", "C": "坐在椅子上的是爺爺，Ella 是嬰兒，不是爺爺的太太。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-1-15', 'EN-9B-1', 'relative-thing', 'I''m very sad today. The bike (1)＿＿＿ my dad gave me last year (2)＿＿＿ stolen yesterday afternoon. I parked it in front of the library, and when I came out, it was gone. I''m going to tell the police about it.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "which; were"}, {"key": "B", "text": "who; was"}, {"key": "C", "text": "whose; is"}, {"key": "D", "text": "which; was"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '(1) 先行詞 The bike 是物品，在子句中當 gave 的受詞，用 which。(2) 整句的主詞是 The bike（關係子句 which my dad gave me last year 只是修飾它），腳踏車是「被偷」，yesterday 是過去，單數主詞用 was stolen。', '["(1) 先行詞是人還是物？", "去掉關係子句後，整句的主詞是什麼？是單數還是複數？", "yesterday afternoon 提示 (2) 要用什麼時態？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "先行詞 The bike 是物品，不能用 who。", "A": "句子的主詞是 The bike（單數），不是 my dad 或 me，be 動詞要用 was。", "C": "空格後面不是接名詞，不能用 whose；而且 yesterday 是過去，要用 was。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-1-16', 'EN-9B-1', 'relative-thing', 'Mr. Lin: Whose books are these? They are on my desk, and I need the desk for my computer.
Ann: The books which (1)＿＿＿ on your desk (2)＿＿＿ to Joe. He left them there this morning.
Mr. Lin: OK. Please tell him to take them back after class.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "are; belong"}, {"key": "B", "text": "is; belongs"}, {"key": "C", "text": "are; belongs"}, {"key": "D", "text": "is; belong"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '(1) which 代替先行詞 The books（複數），關係子句的 be 動詞用 are。(2) 整句的主詞是 The books，which are on your desk 只是修飾語，所以主要動詞用複數 belong（belong to 表示「屬於」）。', '["which 代替的是哪個名詞？", "整句話真正的主詞是什麼？不要被 your desk 騙了。", "主詞是複數時，動詞要不要加 s？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "which 代替的是 The books（複數），整句的主詞也是 The books，兩格都要用複數。", "C": "(2) 的主詞是 The books，不是最靠近的 your desk，動詞不加 s。", "D": "(1) which 代替複數的 The books，be 動詞要用 are。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-1-17', 'EN-9B-1', 'reading-detail', 'Help Wanted
We need a person who can speak English and Japanese, who is free on weekends, and who likes working with children. Please call Ms. Ho at 2233-4455.

Who is the best person for this job?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Ben, who loves kids and is free on weekends, speaks only English."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Cindy, who speaks English and Japanese and is free on weekends, has taught children for two years."}, {"key": "C", "text": "David, who speaks Japanese and English, doesn''t like noisy children."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Amy, who speaks English and Japanese, works at a bank on weekends."}]'::jsonb, 'B', '徵人條件有三個（三個 who 子句）：會說英文和日文、週末有空、喜歡和小孩一起工作。Cindy 會說英日文、週末有空，而且教過小孩兩年，三個條件都符合。Amy 週末要上班、Ben 不會日文、David 不喜歡小孩。', '["徵人廣告用了幾個 who 子句？各是什麼條件？", "把每個人的資料和三個條件一一對照。", "只有一個人三個條件全部符合。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "Amy 週末要在銀行上班，不符合「週末有空」的條件。", "A": "Ben 只會說英文，不符合「會說英文和日文」的條件。", "C": "David 不喜歡吵鬧的小孩，不符合「喜歡和孩子相處」的條件。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-1-18', 'EN-9B-1', 'reading-detail', 'Guess what animal I am thinking of. It is an animal that lives in the sea, but it isn''t a fish. Its babies drink milk from their mothers. It can''t stay under the water all the time; it must come up to get air. One kind of this animal is the biggest animal that has ever lived on Earth.

What animal is it?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "A shark"}, {"key": "B", "text": "An elephant"}, {"key": "C", "text": "A turtle"}, {"key": "D", "text": "A whale"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '線索：住在海裡但不是魚、寶寶喝母奶、要浮上水面換氣，而且其中一種（藍鯨）是地球上有史以來最大的動物。符合所有條件的是鯨魚（whale）。', '["題目給了幾個線索？把每個 that 子句的內容整理出來。", "住在海裡卻不是魚，寶寶還喝母奶，是哪一類動物？", "地球上最大的動物是什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "鯊魚是魚，但文中說 it isn''t a fish。", "B": "大象住在陸地上，但文中說這種動物 lives in the sea。", "C": "海龜的寶寶不喝母奶，而且海龜也不是地球上最大的動物。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-2-13', 'EN-9B-2', 'indirect-question', 'Tourist: Excuse me. Could you tell me (1)＿＿＿?
Clerk: The next one leaves at 3:15.
Tourist: Thank you. And do you know (2)＿＿＿?
Clerk: Sure. You can buy one at the machine over there. It only takes coins.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "when does the next bus leave; where I can buy a ticket"}, {"key": "B", "text": "when the next bus leaves; where I can buy a ticket"}, {"key": "C", "text": "when the next bus leaves; where can I buy a ticket"}, {"key": "D", "text": "when the next bus leave; where I buy can a ticket"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '間接問句要用直述句語序：疑問詞 + 主詞 + 動詞。(1) When does the next bus leave? 去掉 does，主詞 the next bus 是單數，動詞加 s：when the next bus leaves。(2) Where can I buy a ticket? 改成 where I can buy a ticket。', '["疑問句放進 Could you tell me / do you know 後面時，語序要怎麼改？", "去掉助動詞 does 之後，動詞要不要變化？", "間接問句中，主詞要放在助動詞 can 的前面還是後面？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "(1) 保留了直接問句的 does 倒裝，間接問句要改成直述句語序。", "C": "(2) 保留了直接問句 can I 的倒裝，間接問句要主詞在前：I can。", "D": "去掉 does 後，第三人稱單數的 leave 要加 s；can 也要放在動詞 buy 前面。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-2-14', 'EN-9B-2', 'indirect-question', 'Ms. Wang: Amy, do you know (1)＿＿＿ yesterday? I didn''t see him in class.
Amy: No, he didn''t. He had a bad cold, so he stayed home.
Ms. Wang: I see. Can you tell me (2)＿＿＿? I want to call his parents.
Amy: Sorry, I don''t know his phone number.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "if Ken came to school; what is his phone number"}, {"key": "B", "text": "did Ken come to school; what his phone number is"}, {"key": "C", "text": "if Ken came to school; what his phone number is"}, {"key": "D", "text": "where Ken came to school; what his phone number is"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '(1) Amy 回答 No, he didn''t.，可知原本的問題是 Yes/No 問句 Did Ken come to school yesterday?，變成間接問句要用 if 連接，去掉 did、動詞改成過去式：if Ken came to school。(2) What is his phone number? 改成直述句語序：what his phone number is。', '["Amy 用 No, he didn''t. 回答，原本是哪一種問句？", "Yes/No 問句變成間接問句時要加哪個字？", "(2) 的主詞是什麼？它要放在 is 的前面還是後面？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "(1) 間接問句不能保留 did 倒裝，Yes/No 問句要用 if 連接。", "A": "(2) 間接問句要用直述句語序，主詞 his phone number 要放在 is 前面。", "D": "Amy 回答 No, he didn''t.，表示原本是 Yes/No 問句，要用 if（是否），不是 where。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-2-15', 'EN-9B-2', 'reading-inference', 'A: Good afternoon. What''s the problem today?
B: I''ve had a terrible toothache since last night. I couldn''t sleep at all.
A: Let me take a look. Open your mouth, please... Hmm, there''s a big hole in this tooth. I''ll fix it for you today. After that, don''t eat too many sweets, and brush your teeth after every meal.
B: OK. Thank you.

Where does this conversation probably take place?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "At a dentist''s office"}, {"key": "B", "text": "At a hotel"}, {"key": "C", "text": "At a restaurant"}, {"key": "D", "text": "At a candy store"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'B 說牙痛（toothache）睡不著，A 請 B 張開嘴巴檢查，發現牙齒有個洞，說今天幫他補好，並提醒少吃甜食、飯後刷牙。能檢查並治療牙齒的是牙醫，所以對話最可能發生在牙醫診所。', '["B 哪裡不舒服？", "A 為 B 做了什麼？會說這些話的是什麼職業的人？", "不要只看到單一個字（sweets、meal）就選答案。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "看到 sweets 就選糖果店，但 A 是叫 B 不要吃太多甜食，還要幫 B 補牙。", "C": "看到 meal 就選餐廳，但對話內容是檢查和治療牙齒。", "B": "看到 couldn''t sleep 就聯想到旅館，但 B 睡不著是因為牙痛。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-2-16', 'EN-9B-2', 'reading-inference', 'Jenny practiced the piano for three hours every day for a month before the music contest. On the day of the contest, her hands were shaking before she went on stage. But when she started to play, she forgot about everything around her. When she finished, everyone stood up and clapped for a long time. Jenny smiled with tears in her eyes.

How did Jenny probably feel at the end?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Happy and proud"}, {"key": "B", "text": "Bored and tired"}, {"key": "C", "text": "Nervous and afraid"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Angry and upset"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Jenny 苦練一個月，表演結束時全場起立、鼓掌很久，她 smiled with tears in her eyes（含著淚微笑），這是喜極而泣，表示她很開心、也為自己感到驕傲。上台前手發抖的緊張已經過去了。', '["題目問的是哪個時間點的心情？", "表演結束時，觀眾有什麼反應？", "一邊微笑一邊流淚，通常是什麼樣的心情？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "緊張發抖是她上台「之前」的心情，題目問的是表演結束時。", "D": "全場起立鼓掌很久，她還面帶微笑，沒有生氣的線索。", "B": "她努力練習一個月，表演後得到熱烈掌聲，不會覺得無聊。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-2-17', 'EN-9B-2', 'reading-main-idea', 'Some students are afraid to ask questions in class. They worry about what others will think, or they don''t know how they should ask. But asking questions is one of the best ways to learn. When you ask, you find out what you don''t understand. Most teachers are happy when students ask questions. If you are shy, you can write down your questions and ask your teacher after class.

What is the main idea of the passage?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Teachers don''t like students who ask questions."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Shy students should not talk in class."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Students shouldn''t be afraid to ask questions."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Students should write down everything the teacher says."}]'::jsonb, 'C', '作者先說有些學生不敢發問，接著用 But 轉折，說發問是最好的學習方法之一，老師也樂於學生發問，最後給害羞的人建議。全文都在鼓勵學生不要害怕發問。', '["第一句提出了什麼問題？", "But 之後，作者的看法是什麼？", "最後一句的建議是在幫助什麼樣的學生？目的是什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "文中說 Most teachers are happy when students ask questions.，和這句相反。", "B": "作者是建議害羞的學生可以下課再問，不是叫他們不要說話。", "D": "作者只建議害羞的人把「問題」寫下來，不是寫下老師說的每句話。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-2-18', 'EN-9B-2', 'reading-main-idea', 'Three years ago, people in Green Town threw away thousands of plastic bags every day. Then the town decided to make a change. Now, stores don''t give out free plastic bags, so people bring their own bags when they go shopping. Many restaurants also let people pay less if they bring their own cups. Today, there is much less plastic in the town''s trash.

What is the best title for this passage?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Why Plastic Bags Are Cheap"}, {"key": "B", "text": "How Green Town Uses Fewer Plastic Bags"}, {"key": "C", "text": "A Famous Restaurant in Green Town"}, {"key": "D", "text": "The Best Stores in Green Town"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '文章先說三年前鎮上每天丟掉大量塑膠袋，接著說明鎮上的改變：商店不再免費提供塑膠袋、餐廳鼓勵自備杯子，結果垃圾中的塑膠少了很多。全文在說綠鎮如何減少使用塑膠袋，所以最好的標題是 How Green Town Uses Fewer Plastic Bags。', '["文章前後比較了綠鎮哪方面的變化？", "商店和餐廳的例子都是為了說明什麼？", "好的標題要能涵蓋整篇文章，而不只是其中一個細節。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "文中沒有比較哪些商店最好，商店只是不再免費給塑膠袋。", "A": "文中沒有討論塑膠袋的價格。", "C": "餐廳只是其中一個例子，而且文中沒有提到某家有名的餐廳。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-1-19', 'EN-7A-1', 'be-verb', 'I ＿＿＿ a student at Hope Junior High School.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "am"}, {"key": "B", "text": "is"}, {"key": "C", "text": "are"}, {"key": "D", "text": "be"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '主詞是 I（我），be 動詞固定搭配 am，所以是 I am a student.（我是學生）。is 配第三人稱單數，are 配 you、we、they 或複數。', '["先看主詞是誰。", "I 有自己專屬的 be 動詞。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "以為 a student 是單數就用 is，但 be 動詞要看主詞 I，不是看後面的名詞。", "C": "把 are 當成萬用的 be 動詞，忘了 I 只能配 am。", "D": "be 是原形，句子裡要依主詞變化成 am、is、are。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-1-20', 'EN-7A-1', 'be-verb', 'The books on the desk ＿＿＿ new.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "be"}, {"key": "B", "text": "is"}, {"key": "C", "text": "am"}, {"key": "D", "text": "are"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '主詞是 The books（那些書），books 有 s 是複數；on the desk 只是說明書在哪裡。複數主詞的 be 動詞用 are。', '["真正的主詞是 books 還是 desk？", "books 是單數還是複數？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "看到最靠近空格的 desk 是單數就用 is，誤把 desk 當主詞。", "C": "am 只能和 I 搭配。", "A": "be 是原形，不能直接當句子的動詞。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-1-21', 'EN-7A-1', 'be-verb', '＿＿＿ Mr. Wang your English teacher? — No, he isn''t. He is our math teacher.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Are"}, {"key": "B", "text": "Is"}, {"key": "C", "text": "Do"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Does"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '答句用 he isn''t，可知問句是 be 動詞疑問句；主詞 Mr. Wang 是第三人稱單數，所以把 Is 放句首：Is Mr. Wang your English teacher?', '["先看答句用的是 be 動詞還是助動詞。", "Mr. Wang 是一個人，配哪個 be 動詞？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "看到 your 就以為要用 Are，但主詞是 Mr. Wang 一個人。", "C": "句子裡沒有一般動詞，不能用助動詞 Do 來問。", "D": "Does 雖然配第三人稱單數，但答句是 isn''t，表示要用 be 動詞而不是助動詞。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-1-22', 'EN-7A-1', 'be-verb', 'Where ＿＿＿ my glasses? — They''re on the table.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "am"}, {"key": "B", "text": "are"}, {"key": "C", "text": "does"}, {"key": "D", "text": "is"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'glasses（眼鏡）在英文裡一定是複數，答句也用 They''re 來代替，所以 be 動詞要用 are：Where are my glasses?', '["答句用哪個代名詞代替 my glasses？", "glasses 字尾有 es，是單數還是複數？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "中文說「一副眼鏡」像是單數，就用 is，忘了 glasses 是複數。", "A": "am 只配 I，主詞是 my glasses。", "C": "句子沒有一般動詞，問「在哪裡」要用 be 動詞，不用 does。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-1-23', 'EN-7A-1', 'pronoun', 'Lisa and I are good friends. ＿＿＿ are in Class 702.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "She"}, {"key": "B", "text": "We"}, {"key": "C", "text": "They"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Us"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'Lisa and I（Lisa 和我）包含說話的人自己，代名詞要用「我們」；空格在句首當主詞，用主格 We。', '["Lisa and I 裡面有沒有「我」？", "「我們」當主詞時要用主格還是受格？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "They 是「他們」，不包含說話者自己，但這裡有 I。", "D": "Us 是受格，不能放在句首當主詞。", "A": "She 只代替 Lisa 一個人，而且 be 動詞是 are，主詞應是複數。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-1-24', 'EN-7A-1', 'pronoun', 'These are not my shoes. ＿＿＿ are under the bed.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "I"}, {"key": "B", "text": "Me"}, {"key": "C", "text": "Mine"}, {"key": "D", "text": "My"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '空格當主詞，後面直接接 are，沒有名詞，所以要用所有格代名詞 Mine（= my shoes，我的鞋子）。My 後面一定要接名詞。', '["空格後面有沒有接名詞？", "「我的（東西）」單獨使用時要用哪個字？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "My 是所有格形容詞，後面必須接名詞，例如 My shoes are...。", "B": "Me 是受格，不能當主詞，也不能表示「我的」。", "A": "I 是「我」，句意變成「我在床底下」，而且 I 不配 are。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-1-25', 'EN-7A-1', 'pronoun', 'Mr. and Mrs. Chen are my neighbors. ＿＿＿ dog is very friendly.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Their"}, {"key": "B", "text": "They"}, {"key": "C", "text": "Theirs"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Them"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '空格後面接名詞 dog，要用所有格形容詞。Mr. and Mrs. Chen 是兩個人，「他們的狗」是 Their dog。', '["空格後面接的是名詞還是動詞？", "「他們的」後面接名詞時用哪個字？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "They 是主格，They dog 不合文法，主格後面不能直接接名詞。", "D": "Them 是受格，只能放在動詞或介系詞後面。", "C": "Theirs 是所有格代名詞，後面不能再接名詞 dog。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-1-26', 'EN-7A-1', 'dialogue-response', 'A: How are you today?
B: ＿＿＿', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Nice to meet you, too, Ken."}, {"key": "B", "text": "I''m fine, thank you. And you?"}, {"key": "C", "text": "Yes, I am. I''m a student."}, {"key": "D", "text": "I''m Ken. I''m from Taipei."}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'How are you? 是問「你好嗎？」，要回答自己的狀況，例如 I''m fine, thank you. And you?（我很好，謝謝。你呢？）。', '["How are you? 是在問名字還是問狀況？", "回答後也可以禮貌地反問對方。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "I''m Ken. I''m from Taipei. 是自我介紹，回答 What''s your name? 或 Where are you from?，不是說自己好不好。", "A": "Nice to meet you, too, Ken. 是回應初次見面的 Nice to meet you.", "C": "Yes, I am. 只能回答 Are you...? 的是非問句，How 問句不能用 Yes 回答。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-1-27', 'EN-7A-1', 'dialogue-response', 'A: Is that your brother?
B: ＿＿＿ He''s my cousin, Sam.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "No, he doesn''t."}, {"key": "B", "text": "No, they aren''t."}, {"key": "C", "text": "No, he isn''t."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Yes, he is."}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'B 接著說「他是我表哥 Sam」，表示那個人不是 B 的哥哥，所以要否定回答。問句用 Is，答句也用 be 動詞：No, he isn''t.', '["B 後面那句話說那個人是誰？", "問句用 Is，回答要用同一種動詞。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "沒注意後面說他是 cousin，不是 brother，所以不能肯定回答。", "A": "問句用 be 動詞 Is，答句不能改用助動詞 doesn''t。", "B": "問的是一個人，不能用複數 they aren''t。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-1-28', 'EN-7A-1', 'reading-detail', 'Hi, I''m Ryan. I''m from Canada, but my family and I are in Taiwan now. My father is an engineer, and my mother is a nurse. My sister, Kate, and I are students at Rose Junior High School. Kate is in the eighth grade, and I am in the seventh grade. Our favorite teacher is Ms. Huang. She is our music teacher.

Who is a nurse?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Kate"}, {"key": "B", "text": "Ms. Huang"}, {"key": "C", "text": "Ryan''s father"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Ryan''s mother"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '文中寫 my mother is a nurse，my 指的是 Ryan，所以護理師是 Ryan 的媽媽。爸爸是工程師，Ms. Huang 是音樂老師，Kate 是學生。', '["找出 nurse 這個字出現在哪一句。", "那一句的主詞是誰？my 指的是寫信的人。"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "把 engineer 和 nurse 看反了，Ryan 的爸爸是工程師。", "B": "Ms. Huang 是他們的音樂老師，不是護理師。", "A": "Kate 是 Ryan 的姊姊，還在讀八年級，是學生。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-1-29', 'EN-7A-1', 'reading-detail', 'These are three new students in our class.
Andy is thirteen. He is from Tainan, and he is in the art club.
Becky and Cindy are twins. They are twelve, and they are from Taichung. Becky is in the art club, but Cindy isn''t. She is in the music club.

Which is TRUE?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "The twins are thirteen years old."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Andy and Cindy are from the same city."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Cindy and Andy are in the art club."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Andy and Becky are in the same club."}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Andy 在美術社（art club），Becky 也在美術社，所以 Andy 和 Becky 在同一個社團。Andy 來自臺南、雙胞胎來自臺中；雙胞胎是 12 歲；Cindy 在音樂社。', '["把三個人的年齡、城市、社團各自整理出來。", "Becky 和 Cindy 雖然是雙胞胎，社團一樣嗎？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "Andy 來自臺南，Cindy 來自臺中，不是同一個城市。", "A": "13 歲的是 Andy，雙胞胎是 12 歲，把年齡配錯人。", "C": "以為雙胞胎社團一樣，但文中說 Cindy isn''t（不在美術社），她在音樂社。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-1-30', 'EN-7A-1', 'pronoun', 'Jim: Mom, this is Leo. (1)＿＿＿ is my new classmate.
Mom: Hi, Leo. Nice to meet you. Are you from Taipei?
Leo: No, I''m not. My parents and I are from Tainan, but now (2)＿＿＿ live in Taipei.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "He; we"}, {"key": "B", "text": "Him; our"}, {"key": "C", "text": "His; we"}, {"key": "D", "text": "He; us"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '(1) 代替 Leo 當主詞，Leo 是男生，主格用 He。(2) 代替 My parents and I（包含 Leo 自己），後面接動詞 live，要用主格「我們」we。', '["兩個空格後面接的都是動詞，所以都要當主詞。", "My parents and I 包含說話的 Leo 自己，要用「我們」。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "(2) 的 us 是受格，不能放在動詞 live 前面當主詞。", "C": "(1) 的 His 是所有格，後面要接名詞，不能直接接 is 當主詞。", "B": "Him 是受格、our 是所有格，兩個都不能當主詞。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-2-19', 'EN-7A-2', 'simple-present', 'My mother ＿＿＿ to work at eight every morning.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "is go"}, {"key": "B", "text": "go"}, {"key": "C", "text": "goes"}, {"key": "D", "text": "going"}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'every morning 表示每天的習慣，用現在簡單式。主詞 My mother 是第三人稱單數，go 要加 es 變成 goes。', '["every morning 表示什麼樣的動作？", "第三人稱單數當主詞時，動詞要怎麼變化？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "忘了主詞是第三人稱單數，動詞要加 es。", "D": "going 是 V-ing，前面沒有 be 動詞不能單獨當動詞。", "A": "be 動詞和一般動詞原形不能同時放在一起當動詞。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-2-20', 'EN-7A-2', 'simple-present', 'We ＿＿＿ English class on Mondays and Fridays.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "has"}, {"key": "B", "text": "are have"}, {"key": "C", "text": "having"}, {"key": "D", "text": "have"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'on Mondays and Fridays 表示每週固定的習慣，用現在簡單式。主詞 We 是複數，動詞用原形 have。', '["主詞 We 是第幾人稱？", "has 只配哪一類主詞？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "has 只配第三人稱單數（he、she、it），We 要用 have。", "C": "having 前面沒有 be 動詞，不能當句子的動詞。", "B": "are 和 have 不能同時當動詞，一句只需要一個主要動詞。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-2-21', 'EN-7A-2', 'frequency', 'Lucy ＿＿＿ drinks milk. She drinks a glass of it every morning.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "never"}, {"key": "B", "text": "sometimes"}, {"key": "C", "text": "always"}, {"key": "D", "text": "seldom"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '後一句說她每天早上都喝一杯牛奶，表示頻率是「總是」，要用 always。', '["後面那句說她多久喝一次牛奶？", "「每天都做」對應哪一個頻率副詞？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "never 是「從不」，和「每天早上都喝」矛盾。", "D": "seldom 是「很少」，和每天都喝不符。", "B": "sometimes 是「有時候」，但每天都喝的頻率比有時候高很多。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-2-22', 'EN-7A-2', 'dialogue-response', 'A: Where does your uncle work?
B: ＿＿＿', '[{"key": "A", "text": "He works very hard."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Yes, he does."}, {"key": "C", "text": "He goes to work by bus."}, {"key": "D", "text": "He works in a hospital."}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Where 問「在哪裡」，要回答地點。He works in a hospital.（他在醫院工作）說出工作地點，最合適。', '["問句的疑問詞是哪一個？", "Where 要用什麼資訊來回答？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "Where 開頭的問句不能用 Yes 或 No 回答。", "A": "He works very hard. 說的是工作的態度，回答的是 How。", "C": "by bus 是交通方式，回答的是 How does he go to work?"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-2-23', 'EN-7A-2', 'simple-present', 'My brother ＿＿＿ TV after dinner. He studies in his room.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "don''t watch"}, {"key": "B", "text": "isn''t watch"}, {"key": "C", "text": "doesn''t watch"}, {"key": "D", "text": "doesn''t watches"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '後句說他在房間讀書，所以前句是否定。主詞 My brother 是第三人稱單數，否定要用 doesn''t，後面的動詞要用原形 watch。', '["主詞是第三人稱單數，否定助動詞用哪一個？", "用了 doesn''t 以後，動詞還要加 s 嗎？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "don''t 配 I、you、we、they，第三人稱單數要用 doesn''t。", "D": "doesn''t 後面的動詞要回到原形，不能再加 es。", "B": "watch 是一般動詞，否定要用助動詞，不能用 isn''t。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-2-24', 'EN-7A-2', 'simple-present', 'What time ＿＿＿ your father get up on Sundays? — At nine.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "are"}, {"key": "B", "text": "is"}, {"key": "C", "text": "does"}, {"key": "D", "text": "do"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '句子有一般動詞 get up，疑問句要用助動詞。主詞 your father 是第三人稱單數，所以用 does，後面動詞用原形 get。', '["句子裡的動詞 get up 是 be 動詞還是一般動詞？", "主詞 your father 是單數還是複數？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "看到 your 就用 do，但主詞是 your father 一個人，要用 does。", "B": "句子已經有一般動詞 get up，不能再用 be 動詞 is 來問。", "A": "are 是 be 動詞，而且是複數，和 get up 不能搭配。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-2-25', 'EN-7A-2', 'frequency', 'Mary ＿＿＿ tired in the morning because she goes to bed late every night.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "always is"}, {"key": "B", "text": "always"}, {"key": "C", "text": "is always"}, {"key": "D", "text": "is never"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '她每晚都很晚睡，所以早上「總是」很累。頻率副詞要放在 be 動詞後面，因此是 is always tired。', '["她每天很晚睡，早上會累嗎？", "頻率副詞遇到 be 動詞時，要放在前面還是後面？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "頻率副詞要放在 be 動詞後面，always is 的位置放反了。", "B": "tired 是形容詞，前面一定要有 be 動詞，只用 always 缺少動詞。", "D": "每天晚睡應該會累，is never tired（從不累）和原因不合。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-2-26', 'EN-7A-2', 'frequency', 'A: How often does Sam play tennis?
B: ＿＿＿', '[{"key": "A", "text": "For two hours."}, {"key": "B", "text": "With his father."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Three times a week."}, {"key": "D", "text": "In the park."}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'How often 是問「多常、多久一次」，要回答頻率，例如 Three times a week.（一週三次）。', '["How often 問的是時間長度、地點，還是次數？", "回答頻率常用「次數＋a week / a month」。"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "For two hours. 是回答 How long（多久的時間）。", "D": "In the park. 是回答 Where（在哪裡）。", "B": "With his father. 是回答 With whom / Who（和誰）。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-2-27', 'EN-7A-2', 'dialogue-response', 'A: Do you and your sister walk to school?
B: ＿＿＿ We ride our bikes.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "No, we aren''t."}, {"key": "B", "text": "No, we don''t."}, {"key": "C", "text": "No, they don''t."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Yes, we do."}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'B 說「我們騎腳踏車」，表示不是走路上學，要否定回答。問句主詞 you and your sister，回答時要用 we，助動詞用 don''t。', '["B 說他們怎麼去學校？", "you and your sister 在回答時要換成哪個代名詞？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "沒注意後面說騎腳踏車，所以不能說 Yes。", "C": "回答的人自己也在裡面，要用 we，不能用 they。", "A": "問句用助動詞 Do，回答也要用 don''t，不能改用 be 動詞。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-2-28', 'EN-7A-2', 'reading-detail', 'Nancy loves animals. On Saturdays, she helps at an animal hospital near her home. She feeds the dogs there and cleans their rooms. On Sundays, she usually goes hiking in the mountains with her family. She seldom stays home on weekends.

Where does Nancy go on Saturdays?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "A pet shop"}, {"key": "B", "text": "Her friend''s house"}, {"key": "C", "text": "An animal hospital"}, {"key": "D", "text": "A mountain"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '文中說 On Saturdays, she helps at an animal hospital near her home.，所以星期六她去動物醫院幫忙。去爬山是星期日的事。', '["找出 On Saturdays 那一句。", "注意星期六和星期日做的事不一樣。"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "看到餵狗就猜是寵物店，但文中說的是 animal hospital。", "D": "去山上爬山是星期日（On Sundays）的活動。", "B": "文中沒有提到去朋友家。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-2-29', 'EN-7A-2', 'reading-detail', 'In Kelly''s family, everyone goes out early on weekdays. Her father always takes the MRT to work. Her mother usually drives to work, but she takes the bus on rainy days. Kelly and her brother Danny live near their school, so they walk there every day. Danny never takes the bus.

It is a rainy Wednesday morning. Who takes the bus?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Kelly''s father"}, {"key": "B", "text": "Nobody in the family"}, {"key": "C", "text": "Kelly''s mother"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Kelly and Danny"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '星期三是平日，又是下雨天。媽媽平常開車，但 on rainy days 會搭公車，所以搭公車的是媽媽。爸爸總是搭捷運，Kelly 和 Danny 每天走路。', '["先確認星期三是平日，再注意「下雨」這個條件。", "誰的交通方式會因為下雨而改變？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "爸爸 always takes the MRT，搭的是捷運不是公車。", "D": "Kelly 和 Danny 每天走路上學，Danny 更是 never takes the bus。", "B": "只看到 usually drives，沒讀到後面 but she takes the bus on rainy days。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7A-2-30', 'EN-7A-2', 'simple-present', 'My grandparents live in the country. Grandpa (1)＿＿＿ up at five every day and works on the farm. Grandma (2)＿＿＿ like to get up early, so she gets up at seven.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "get; doesn''t"}, {"key": "B", "text": "gets; don''t"}, {"key": "C", "text": "gets; doesn''t"}, {"key": "D", "text": "gets; isn''t"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '(1) 主詞 Grandpa 是第三人稱單數，每天的習慣用現在簡單式，get 要加 s 變 gets。(2) 奶奶七點才起床，表示她「不喜歡」早起；主詞第三人稱單數、動詞 like 是一般動詞，否定用 doesn''t。', '["兩個空格的主詞各是誰？是單數還是複數？", "(2) 後面接一般動詞 like，否定要用助動詞還是 be 動詞？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "(1) 主詞 Grandpa 是第三人稱單數，get 要加 s。", "B": "(2) 主詞 Grandma 是第三人稱單數，否定要用 doesn''t，不是 don''t。", "D": "(2) like 是一般動詞，否定不能用 be 動詞 isn''t。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-1-19', 'EN-7B-1', 'present-progressive', 'Be quiet! The baby ＿＿＿.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "is sleeping"}, {"key": "B", "text": "are sleeping"}, {"key": "C", "text": "sleeps"}, {"key": "D", "text": "sleeping"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Be quiet!（安靜！）表示寶寶「現在正在」睡覺，用現在進行式 be + V-ing。主詞 The baby 是單數，be 動詞用 is：is sleeping。', '["叫大家安靜，是因為寶寶現在正在做什麼？", "現在進行式的形式是什麼？主詞是單數還是複數？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "sleeps 是現在簡單式，表示習慣，不能表達「此刻正在睡」。", "B": "The baby 是單數，be 動詞要用 is，不是 are。", "D": "只有 V-ing 少了 be 動詞，不能構成現在進行式。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-1-20', 'EN-7B-1', 'imperative', '＿＿＿ careful! The floor is wet.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Are"}, {"key": "B", "text": "Be"}, {"key": "C", "text": "Is"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Being"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '祈使句用來提醒或命令，以動詞原形開頭。careful 是形容詞，前面要用 be 動詞的原形 Be：Be careful!（小心！）', '["這句話是在提醒別人，屬於哪一種句子？", "祈使句開頭的動詞要用什麼形式？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "Is 放句首會變成疑問句，而且句尾是驚嘆號，不是問句。", "A": "Are 不是原形，祈使句要用原形動詞開頭。", "D": "Being 是 V-ing 形式，祈使句不用 V-ing 開頭。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-1-21', 'EN-7B-1', 'present-progressive', 'Look! Ben and Leo ＿＿＿ soccer on the playground.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "is playing"}, {"key": "B", "text": "are playing"}, {"key": "C", "text": "playing"}, {"key": "D", "text": "play"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'Look! 表示叫人看「現在正在發生」的事，用現在進行式。主詞 Ben and Leo 是兩個人，用 are playing。', '["Look! 暗示動作是什麼時候發生的？", "Ben and Leo 是幾個人？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "主詞是兩個人，be 動詞要用 are 而不是 is。", "D": "play 是現在簡單式，表示習慣，不能表達「看！正在踢」。", "C": "playing 前面少了 be 動詞。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-1-22', 'EN-7B-1', 'dialogue-response', 'A: What are you doing, Mary?
B: ＿＿＿', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Yes, I am. I''m very busy."}, {"key": "B", "text": "I''m reading a comic book."}, {"key": "C", "text": "I read comic books at home."}, {"key": "D", "text": "I''m Mary, Tom''s sister."}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'What are you doing? 問「你現在正在做什麼？」，要用現在進行式回答：I''m reading a comic book.（我正在看漫畫）。', '["問句用的是哪一種時態？", "回答時要和問句用同一種時態。"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "I read comic books at home. 是現在簡單式，說的是習慣，不是現在正在做的事。", "A": "What 開頭的問句不能用 Yes 回答。", "D": "I''m Mary, Tom''s sister. 是在介紹自己，但對方問的是正在做什麼。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-1-23', 'EN-7B-1', 'present-progressive', 'Peter is ＿＿＿ in the pool now.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "swims"}, {"key": "B", "text": "swiming"}, {"key": "C", "text": "swim"}, {"key": "D", "text": "swimming"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'is ... now 是現在進行式，要用 V-ing。swim 是「短母音＋單一子音」結尾的單音節字，要重複字尾 m 再加 ing：swimming。', '["is 後面接什麼形式的動詞，才是現在進行式？", "swim 加 ing 時，字尾子音要不要重複？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "知道要加 ing，但忘了 swim 要重複字尾 m。", "A": "swims 是現在簡單式，不能接在 is 後面。", "C": "swim 是原形，不能接在 be 動詞 is 後面。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-1-24', 'EN-7B-1', 'present-progressive', '＿＿＿ the students ＿＿＿ a test now? — Yes. Please be quiet.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Is; taking"}, {"key": "B", "text": "Are; taking"}, {"key": "C", "text": "Do; take"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Are; take"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'now 表示現在正在進行，疑問句要把 be 動詞移到句首，動詞用 V-ing。主詞 the students 是複數，所以用 Are ... taking。', '["now 提示你要用哪一種時態？", "the students 是單數還是複數？動詞要用什麼形式？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "Do ... take 是現在簡單式疑問句，問的是習慣，不是此刻。", "A": "the students 是複數，不能用 Is。", "D": "be 動詞後面的動詞要用 V-ing，Are ... take 不合文法。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-1-25', 'EN-7B-1', 'imperative', '＿＿＿ late again, Tim. Class starts at eight.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Don''t"}, {"key": "B", "text": "Not be"}, {"key": "C", "text": "Doesn''t be"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Don''t be"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '否定祈使句是 Don''t + 原形動詞。late 是形容詞，前面需要 be，所以是 Don''t be late.（不要遲到）。', '["否定的祈使句要怎麼開頭？", "late 是形容詞還是動詞？前面需要什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "late 是形容詞，Don''t 後面要先接原形動詞 be。", "B": "祈使句的否定要用 Don''t，不能只用 Not。", "C": "祈使句沒有主詞，否定一律用 Don''t，不用 Doesn''t。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-1-26', 'EN-7B-1', 'imperative', 'It''s raining. Let''s ＿＿＿ out today. Let''s watch a movie at home.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "not going"}, {"key": "B", "text": "not go"}, {"key": "C", "text": "don''t go"}, {"key": "D", "text": "no go"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'Let''s 的否定是 Let''s not + 原形動詞，所以「我們今天不要出去」是 Let''s not go out today.', '["Let''s 後面接什麼形式的動詞？", "Let''s 的否定，not 要放在哪裡？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "一般祈使句否定用 Don''t，但 Let''s 的否定是 Let''s not，不是 Let''s don''t。", "A": "Let''s 後面要接原形動詞，不能接 V-ing。", "D": "no 不能用來否定動詞，要用 not。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-1-27', 'EN-7B-1', 'dialogue-response', 'A: Please pass me the salt.
B: ＿＿＿', '[{"key": "A", "text": "That''s all right."}, {"key": "B", "text": "You''re welcome."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Here you are."}, {"key": "D", "text": "I''m sorry to hear that."}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'A 請 B 把鹽遞過來，B 把東西交給對方時常說 Here you are.（拿去吧／給你）。', '["A 是在道謝、道歉，還是請別人做事？", "把東西交給別人時通常說什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "You''re welcome. 是對方說謝謝時的回答。", "A": "That''s all right. 多用來回應對方的道歉。", "D": "I''m sorry to hear that. 是聽到壞消息時的回應。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-1-28', 'EN-7B-1', 'reading-detail', 'It is seven o''clock in the evening at the Lins'' house. Mr. Lin is cooking dinner in the kitchen. His son, Jim, is putting bowls and chopsticks on the table. Mrs. Lin is in the living room. She is talking with Grandma on the phone. Their daughter, Amy, is taking a bath.

What is Mrs. Lin doing?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "She is taking a bath."}, {"key": "B", "text": "She is talking with Grandma on the phone."}, {"key": "C", "text": "She is putting bowls on the table."}, {"key": "D", "text": "She is cooking dinner."}]'::jsonb, 'B', '文中說 Mrs. Lin is in the living room. She is talking with Grandma on the phone.，所以林太太正在和奶奶講電話。煮飯的是林先生。', '["找到 Mrs. Lin 出現的句子。", "後面那句的 She 指的是誰？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "煮晚餐的是 Mr. Lin，不是 Mrs. Lin。", "A": "在洗澡的是女兒 Amy。", "C": "擺碗筷的是兒子 Jim。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-1-29', 'EN-7B-1', 'imperative', 'Museum Notice
1. Please keep your voice down.
2. Don''t touch the paintings.
3. Don''t take photos in Room A. Photos are OK in Room B.

Which visitor is NOT following the rules?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Leo is taking photos in Room B."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Ken is taking photos of the paintings in Room A."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Amy is talking quietly with her mom in Room B."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Sue is looking at the paintings in Room A."}]'::jsonb, 'B', '第 3 條規定在 A 室不能拍照，Ken 卻在 A 室拍畫作，違反規定。Amy 小聲說話符合第 1 條；B 室可以拍照；只是看畫沒有碰觸，也沒有違規。', '["把每個人的行為和三條規則一一對照。", "拍照的規定在 A 室和 B 室有什麼不同？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "規定是降低音量，小聲說話（talking quietly）是遵守規則。", "A": "第 3 條說 B 室可以拍照，Leo 沒有違規。", "D": "規定是不能碰畫，只是看畫沒有違規。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-1-30', 'EN-7B-1', 'present-progressive', 'It is three o''clock on Saturday afternoon. Right now, my dad (1)＿＿＿ the car outside, and my brothers are helping him. My mom is in the kitchen. She (2)＿＿＿ a cake for my grandma''s birthday.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "is washing; makes"}, {"key": "B", "text": "washes; is making"}, {"key": "C", "text": "are washing; is making"}, {"key": "D", "text": "is washing; is making"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Right now（就在現在）表示兩個動作都正在進行，都要用現在進行式。(1) 主詞 my dad 是單數，用 is washing；(2) 主詞 She 是單數，用 is making。', '["Right now 告訴你這些動作是什麼時候發生的？", "兩個空格的主詞各是單數還是複數？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "(1) washes 是現在簡單式，表示習慣，但 Right now 是正在進行的動作。", "A": "(2) makes 是現在簡單式，媽媽此刻正在做蛋糕，要用 is making。", "C": "(1) 主詞是 my dad 一個人，雖然後面提到哥哥們，be 動詞仍要用 is。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-2-19', 'EN-7B-2', 'past-tense', 'My grandparents ＿＿＿ in Tainan ten years ago. Now they live in Taipei.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "living"}, {"key": "B", "text": "lived"}, {"key": "C", "text": "lives"}, {"key": "D", "text": "live"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'ten years ago（十年前）是過去的時間，要用過去式。live 字尾是 e，直接加 d 變成 lived。', '["ten years ago 指的是現在還是過去？", "規則動詞的過去式怎麼變化？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "live 是現在式，但 ten years ago 是過去的時間。", "C": "lives 是第三人稱單數現在式，而且主詞是複數。", "A": "living 前面沒有 be 動詞，不能當動詞。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-2-20', 'EN-7B-2', 'irregular-verb', 'I ＿＿＿ a great movie with my friends last Saturday.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "seed"}, {"key": "B", "text": "see"}, {"key": "C", "text": "saw"}, {"key": "D", "text": "seen"}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'last Saturday（上週六）是過去，要用過去式。see 是不規則動詞，過去式是 saw。', '["last Saturday 表示什麼時候？", "see 的過去式是規則變化嗎？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "see 是現在式，沒有配合過去時間 last Saturday。", "A": "把 see 當成規則動詞加 d，但 see 是不規則動詞。", "D": "seen 是過去分詞，不能單獨當過去式動詞。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-2-21', 'EN-7B-2', 'past-tense', 'I ＿＿＿ very tired yesterday, so I went to bed early.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "am"}, {"key": "B", "text": "was"}, {"key": "C", "text": "is"}, {"key": "D", "text": "were"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'yesterday 是過去的時間，be 動詞要用過去式。主詞 I 的 be 動詞過去式是 was。', '["yesterday 是過去還是現在？", "am 的過去式是什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "am 是現在式，和 yesterday 不合。", "D": "were 用在 you、we、they 或複數主詞，I 要用 was。", "C": "is 是現在式，而且不配主詞 I。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-2-22', 'EN-7B-2', 'dialogue-response', 'A: Did you have a good weekend?
B: ＿＿＿', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Yes, I did. I went hiking with my dad."}, {"key": "B", "text": "No, I wasn''t. I was at home all day."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Yes, I do. I go hiking with my dad."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Yes, I will. I''ll go hiking with my dad."}]'::jsonb, 'A', '問句用 Did，問的是過去的週末，回答也要用 did，後面補充的內容也用過去式 went。', '["問句用了哪個助動詞？", "回答時要和問句用相同的時態。"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "do 和 go 是現在式，但問的是已經過去的週末。", "B": "問句用助動詞 Did，不能用 be 動詞 wasn''t 回答。", "D": "will 是未來式，問的是過去的事。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-2-23', 'EN-7B-2', 'past-tense', 'Lisa ＿＿＿ to the party last night. She stayed home.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "wasn''t go"}, {"key": "B", "text": "didn''t went"}, {"key": "C", "text": "doesn''t go"}, {"key": "D", "text": "didn''t go"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '她待在家裡，所以昨晚沒有去派對。過去式否定用 didn''t，後面接原形動詞 go：didn''t go。', '["last night 要用什麼時態？", "didn''t 後面的動詞要用什麼形式？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "doesn''t 是現在式，和 last night 不合。", "B": "didn''t 已經表示過去，後面的動詞要用原形 go，不能用 went。", "A": "go 是一般動詞，否定要用 didn''t，不能用 be 動詞 wasn''t。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-2-24', 'EN-7B-2', 'past-tense', 'The baby ＿＿＿ a lot last night, so his parents didn''t sleep well.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "cryed"}, {"key": "B", "text": "crys"}, {"key": "C", "text": "cries"}, {"key": "D", "text": "cried"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'last night 要用過去式。cry 是「子音＋y」結尾，要把 y 改成 i 再加 ed：cried。', '["last night 要用什麼時態？", "動詞以「子音＋y」結尾時，加 ed 前要怎麼改？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "忘了「子音＋y」結尾要先把 y 改成 i 再加 ed。", "C": "cries 是現在式，和 last night 不合。", "B": "crys 拼法錯誤，而且也不是過去式。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-2-25', 'EN-7B-2', 'irregular-verb', 'Ms. Lee ＿＿＿ us a funny story in class yesterday.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "tells"}, {"key": "B", "text": "told"}, {"key": "C", "text": "telled"}, {"key": "D", "text": "tell"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'yesterday 要用過去式。tell 是不規則動詞，過去式是 told，不是加 ed。', '["yesterday 表示什麼時態？", "tell 的過去式是規則變化嗎？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "把 tell 當成規則動詞加 ed，但 tell 的過去式是 told。", "A": "tells 是現在式，和 yesterday 不合。", "D": "tell 是原形，沒有配合過去時間。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-2-26', 'EN-7B-2', 'irregular-verb', 'Mike ＿＿＿ a bad cold last week, but he''s fine now.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "haved"}, {"key": "B", "text": "had"}, {"key": "C", "text": "has"}, {"key": "D", "text": "have"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'last week 是過去，「得了感冒」要用過去式。have 是不規則動詞，過去式是 had。', '["感冒是上週還是現在的事？", "have 的過去式是什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "has 是現在式，但感冒發生在 last week。", "A": "have 是不規則動詞，沒有 haved 這個字。", "D": "have 是原形，而且主詞是第三人稱單數，也不能用 have 當現在式。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-2-27', 'EN-7B-2', 'dialogue-response', 'A: When did you come back from Japan?
B: ＿＿＿', '[{"key": "A", "text": "With my parents."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Two days ago."}, {"key": "C", "text": "By plane."}, {"key": "D", "text": "For five days."}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'When 問「什麼時候」，要回答時間點。Two days ago.（兩天前）說出回來的時間，最合適。', '["問句的疑問詞是什麼？", "When 要用時間點還是時間長度來回答？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "For five days. 是時間長度，回答的是 How long。", "C": "By plane. 是交通方式，回答的是 How。", "A": "With my parents. 是同伴，回答的是 Who / With whom。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-2-28', 'EN-7B-2', 'reading-detail', 'Sunday, October 5
Today I went to the night market with my cousin. We ate stinky tofu and played some games. I won a big teddy bear! At nine, it rained very hard, so we took a taxi home. It was a fun night.

How did the writer go home?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "By bus."}, {"key": "B", "text": "By taxi."}, {"key": "C", "text": "On foot."}, {"key": "D", "text": "By MRT."}]'::jsonb, 'B', '日記寫 it rained very hard, so we took a taxi home.，因為下大雨，所以作者搭計程車回家。', '["找出和「回家」有關的那一句。", "took a taxi 是什麼意思？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "文中沒有提到搭公車。", "C": "下大雨所以沒有走路回家，文中說的是搭計程車。", "D": "文中沒有提到捷運。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-2-29', 'EN-7B-2', 'irregular-verb', 'Last Sunday, I (1)＿＿＿ a long letter to my pen pal in Japan. I also (2)＿＿＿ some photos of Taiwan in the letter. I hope she likes them.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "write; puts"}, {"key": "B", "text": "wrote; put"}, {"key": "C", "text": "writed; put"}, {"key": "D", "text": "wrote; putted"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'Last Sunday 是過去，兩個動詞都要用過去式。write 的過去式是不規則的 wrote；put 的過去式和原形一樣，仍是 put。', '["Last Sunday 表示要用哪一種時態？", "write 和 put 都是不規則動詞，有一個的過去式和原形長得一樣。"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "write 是不規則動詞，過去式是 wrote，不是 writed。", "D": "put 的過去式還是 put，不能加 ted。", "A": "write 和 puts 都是現在式，沒有配合 Last Sunday。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7B-2-30', 'EN-7B-2', 'reading-detail', 'Yesterday, Ken left home at 7:20. He walked to the MRT station in 10 minutes. Then he took the MRT, and the trip took 25 minutes. After he got off the MRT, he walked for 5 more minutes to his school.

What time did Ken get to school?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "8:05"}, {"key": "B", "text": "7:45"}, {"key": "C", "text": "8:00"}, {"key": "D", "text": "7:55"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '把每段時間加起來：走到捷運站 10 分鐘＋搭捷運 25 分鐘＋再走 5 分鐘＝40 分鐘。7:20 再加 40 分鐘是 8:00。', '["Ken 去學校分成哪幾段路？", "把所有段落的分鐘數加起來，再從 7:20 往後算。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "漏算最後走路的 5 分鐘，只算到 35 分鐘。", "B": "漏算第一段走到捷運站的 10 分鐘。", "A": "多加了 5 分鐘，可能把最後的走路時間算了兩次。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-1-19', 'EN-8A-1', 'future-tense', 'My uncle will ＿＿＿ us next week.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "visited"}, {"key": "B", "text": "visits"}, {"key": "C", "text": "visiting"}, {"key": "D", "text": "visit"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'will 是助動詞，後面一定接原形動詞，所以是 will visit。next week 也表示未來。', '["will 後面要接什麼形式的動詞？", "主詞是第三人稱單數，用了 will 以後動詞還要加 s 嗎？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "看到主詞 My uncle 是第三人稱單數就加 s，但 will 後面要用原形。", "A": "visited 是過去式，和 will、next week 不合。", "C": "will 後面不接 V-ing。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-1-20', 'EN-8A-1', 'modal-verb', 'Ann ＿＿＿ speak three languages: Chinese, English, and Japanese.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "can"}, {"key": "B", "text": "is can"}, {"key": "C", "text": "cans"}, {"key": "D", "text": "can to"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'can 表示「能夠、會」，是助動詞，沒有人稱變化，後面直接接原形動詞：Ann can speak...。', '["can 是一般動詞還是助動詞？", "助動詞後面接什麼？會不會因為主詞加 s？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "助動詞 can 不會因為第三人稱單數加 s。", "D": "can 後面直接接原形動詞，不需要 to。", "B": "can 已經是助動詞，前面不能再加 be 動詞。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-1-21', 'EN-8A-1', 'future-tense', 'We are going to ＿＿＿ a party for Mom next Sunday.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "had"}, {"key": "B", "text": "having"}, {"key": "C", "text": "have"}, {"key": "D", "text": "has"}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'be going to 表示「打算、將要」，to 後面要接原形動詞，所以是 are going to have。', '["be going to 的 to 後面接什麼形式？", "主詞 We 之後已經有 are，空格只要填原形。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "has 是第三人稱單數現在式，to 後面要用原形。", "B": "going to 後面不接 V-ing，having 不正確。", "A": "had 是過去式，和 next Sunday 以及 to 都不合。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-1-22', 'EN-8A-1', 'dialogue-response', 'A: What are you going to do this weekend?
B: ＿＿＿', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Yes, I am. I''m very excited about it."}, {"key": "B", "text": "I visited my aunt in Tainan last week."}, {"key": "C", "text": "I''m going to visit my aunt in Tainan."}, {"key": "D", "text": "I visit my aunt in Tainan every day."}]'::jsonb, 'C', '問句用 be going to 問「這個週末打算做什麼」，回答也用 be going to 說出計畫：I''m going to visit my aunt in Tainan.', '["問的是過去、習慣，還是未來的計畫？", "回答時用和問句相同的句型。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "visited 和 last week 是過去式，說的是上週的事，但問的是還沒到的週末。", "A": "What 開頭的問句不能用 Yes 回答。", "D": "every day 是每天的習慣，沒有回答週末的計畫。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-1-23', 'EN-8A-1', 'future-tense', 'Mr. Wu ＿＿＿ in Taipei next year. His family is going to move to Tainan this summer.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "didn''t work"}, {"key": "B", "text": "doesn''t work"}, {"key": "C", "text": "won''t works"}, {"key": "D", "text": "won''t work"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '他們家今年夏天要搬去臺南，所以吳先生明年「將不會」在臺北工作。next year 是未來，否定用 won''t + 原形動詞。', '["next year 是什麼時間？要用什麼時態？", "won''t 後面的動詞要用什麼形式？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "doesn''t work 是現在式，表示現在的習慣，但說的是明年。", "A": "didn''t work 是過去式，和 next year 矛盾。", "C": "won''t 是助動詞，後面要接原形 work，不能加 s。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-1-24', 'EN-8A-1', 'future-tense', 'A: Will Jenny come to the meeting tomorrow?
B: ＿＿＿ She is sick in bed.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "No, she isn''t."}, {"key": "B", "text": "No, she won''t."}, {"key": "C", "text": "No, she doesn''t."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Yes, she will."}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'B 說 Jenny 生病躺在床上，所以明天不會來，要否定回答。問句用 Will，回答也用 will 的否定 won''t。', '["Jenny 現在身體狀況如何？明天會來嗎？", "問句用什麼助動詞，回答就用什麼。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "她生病臥床，說她會來和後面的理由矛盾。", "A": "問句用 Will，回答不能改用 be 動詞 isn''t。", "C": "問句用 Will，回答不能改用 doesn''t。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-1-25', 'EN-8A-1', 'modal-verb', 'You ＿＿＿ talk loudly in the library. Other people are reading.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "mustn''t"}, {"key": "B", "text": "don''t have to"}, {"key": "C", "text": "can"}, {"key": "D", "text": "must"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '圖書館裡有人在看書，所以「不可以」大聲說話，表示禁止要用 mustn''t（must not）。', '["後一句說明了什麼原因？", "表示「禁止、不可以」要用哪個助動詞？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "don''t have to 是「不必」，表示可做可不做，不是禁止。", "D": "must 是「必須」，變成「你必須大聲說話」，意思相反。", "C": "can 是「可以」，和別人在看書的情境矛盾。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-1-26', 'EN-8A-1', 'modal-verb', 'My little brother is only two years old. He ＿＿＿ read or write.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "doesn''t have to"}, {"key": "B", "text": "can''t"}, {"key": "C", "text": "mustn''t"}, {"key": "D", "text": "shouldn''t"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '兩歲的小孩還沒有讀寫的能力，表示「不會、不能」要用 can''t。', '["兩歲小孩做不到這件事，是因為被禁止還是沒有能力？", "表示「能力上做不到」要用哪個助動詞？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "mustn''t 是「禁止」，但讀書寫字不是被禁止的事。", "A": "doesn''t have to 是「不必」，沒有表達出能力不足的意思。", "D": "shouldn''t 是「不應該」，讀寫並不是不應該做的事。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-1-27', 'EN-8A-1', 'dialogue-response', 'A: I have a bad toothache.
B: ＿＿＿', '[{"key": "A", "text": "You should see a dentist."}, {"key": "B", "text": "I''ll be there on time."}, {"key": "C", "text": "You don''t have to brush your teeth."}, {"key": "D", "text": "You must eat more candy."}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'A 說牙齒很痛，合理的建議是 You should see a dentist.（你應該去看牙醫），should 用來給建議。', '["A 遇到了什麼問題？", "給別人建議時常用哪個助動詞？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "牙痛還要多吃糖果，建議不合理。", "C": "牙痛時更需要刷牙，說不必刷牙不合常理。", "B": "I''ll be there on time. 是答應準時到，和牙痛無關。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-1-28', 'EN-8A-1', 'reading-detail', 'Class 801 Field Trip
We will go to the Science Museum this Friday. Please meet at the school gate at 8:00 a.m. You should wear your school uniform. You don''t have to bring lunch. The school will give everyone a lunch box.

Which is TRUE?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "The school will give the students lunch."}, {"key": "B", "text": "The students don''t have to wear school uniforms."}, {"key": "C", "text": "The students will meet at the museum."}, {"key": "D", "text": "The students must bring their lunch."}]'::jsonb, 'A', '通知最後說 The school will give everyone a lunch box.，所以學校會提供午餐。集合地點是校門口；不必帶午餐；應該穿制服。', '["逐一核對集合地點、服裝和午餐三件事。", "You don''t have to bring lunch. 的原因寫在下一句。"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "集合地點是 the school gate（校門口），不是博物館。", "D": "通知說 You don''t have to bring lunch.（不必帶午餐）。", "B": "通知說 You should wear your school uniform.，應該穿制服。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-1-29', 'EN-8A-1', 'modal-verb', 'Mia: Mom, can I go to Amy''s house tonight?
Mom: Yes, but you (1)＿＿＿ finish your homework before you go. That''s our rule.
Mia: OK. Do I have to take the bus there?
Mom: No, you (2)＿＿＿. Dad will drive you.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "must; mustn''t"}, {"key": "B", "text": "must; don''t have to"}, {"key": "C", "text": "can''t; don''t have to"}, {"key": "D", "text": "don''t have to; must"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '(1) 媽媽說 That''s our rule.（這是我們的規定），表示「必須」先寫完作業，用 must。(2) 回答 Do I have to...? 的否定是 No, you don''t have to.（不必），因為爸爸會載她。', '["(1) 後面的 That''s our rule. 表示這件事是必須還是可有可無？", "回答 Do I have to...? 的否定時，要說「不必」還是「禁止」？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "(2) mustn''t 是「禁止」，但搭公車並沒有被禁止，只是爸爸會載她所以不必。", "D": "(1) 有家規要求先寫完作業，不能說 don''t have to（不必）。", "C": "(1) can''t finish 是「不能寫完」，和「寫完才能去」的意思不合。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-1-30', 'EN-8A-1', 'reading-detail', 'Ben: Are you free after school next week, Jason? Let''s play basketball.
Jason: Let me see. I''m going to see the dentist on Tuesday, and I''ll help my mom at her shop on Thursday. On Friday, my family is going to have dinner at Grandpa''s house.
Ben: How about Monday or Wednesday?
Jason: Monday is OK. On Wednesday I have a piano lesson.

When will they probably play basketball?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Thursday"}, {"key": "B", "text": "Wednesday"}, {"key": "C", "text": "Monday"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Tuesday"}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'Jason 星期二看牙醫、星期三上鋼琴課、星期四幫媽媽顧店、星期五去爺爺家吃飯，只有星期一有空，他也說 Monday is OK.，所以他們應該星期一打球。', '["把 Jason 每天的計畫列出來。", "哪一天 Jason 說可以？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "星期二 Jason 要去看牙醫。", "B": "Ben 提議過星期三，但 Jason 那天有鋼琴課。", "A": "星期四 Jason 要去媽媽的店幫忙。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-2-19', 'EN-8A-2', 'comparative', 'In Taiwan, summer is ＿＿＿ than spring.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "hotter"}, {"key": "B", "text": "hoter"}, {"key": "C", "text": "more hot"}, {"key": "D", "text": "hottest"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '有 than 表示兩者比較，用比較級。hot 是「短母音＋單一子音」結尾，要重複 t 再加 er：hotter。', '["句子裡有 than，要用原級、比較級還是最高級？", "hot 加 er 時字尾要不要重複？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "知道加 er，但忘了 hot 要重複字尾 t。", "C": "hot 是單音節形容詞，比較級直接加 er，不用 more。", "D": "hottest 是最高級，有 than 要用比較級。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-2-20', 'EN-8A-2', 'superlative', 'Mount Jade is the ＿＿＿ mountain in Taiwan.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "highest"}, {"key": "B", "text": "most high"}, {"key": "C", "text": "higher"}, {"key": "D", "text": "high"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '玉山在臺灣所有山裡最高，「在某範圍內最…」要用最高級：the highest。前面已經有 the。', '["in Taiwan 表示在一個範圍裡比較，用哪一級？", "high 的最高級怎麼變化？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "higher 是比較級，用在兩者比較，而且通常搭配 than。", "D": "high 是原級，沒有表達「最」的意思。", "B": "high 是單音節字，最高級直接加 est，不用 most。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-2-21', 'EN-8A-2', 'comparative', 'This story is ＿＿＿ than that one. I can''t stop reading it.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "interestinger"}, {"key": "B", "text": "more interesting"}, {"key": "C", "text": "interesting"}, {"key": "D", "text": "most interesting"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '有 than 要用比較級。interesting 是多音節形容詞，比較級要在前面加 more：more interesting。', '["看到 than 要用哪一級？", "長的形容詞（三個音節以上）比較級要怎麼變？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "interesting 是長形容詞，不能直接加 er。", "D": "most interesting 是最高級，有 than 要用比較級。", "C": "interesting 是原級，不能和 than 搭配。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-2-22', 'EN-8A-2', 'as-as', 'My bag is as ＿＿＿ as yours. They both cost NT$500.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "cheap"}, {"key": "B", "text": "more cheap"}, {"key": "C", "text": "cheaper"}, {"key": "D", "text": "cheapest"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '兩個包包價錢一樣，用「as + 原級 + as」表示「和……一樣」，中間要放原級形容詞 cheap。', '["兩個包包的價錢一樣還是不一樣？", "as ... as 中間要放哪一級的形容詞？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "as ... as 中間要放原級，不能放比較級 cheaper。", "D": "cheapest 是最高級，不能放在 as ... as 中間。", "B": "cheap 的比較級是 cheaper，沒有 more cheap，而且 as ... as 中間要用原級。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-2-23', 'EN-8A-2', 'comparative', 'Tom''s English is good, but his sister''s English is even ＿＿＿.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "gooder"}, {"key": "B", "text": "better"}, {"key": "C", "text": "more good"}, {"key": "D", "text": "best"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'even（更加）用來加強比較級。good 的比較級是不規則的 better，所以是 even better（更好）。', '["even 後面通常接哪一級的形容詞？", "good 的比較級是規則變化嗎？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "good 是不規則變化，沒有 gooder 這個字。", "D": "best 是最高級，even 用來修飾比較級。", "C": "good 的比較級是 better，不用 more good。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-2-24', 'EN-8A-2', 'superlative', 'Of all the students in my class, Leo runs ＿＿＿.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "the most fast"}, {"key": "B", "text": "faster"}, {"key": "C", "text": "fast"}, {"key": "D", "text": "the fastest"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Of all the students in my class（在全班同學中）表示三者以上比較，要用最高級 the fastest。', '["Of all the students 表示比較的對象有幾個？", "fast 的最高級怎麼變化？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "faster 是比較級，用在兩者比較，這裡是全班比較。", "C": "fast 是原級，沒有表達「最快」。", "A": "fast 是單音節字，最高級是 fastest，不用 most。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-2-25', 'EN-8A-2', 'superlative', 'In Taiwan, winter is ＿＿＿ season of the year.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "coldest"}, {"key": "B", "text": "colder"}, {"key": "C", "text": "the colder"}, {"key": "D", "text": "the coldest"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'season of the year 表示在一年四季中比較，四季中最冷用最高級，而且最高級前面要加 the：the coldest。', '["一年有幾個季節？是兩者比較還是多者比較？", "最高級前面通常要加什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "colder 是比較級，四季比較要用最高級。", "C": "the colder 用在兩者之中，這裡是四個季節。", "A": "最高級前面少了 the，is coldest season 不合文法。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-2-26', 'EN-8A-2', 'as-as', 'Ken is 165 cm tall, and Paul is 165 cm tall, too. Ken is ＿＿＿ Paul.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "shorter than"}, {"key": "B", "text": "as taller as"}, {"key": "C", "text": "as tall as"}, {"key": "D", "text": "taller than"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '兩人都是 165 公分，一樣高，用「as + 原級 + as」：Ken is as tall as Paul.', '["兩人的身高一樣嗎？", "表示「一樣……」的句型是什麼？中間放哪一級？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "兩人一樣高，不能說 Ken 比較高。", "B": "as ... as 中間要放原級 tall，不能放比較級。", "A": "兩人一樣高，不能說 Ken 比較矮。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-2-27', 'EN-8A-2', 'comparative', 'A: Which is ＿＿＿, a bike or a car?
B: A car, of course.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "fastest"}, {"key": "B", "text": "the fast"}, {"key": "C", "text": "faster"}, {"key": "D", "text": "more fast"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '問句在腳踏車和汽車「兩者」之間比較，用比較級。fast 是單音節字，比較級是 faster。', '["問句裡比較的東西有幾個？", "兩者比較要用比較級還是最高級？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "fastest 是最高級，用在三者以上，這裡只有兩樣東西。", "B": "fast 是原級，加 the 也不能表示比較。", "D": "fast 是單音節字，比較級直接加 er，不用 more。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-2-28', 'EN-8A-2', 'reading-detail', 'Tim is looking at three backpacks in a store. The red one is NT$800. The blue one is NT$600, and it is the lightest of the three. The green one is NT$1,000, and it is the biggest.

Tim wants the cheapest backpack. Which one will he buy?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "The biggest one"}, {"key": "B", "text": "The blue one"}, {"key": "C", "text": "The green one"}, {"key": "D", "text": "The red one"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '三個背包的價錢：紅色 800 元、藍色 600 元、綠色 1,000 元，最便宜的是藍色，所以 Tim 會買藍色的。', '["把三個背包的價錢列出來比較。", "cheapest 是「最便宜」，找價錢最低的。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "紅色 800 元，比藍色的 600 元貴。", "C": "綠色 1,000 元是最貴的。", "A": "最大的是綠色背包，也是最貴的，不符合 Tim 要最便宜的條件。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-2-29', 'EN-8A-2', 'comparative', 'Mia: Excuse me. Which jacket is (1)＿＿＿, the black one or the white one?
Clerk: The black one. It''s NT$1,500, and the white one is only NT$1,200.
Mia: Then I''ll take the white one. It''s (2)＿＿＿, and it looks nice, too.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "more expensive; more cheap"}, {"key": "B", "text": "cheaper; more expensive"}, {"key": "C", "text": "expensiver; cheaper"}, {"key": "D", "text": "more expensive; cheaper"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '店員回答「黑色的，1,500 元，白色的只要 1,200 元」，表示 Mia 問的是哪件比較貴，(1) 用 more expensive。Mia 選白色的，因為它比較便宜，(2) 用 cheaper。', '["店員回答黑色的，並說白色的「只要」1,200 元，Mia 問的是比較貴還是比較便宜？", "expensive 和 cheap 的比較級各怎麼變化？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "把兩個空格的意思弄反了：店員回答黑色，而黑色比較貴。", "C": "expensive 是長形容詞，比較級是 more expensive，沒有 expensiver。", "A": "cheap 是單音節字，比較級是 cheaper，不是 more cheap。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8A-2-30', 'EN-8A-2', 'superlative', 'How to get from Green Town to Blue Lake:
By train: 2 hours, NT$450
By bus: 4 hours, NT$300
By plane: 40 minutes, NT$1,800

Which is TRUE?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "The plane is the fastest, and it is cheaper than the train."}, {"key": "B", "text": "The bus is as fast as the train, but it costs less."}, {"key": "C", "text": "The bus is the cheapest, but it is also the slowest."}, {"key": "D", "text": "The train is faster than the plane, and it costs less."}]'::jsonb, 'C', '比較價錢：公車 300 元最便宜；比較時間：公車 4 小時最久，所以公車最便宜也最慢。飛機 40 分鐘最快；飛機 1,800 元比火車貴；公車 4 小時比火車 2 小時慢。', '["分別比較三種交通方式的「時間」和「價錢」。", "花的時間越長，表示越快還是越慢？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "火車比飛機便宜沒錯，但火車要 2 小時，飛機只要 40 分鐘，飛機比較快。", "A": "飛機最快沒錯，但飛機 1,800 元，火車 450 元，飛機比較貴。", "B": "公車比火車便宜沒錯，但公車要 4 小時，火車 2 小時，兩者速度不一樣。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-1-19', 'EN-8B-1', 'gerund', 'Kevin is good at ＿＿＿ pictures. He wants to be an artist.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "draw"}, {"key": "B", "text": "to draw"}, {"key": "C", "text": "drawing"}, {"key": "D", "text": "draws"}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'be good at 的 at 是介系詞，介系詞後面的動詞要改成動名詞（V-ing），所以要用 drawing。be good at drawing pictures 意思是「擅長畫畫」。', '["空格前面的 at 是什麼詞性？", "介系詞後面如果接動詞，要變成什麼形式？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "以為空格前面有 is 就可以直接接原形動詞，忽略了 at 是介系詞，後面要接 V-ing。", "B": "把 to 不定詞和介系詞後的動名詞搞混了；at 後面不能再接 to V。", "D": "以為主詞 Kevin 是第三人稱單數就要加 s，但這裡空格在介系詞 at 後面，不是句子的主要動詞。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-1-20', 'EN-8B-1', 'infinitive', 'Joy hopes ＿＿＿ her grandparents in Japan this summer.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "visited"}, {"key": "B", "text": "visit"}, {"key": "C", "text": "to visit"}, {"key": "D", "text": "visiting"}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'hope（希望）後面接動詞時，要用不定詞 to V，所以是 hopes to visit her grandparents，意思是「希望今年夏天去日本看爺爺奶奶」。', '["hope 後面接另一個動詞時，要用 to V 還是 V-ing？", "句子裡已經有一個動詞 hopes，第二個動詞不能直接用原形。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "句子已經有動詞 hopes，第二個動詞不能直接接原形，要用 to visit。", "D": "把 hope 和 enjoy 這類接 V-ing 的動詞搞混了；hope 要接 to V。", "A": "看到動作還沒發生卻用了過去式；而且 hope 後面要接 to V，不能接過去式動詞。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-1-21', 'EN-8B-1', 'gerund', 'Would you mind ＿＿＿ the window? It''s hot in here.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "to open"}, {"key": "B", "text": "open"}, {"key": "C", "text": "opened"}, {"key": "D", "text": "opening"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'mind（介意）後面接動詞要用動名詞 V-ing。Would you mind opening the window? 是很有禮貌的請求，意思是「你介意打開窗戶嗎？」。', '["mind 是「介意」的意思，它後面接動詞的習慣用法是哪一種？", "和 enjoy、finish 一樣，mind 後面接的動詞要加 -ing 嗎？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "以為 Would you 後面都接原形動詞，但這裡原形動詞是 mind，第二個動詞 open 要改成 V-ing。", "A": "把 mind 和 want、would like 這類接 to V 的動詞搞混了；mind 後面要接 V-ing。", "C": "以為 Would 是過去式所以後面也要用過去式，但 mind 後面要接 V-ing。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-1-22', 'EN-8B-1', 'infinitive', 'It''s ten o''clock. It''s time ＿＿＿ to bed, kids.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "to go"}, {"key": "B", "text": "go"}, {"key": "C", "text": "going"}, {"key": "D", "text": "went"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'It''s time to + 原形動詞 表示「該做某事的時候了」，所以要用 to go。It''s time to go to bed. 意思是「該上床睡覺了」。', '["「該是做……的時候了」英文怎麼說？", "It''s time 後面接動詞時，要先加哪一個小字？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "句子已經有動詞 is（It''s），go 不能直接放在 time 後面，要用 to go。", "C": "把 It''s time to V 記成接 V-ing 了；這個句型要用不定詞。", "D": "說的是現在該去睡覺，不是過去；而且 It''s time 後面要接 to V，不能接過去式。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-1-23', 'EN-8B-1', 'gerund', 'I''m tired of ＿＿＿ the same lunch every day. Let''s try something new.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "eat"}, {"key": "B", "text": "eating"}, {"key": "C", "text": "ate"}, {"key": "D", "text": "to eat"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'be tired of 表示「對……感到厭倦」，of 是介系詞，介系詞後面的動詞要用 V-ing，所以是 tired of eating the same lunch（每天吃一樣的午餐吃膩了）。', '["be tired of 的 of 是什麼詞性？", "介系詞後面接動詞的規則和 be good at 一樣嗎？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "看到前面有 I''m 就以為接原形，忽略了 of 是介系詞，後面要接 V-ing。", "D": "以為兩個動詞之間要用 to 連接，但 of 是介系詞，後面要接 V-ing 而不是 to V。", "C": "以為每天吃的事情是過去發生的就用過去式；介系詞後面不能接過去式動詞。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-1-24', 'EN-8B-1', 'infinitive', 'I can''t decide what ＿＿＿ for Mom''s birthday. Can you give me some ideas?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "buy"}, {"key": "B", "text": "buying"}, {"key": "C", "text": "to buy"}, {"key": "D", "text": "bought"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '「疑問詞 + to V」可以當名詞用，例如 what to buy（要買什麼）、how to do（怎麼做）。decide what to buy for Mom''s birthday 意思是「決定要買什麼給媽媽當生日禮物」。', '["what 後面接動詞，可以組成「要……什麼」的片語。", "想想 how to swim、where to go 這類片語的結構。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "把「疑問詞 + to V」記成「疑問詞 + V-ing」；what 後面要接 to V。", "A": "what 後面直接接原形 buy 缺少主詞，不是完整的用法，要用 what to buy。", "D": "以為買東西的動作已經發生，但說話者還沒決定要買什麼，而且這裡要用 what to buy 的結構。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-1-25', 'EN-8B-1', 'infinitive', 'Remember ＿＿＿ the lights when you leave the classroom. We need to save energy.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "turning off"}, {"key": "B", "text": "to turn off"}, {"key": "C", "text": "turned off"}, {"key": "D", "text": "turn off"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'remember to V 表示「記得要去做（還沒做的事）」，remember V-ing 表示「記得曾經做過某事」。這句是提醒離開教室時要關燈，動作還沒發生，所以用 to turn off。', '["關燈這件事是已經做了，還是離開教室時才要去做？", "remember to V 和 remember V-ing 的意思有什麼不同？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "remember V-ing 是「記得做過某事」，但關燈是之後才要做的事，要用 remember to V。", "D": "句子的動詞已經是 Remember，第二個動詞不能直接用原形，要用 to turn off。", "C": "以為提醒的是已經做完的事而用過去式；remember 後面不能接過去式動詞。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-1-26', 'EN-8B-1', 'dialogue-response', 'A: Would you mind turning down the TV? I''m studying.
B: ＿＿＿ I''ll do it right now.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Not at all."}, {"key": "B", "text": "No, thanks."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Yes, please."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Yes, I would like."}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Would you mind + V-ing? 字面意思是「你介意……嗎？」，答應對方時要說「不介意」，常用 Not at all.（一點也不介意）。B 後面說 I''ll do it right now.（我馬上做），表示答應，所以選 Not at all.', '["mind 是「介意」，對方問「你介意把電視轉小聲嗎？」", "如果願意幫忙，應該回答「介意」還是「不介意」？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "Yes, please. 是接受別人提供東西或幫忙時說的，不能用來回答 Would you mind…?", "D": "Yes, I would like. 本身文法不完整（like 後面少了受詞），也不是回答 Would you mind 的說法。", "B": "No, thanks. 是拒絕別人好意時說的，不能用來答應對方的請求。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-1-27', 'EN-8B-1', 'reading-detail', 'Hi, I''m Ivy. Last summer, I learned to swim. At first, I was afraid of putting my face into the water. My coach told me not to worry and taught me to breathe slowly. After two weeks of practicing, I could swim 25 meters. Now I enjoy swimming with my friends every weekend.

What was Ivy afraid of at first?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Swimming 25 meters"}, {"key": "B", "text": "Talking to her coach"}, {"key": "C", "text": "Swimming with her friends"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Putting her face into the water"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '文中說 At first, I was afraid of putting my face into the water.（一開始我害怕把臉放進水裡），所以答案是把臉放進水裡。游 25 公尺是練習兩週後做到的事，和朋友游泳是她現在喜歡的事。', '["找出文章裡 At first 那一句。", "afraid of 後面接的是什麼動作？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "和朋友游泳是 Ivy 現在每週末喜歡做的事（enjoy swimming），不是一開始害怕的事。", "B": "文中教練只是叫她不要擔心，並沒有說她害怕和教練說話。", "A": "游 25 公尺是她練習兩週後的成果，不是一開始害怕的事。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-1-28', 'EN-8B-1', 'reading-main-idea', 'Library Notice
Starting next Monday, students can borrow up to five books at a time. Please remember to return them within two weeks. Eating and drinking are not allowed in the library. Talking on the phone is not allowed, either. Thank you for helping keep the library a quiet place to study.

What is this notice mainly about?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "The library rules for students"}, {"key": "B", "text": "New books in the library"}, {"key": "C", "text": "How to write a book report"}, {"key": "D", "text": "A reading contest next Monday"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '公告說明一次能借幾本書、要在兩週內還書、不能飲食、不能講電話，這些都是使用圖書館的規定，所以主旨是「學生使用圖書館的規則」。', '["公告裡的每一句都在告訴學生什麼？", "借書、還書、不能吃東西、不能講電話，這些可以合稱為什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "公告沒有提到怎麼寫讀書心得，只提到借書和使用圖書館的規定。", "B": "公告雖然提到借書，但沒有介紹任何新書。", "D": "next Monday 是新借書規定開始的日子，不是閱讀比賽。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-1-29', 'EN-8B-1', 'infinitive', 'Last year, Grandpa''s doctor told him (1)＿＿＿ smoking. It wasn''t easy, but Grandpa finally did it. Now he is much healthier, and he spends an hour (2)＿＿＿ in the park every morning.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "stop; walk"}, {"key": "B", "text": "to stop; walking"}, {"key": "C", "text": "to stop; to walk"}, {"key": "D", "text": "stopping; walking"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '(1) tell + 人 + to V 表示「告訴某人去做某事」，所以是 told him to stop smoking（叫他戒菸），stop 後面接 V-ing 表示停止做某事。(2) spend + 時間 + V-ing 表示「花時間做某事」，所以是 spends an hour walking。', '["(1) 醫生「叫爺爺去做」某事，tell 後面接人之後要接什麼形式的動詞？", "(2)「花多少時間做某事」英文是 spend + 時間 + 哪一種動詞形式？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "tell + 人 後面要接 to V，不能接 V-ing；(1) 要用 to stop。", "C": "spend + 時間 後面要接 V-ing，不能接 to V；(2) 要用 walking。", "A": "tell + 人 後面不能直接接原形動詞，spend + 時間 後面也不能接原形動詞。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-1-30', 'EN-8B-1', 'reading-detail', 'Ben used to spend three hours playing video games every night. Last month, his parents asked him to change this habit. Now Ben stops playing games at nine and reads for half an hour before going to bed. Yesterday, on his way home, he stopped to buy a new comic book. He plans to finish reading it this weekend.

Which is TRUE about Ben?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "He doesn''t play video games at all now."}, {"key": "B", "text": "He read the whole new comic book yesterday."}, {"key": "C", "text": "His parents told him to play games for three hours."}, {"key": "D", "text": "He bought a comic book on his way home yesterday."}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'stop V-ing 是「停止做某事」，stop to V 是「停下來去做另一件事」。文中 he stopped to buy a new comic book 表示他昨天回家途中停下來去買漫畫，所以 D 正確。他只是九點停止玩遊戲，並沒有完全不玩；漫畫打算週末看完；父母是要他改掉每晚玩三小時的習慣。', '["注意 stops playing 和 stopped to buy 的意思不一樣。", "stopped to buy 是「停止買」還是「停下來去買」？", "plans to finish reading it this weekend 表示漫畫看完了沒？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "文中說他九點停止玩遊戲（stops playing games at nine），表示他還是會玩，只是每天限制時間，不是完全不玩。", "B": "文中說他打算這個週末看完（plans to finish reading it this weekend），昨天只是買了書。", "C": "每晚玩三小時是他以前的習慣，父母是要他改掉這個習慣，不是叫他玩三小時。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-2-19', 'EN-8B-2', 'conjunction', 'Which do you like better, cats ＿＿＿ dogs?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "but"}, {"key": "B", "text": "so"}, {"key": "C", "text": "or"}, {"key": "D", "text": "and"}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'Which do you like better 是在問「兩者之中比較喜歡哪一個」，要在兩個選項之間做選擇，所以用表示「或者」的 or：cats or dogs（貓還是狗）。', '["這句是要對方「兩個都選」還是「選其中一個」？", "表示「或者、還是」的連接詞是哪一個？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "and 表示「和」，是把兩者加在一起；但 Which…better 是要對方二選一，要用 or。", "A": "but 表示前後語意相反，cats 和 dogs 之間沒有轉折的關係。", "B": "so 表示「所以」，用來連接因果關係的兩個句子，不能連接兩個選項。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-2-20', 'EN-8B-2', 'conjunction', 'It was very cold this morning, ＿＿＿ I put on my coat.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "because"}, {"key": "B", "text": "or"}, {"key": "C", "text": "so"}, {"key": "D", "text": "but"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '前半句「今天早上很冷」是原因，後半句「我穿上外套」是結果，連接「原因 → 結果」要用 so（所以）。', '["「很冷」和「穿外套」之間是什麼關係？", "哪一個連接詞後面接的是「結果」？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "but 表示轉折，但天冷穿外套是很合理的結果，前後沒有相反的意思。", "B": "or 表示「或者」，不能連接原因和結果。", "A": "because 後面要接原因，但「我穿上外套」是結果，不是原因。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-2-21', 'EN-8B-2', 'tag-question', 'This is your pencil case, ＿＿＿?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "is it"}, {"key": "B", "text": "isn''t it"}, {"key": "C", "text": "doesn''t it"}, {"key": "D", "text": "isn''t this"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '附加問句的規則是「前肯定、後否定」，而且主詞 this 在附加問句中要改用代名詞 it。前句動詞是 is，所以附加問句是 isn''t it。', '["前面的句子是肯定句還是否定句？", "附加問句裡的主詞 this / that 要換成哪個代名詞？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "前句是肯定句，附加問句要用否定，所以不能用 is it。", "D": "附加問句裡的 this 要改成代名詞 it，不能照抄 this。", "C": "前句的動詞是 be 動詞 is，附加問句要用 isn''t，不能用助動詞 does。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-2-22', 'EN-8B-2', 'tag-question', 'Mary can swim very well, ＿＿＿?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "can she"}, {"key": "B", "text": "isn''t she"}, {"key": "C", "text": "doesn''t she"}, {"key": "D", "text": "can''t she"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '前句有助動詞 can，而且是肯定句，附加問句要用否定的 can''t；主詞 Mary 是女生，改成代名詞 she，所以是 can''t she。', '["前句裡有沒有助動詞？", "肯定句後面的附加問句要用肯定還是否定？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "前句是肯定句，附加問句要用否定 can''t，不能用 can。", "C": "前句已經有助動詞 can，附加問句要沿用 can，不能改用 does。", "B": "前句沒有 be 動詞，而是助動詞 can，附加問句不能用 isn''t。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-2-23', 'EN-8B-2', 'conjunction', 'Ken didn''t go to school today ＿＿＿ he had a high fever.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "so"}, {"key": "B", "text": "because"}, {"key": "C", "text": "until"}, {"key": "D", "text": "but"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '後半句「他發高燒」是「沒去上學」的原因，表示原因的連接詞是 because（因為）。', '["發高燒和沒去上學，哪一個是原因、哪一個是結果？", "空格後面接的是原因還是結果？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "so 後面要接結果，但「發高燒」是原因，順序反了。", "D": "but 表示轉折，但發燒所以沒上學很合理，沒有相反的意思。", "C": "until 表示「直到」，「沒去上學直到他發燒」意思不通。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-2-24', 'EN-8B-2', 'conjunction', 'Please wait here ＿＿＿ I come back. Don''t go anywhere.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "so"}, {"key": "B", "text": "until"}, {"key": "C", "text": "although"}, {"key": "D", "text": "because"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'until 表示「直到……為止」。Please wait here until I come back. 意思是「請在這裡等，直到我回來」，後面的 Don''t go anywhere. 也支持這個意思。', '["說話者要對方在這裡等多久？", "哪一個連接詞有「直到……為止」的意思？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "because 表示原因，「因為我回來所以在這裡等」意思不通。", "A": "so 表示結果，「在這裡等，所以我回來」意思不通。", "C": "although 表示「雖然」，前後要有相反的意思，這句沒有轉折。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-2-25', 'EN-8B-2', 'tag-question', 'There is a cat under the table, ＿＿＿?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "is there"}, {"key": "B", "text": "isn''t it"}, {"key": "C", "text": "doesn''t it"}, {"key": "D", "text": "isn''t there"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'There is / There are 句型的附加問句，主詞要沿用 there。前句是肯定的 There is，附加問句用否定的 isn''t there。', '["There is 句型的附加問句，主詞要用 it 還是 there？", "前句是肯定句，附加問句要肯定還是否定？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "There is 句型的附加問句主詞要用 there，不能改成 it。", "A": "前句是肯定句，附加問句要用否定，不能用 is there。", "C": "前句用的是 be 動詞 is，附加問句不能改用 does；主詞也要用 there。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-2-26', 'EN-8B-2', 'tag-question', 'Your brother never eats vegetables, ＿＿＿?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "did he"}, {"key": "B", "text": "is he"}, {"key": "C", "text": "doesn''t he"}, {"key": "D", "text": "does he"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'never（從不）帶有否定意思，所以前句其實是否定句，附加問句要用肯定。動詞 eats 是現在簡單式第三人稱單數，所以用 does he。', '["never 這個字有沒有否定的意思？", "前句算否定句的話，附加問句要用肯定還是否定？", "eats 是一般動詞，附加問句要用哪個助動詞？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "沒注意到 never 已經表示否定，前句是否定句，附加問句要用肯定的 does he。", "B": "前句的動詞是一般動詞 eats，附加問句要用助動詞 does，不能用 be 動詞 is。", "A": "前句是現在簡單式（eats），附加問句要用 does，不能用過去式 did。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-2-27', 'EN-8B-2', 'dialogue-response', 'A: You aren''t hungry, are you?
B: ＿＿＿ I just had a big lunch.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "No, I am."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Yes, I am."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Yes, I''m not."}, {"key": "D", "text": "No, I''m not."}]'::jsonb, 'D', '回答附加問句時，看「事實」決定 Yes 或 No：事實是肯定就說 Yes, I am.，事實是否定就說 No, I''m not.。B 剛吃完一頓大餐，所以「不餓」，要回答 No, I''m not.。', '["B 剛吃了一頓大午餐，他現在餓不餓？", "英文回答時，Yes 後面一定接肯定，No 後面一定接否定。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "Yes, I am. 表示「我餓」，但 B 剛吃完大餐，和後面的話矛盾。", "A": "英文的 No 後面一定要接否定句，No, I am. 前後不一致。", "C": "英文的 Yes 後面一定要接肯定句，Yes, I''m not. 前後不一致；這是照中文「對，我不餓」直譯的錯誤。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-2-28', 'EN-8B-2', 'reading-detail', 'Dear Ms. Wu,
I''m writing to tell you that I can''t join the speech contest next Friday. I practiced a lot, but I hurt my leg when I played basketball last weekend, so I have to go to the hospital that day. I''m really sorry. If you need someone else, my classmate Eric is a good speaker, and he is free next Friday.
Best,
Andy

Why can''t Andy join the speech contest?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "He has to go to the hospital that day."}, {"key": "B", "text": "He didn''t practice enough."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Eric wants to take his place."}, {"key": "D", "text": "He has a basketball game that day."}]'::jsonb, 'A', '信中說 I hurt my leg…, so I have to go to the hospital that day.（我腿受傷，所以那天要去醫院），so 後面接的是結果，所以 Andy 不能參加比賽是因為那天要去醫院。', '["找出 so 那一句，so 前面是原因、後面是結果。", "that day 指的是哪一天？那天 Andy 要去哪裡？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "信中說 I practiced a lot（我練習很多），所以不是因為練習不夠。", "D": "打籃球是上週末受傷的原因，信中沒有說比賽那天有籃球比賽。", "C": "推薦 Eric 是 Andy 自己提出的建議，不是 Eric 想取代他。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-2-29', 'EN-8B-2', 'conjunction', 'Lucy was very nervous before the piano contest. (1)＿＿＿ she practiced every day, she was still afraid of making mistakes. Her teacher said, "Take a deep breath, (2)＿＿＿ you will feel better." Lucy did, and she played very well.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "If; or"}, {"key": "B", "text": "Although; but"}, {"key": "C", "text": "Because; or"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Although; and"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '(1)「每天練習」和「還是怕出錯」意思相反，要用 Although（雖然）；注意 although 和 but 不能同時出現在同一句。(2)「祈使句, and + 結果」表示「做了某事，就會……」：深呼吸，你就會覺得好一點，所以用 and。', '["(1) 每天練習卻還是害怕，前後意思是順接還是相反？", "(2)「祈使句, and…」和「祈使句, or…」意思有什麼不同？", "深呼吸之後會覺得比較好，還是不深呼吸才會覺得比較好？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "(1) 練習和害怕之間是相反關係，不是因果；(2) 用 or 會變成「深呼吸，否則你會覺得比較好」，意思不通。", "B": "(2) but 表示轉折，「深呼吸，但是你會覺得比較好」語意不合，祈使句後接好結果要用 and。", "A": "(1)「如果她每天練習，她還是怕」不合文意，前面說的是事實；(2) or 表示「否則」，也不合理。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-8B-2-30', 'EN-8B-2', 'tag-question', 'Mia: You didn''t go to the concert last night, (1)＿＿＿?
Leo: (2)＿＿＿ I went with my sister. The singer was great!
Mia: Lucky you! I had to stay home and study for a test.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "didn''t you; Yes, I did."}, {"key": "B", "text": "did you; Yes, I did."}, {"key": "C", "text": "did you; No, I didn''t."}, {"key": "D", "text": "did you; No, I did."}]'::jsonb, 'B', '(1) 前句是否定句（didn''t go），附加問句要用肯定的 did you。(2) Leo 接著說「我和姊姊一起去了」，事實是「有去」，所以要用 Yes, I did.；英文回答只看事實，Yes 接肯定、No 接否定。', '["(1) 前句是肯定句還是否定句？", "(2) Leo 昨晚到底有沒有去演唱會？", "英文回答 Yes 或 No，是看問題的語氣還是看事實？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "前句已經是否定句，附加問句要用肯定 did you，不能用 didn''t you。", "C": "照中文「對，我沒去」的習慣回答，但 Leo 後面說他和姊姊去了，事實是有去，要說 Yes, I did.", "D": "英文的 No 後面一定接否定，No, I did. 前後矛盾。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-1-19', 'EN-9A-1', 'present-perfect', 'My sister has ＿＿＿ that movie three times. She really loves it.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "saw"}, {"key": "B", "text": "see"}, {"key": "C", "text": "seen"}, {"key": "D", "text": "seeing"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '現在完成式的結構是 have / has + 過去分詞（p.p.）。see 的三態是 see – saw – seen，過去分詞是 seen，所以是 has seen（已經看過三次）。', '["空格前面有 has，這是什麼時態的記號？", "see 的三態變化是什麼？過去式和過去分詞一樣嗎？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "saw 是過去式，不是過去分詞；has 後面要接過去分詞 seen。", "B": "has 後面不能接原形動詞，現在完成式要用過去分詞。", "D": "has + V-ing 不是正確的時態結構；現在完成式要用 has + p.p.。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-1-20', 'EN-9A-1', 'since-for', 'Amy and I have been good friends ＿＿＿ 2020.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "for"}, {"key": "B", "text": "ago"}, {"key": "C", "text": "in"}, {"key": "D", "text": "since"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'since 後面接「開始的時間點」，for 後面接「一段時間」。2020 是一個時間點，表示從 2020 年到現在一直是朋友，所以用 since。', '["2020 是「一個時間點」還是「一段時間」？", "表示「自從……以來」的字是哪一個？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "for 後面要接一段時間（例如 for six years），2020 是時間點，要用 since。", "B": "ago 要放在一段時間的後面（例如 six years ago），而且不能和現在完成式連用。", "C": "in 2020 表示過去某個時間，要配合過去式；現在完成式表示到現在的持續，要用 since。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null)
on conflict (id) do update set unit_id = excluded.unit_id, concept = excluded.concept, stem = excluded.stem, options = excluded.options, answer = excluded.answer, explanation = excluded.explanation, hints = excluded.hints, wrong_reasons = excluded.wrong_reasons, difficulty = excluded.difficulty, listen_script = excluded.listen_script, exam_part = excluded.exam_part;
B: ＿＿＿ I''ve never been to a cold place in winter.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Yes, I did."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Yes, I have."}, {"key": "C", "text": "No, I haven''t."}, {"key": "D", "text": "No, I didn''t."}]'::jsonb, 'C', '用 Have you…? 問的問題，要用 have 回答：Yes, I have. 或 No, I haven''t.。B 後面說他從來沒在冬天去過寒冷的地方，表示沒看過雪，所以回答 No, I haven''t.', '["問句用的助動詞是 Have 還是 Did？", "B 說他從來沒去過寒冷的地方，那他看過雪嗎？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "Yes, I have. 表示看過雪，和後面「從來沒去過寒冷地方」矛盾。", "A": "問句用 Have，回答要用 have，不能用 did；而且意思也和後面矛盾。", "D": "意思雖然是「沒有」，但問句用 Have，回答也要用 haven''t，不能用 didn''t。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-1-23', 'EN-9A-1', 'present-perfect', 'Oh no! I ＿＿＿ my keys, so I can''t open the door now.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "am losing"}, {"key": "B", "text": "will lose"}, {"key": "C", "text": "lose"}, {"key": "D", "text": "have lost"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '現在完成式可以表示「過去發生的動作，對現在造成影響」。鑰匙弄丟了，所以現在開不了門，要用 have lost（已經弄丟了）。', '["弄丟鑰匙是已經發生還是還沒發生的事？", "這件事對「現在」有什麼影響？哪一種時態能表達這種關係？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "lose 是現在簡單式，表示習慣或常態，不能表示「已經弄丟、所以現在開不了門」。", "B": "will lose 表示未來才會弄丟，但現在已經開不了門了，鑰匙早就丟了。", "A": "am losing 表示正在進行，弄丟鑰匙不是一直在進行的動作。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-1-24', 'EN-9A-1', 'since-for', 'Tom has lived in this town since he ＿＿＿ ten years old.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "was"}, {"key": "B", "text": "will be"}, {"key": "C", "text": "is"}, {"key": "D", "text": "has been"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'since 後面如果接一個句子，那個句子說的是「開始的時間點」，屬於過去的事，要用過去式。Tom 從十歲開始住在這裡，所以是 since he was ten years old。', '["since 後面的句子說的是「開始的時間點」，那是過去、現在還是未來？", "主要句子用現在完成式，since 子句通常用什麼時態？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "since 後面的句子表示過去開始的時間，不能用現在式 is。", "D": "since 後面表示「某個過去時間點」，要用過去式，不能用現在完成式。", "B": "從某時開始住到現在，起點一定在過去，不能用未來式。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-1-25', 'EN-9A-1', 'since-for', 'I bought this watch five years ago, and I still wear it. That means I ＿＿＿ this watch for five years.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "bought"}, {"key": "B", "text": "have had"}, {"key": "C", "text": "have bought"}, {"key": "D", "text": "had"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '「買」是一瞬間就結束的動作，不能持續五年，所以不能說 have bought…for five years。要表示「擁有這支錶已經五年」，要用可以持續的動詞 have 的現在完成式：have had。', '["「買東西」這個動作可以一直持續五年嗎？", "要表示「擁有某物一段時間到現在」，可以用哪個動詞？", "這件事一直持續到現在，要用什麼時態？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "buy 是瞬間動作，不能和表示持續的 for five years 連用。", "D": "had 是過去式，表示過去擁有但現在可能沒有了；題目說現在還在戴，要用現在完成式。", "A": "bought 是瞬間動作的過去式，不能接 for five years 表示持續到現在。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-1-26', 'EN-9A-1', 'present-perfect', 'A: Is dinner ready?
B: Not yet. Dad hasn''t finished cooking ＿＿＿.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "yet"}, {"key": "B", "text": "already"}, {"key": "C", "text": "ago"}, {"key": "D", "text": "ever"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'yet 用在現在完成式的否定句和疑問句，表示「還（沒）」；already 用在肯定句，表示「已經」。這句是否定句 hasn''t finished，而且前面說 Not yet，所以用 yet。', '["這句是肯定句還是否定句？", "already 和 yet 分別用在什麼樣的句子裡？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "already 通常用在肯定句表示「已經」，這句是否定句「還沒煮完」，要用 yet。", "D": "ever 表示「曾經」，用來問經驗，不能放在句尾表示「還沒」。", "C": "ago 要接在一段時間後面（例如 two hours ago），而且不和現在完成式連用。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-1-27', 'EN-9A-1', 'reading-detail', 'Hello, I''m Sam. I have collected stamps since I was eight. So far, I have collected more than 500 stamps from 30 countries. My favorite one is from Kenya; my uncle sent it to me last year. I have never been to Africa, but I hope to visit Kenya someday.

Which is TRUE about Sam?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "He started collecting stamps last year."}, {"key": "B", "text": "He has visited Kenya with his uncle."}, {"key": "C", "text": "He has only 30 stamps."}, {"key": "D", "text": "He has collected stamps from 30 countries."}]'::jsonb, 'D', '文中說 I have collected more than 500 stamps from 30 countries.（我收集了來自 30 個國家、超過 500 張郵票），所以 A 正確。他從八歲開始收集；從沒去過非洲；肯亞郵票是叔叔去年寄給他的。', '["找出 So far 那一句，500 和 30 分別指什麼？", "Sam 去過肯亞嗎？I have never been to… 是什麼意思？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "文中說 I have never been to Africa（從沒去過非洲），肯亞郵票是叔叔寄來的。", "A": "last year 是叔叔寄郵票的時間；Sam 從八歲就開始收集郵票了。", "C": "30 是國家的數目，郵票有超過 500 張。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-1-28', 'EN-9A-1', 'present-perfect', 'A: How many times ＿＿＿ to Kenting?
B: Twice. I went there with my family last summer and the summer before.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "did you been"}, {"key": "B", "text": "you have been"}, {"key": "C", "text": "have you been"}, {"key": "D", "text": "have you be"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '問「去過某地幾次」可以用現在完成式 How many times have you been to…?。疑問句要把助動詞 have 移到主詞 you 前面，後面接過去分詞 been，所以是 have you been。', '["How many times 後面接疑問句，助動詞要放在主詞前還是後？", "現在完成式是 have + 原形還是 have + 過去分詞？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "疑問句要把 have 放在主詞 you 前面，you have been 是直述句語序。", "A": "did 後面要接原形動詞，不能接過去分詞 been；這是把過去式和現在完成式混在一起。", "D": "have 後面要接過去分詞 been，不能接原形 be。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-1-29', 'EN-9A-1', 'since-for', 'Lily started learning the piano when she was six. She is fourteen now, and she still practices every day. Last year, she also started learning the violin, and she has played in the school orchestra since this September.

Which is TRUE about Lily?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "She joined the school orchestra when she was six."}, {"key": "B", "text": "She has played the piano since last year."}, {"key": "C", "text": "She has learned the violin for eight years."}, {"key": "D", "text": "She has learned the piano for eight years."}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Lily 六歲開始學鋼琴，現在十四歲，14 − 6 = 8，所以她已經學鋼琴八年了：She has learned the piano for eight years.。小提琴是去年才開始學的；她從今年九月起才在管弦樂團演奏。', '["Lily 開始學鋼琴和開始學小提琴，分別是什麼時候？", "從六歲到十四歲，一共經過幾年？", "for 後面接一段時間，since 後面接時間點，把它們和正確的樂器配對。"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "把鋼琴和小提琴弄混了；小提琴是去年才開始學的，八年是學鋼琴的時間。", "B": "鋼琴是六歲開始學的，since last year 是學小提琴的起點。", "A": "六歲是她開始學鋼琴的年紀；她是從今年九月才在學校管弦樂團演奏。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-1-30', 'EN-9A-1', 'present-perfect', 'Ann: Have you finished your science report (1)＿＿＿?
Ben: Yes, I (2)＿＿＿ it last night. Now I''m working on my English homework.
Ann: Wow, you''re fast! I haven''t even started mine.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "already; have finished"}, {"key": "B", "text": "yet; finished"}, {"key": "C", "text": "yet; have finished"}, {"key": "D", "text": "ago; finished"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '(1) 現在完成式的疑問句問「完成了沒？」，句尾用 yet。(2) 句中有明確的過去時間 last night（昨晚），不能用現在完成式，要用過去式 finished。', '["(1) 問別人「做完了沒」，句尾常用哪個字？", "(2) 句子裡有沒有明確的過去時間？", "有 last night、yesterday 這類過去時間時，可以用現在完成式嗎？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "(2) 有明確的過去時間 last night，不能用現在完成式 have finished，要用過去式。", "D": "(1) ago 前面一定要有一段時間（例如 two days ago），而且不和現在完成式連用。", "C": "(1) 用 yet 正確，但 (2) 有 last night，要用過去式 finished，不能用 have finished。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-2-19', 'EN-9A-2', 'passive-voice', 'Many phones ＿＿＿ in this factory every day.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "are making"}, {"key": "B", "text": "make"}, {"key": "C", "text": "is made"}, {"key": "D", "text": "are made"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '手機是「被製造」的，要用被動語態 be + 過去分詞。主詞 Many phones 是複數，every day 表示經常發生，用現在式 are，所以是 are made。', '["手機是自己製造東西，還是被製造出來？", "主詞 Many phones 是單數還是複數？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "make 是主動語態，變成「手機製造東西」，意思不對。", "C": "主詞 Many phones 是複數，be 動詞要用 are，不能用 is。", "A": "are making 是現在進行式的主動語態，表示手機正在做東西，意思不對。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-2-20', 'EN-9A-2', 'passive-tense', 'The window ＿＿＿ by Ben yesterday, so it is cold in the classroom today.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "breaks"}, {"key": "B", "text": "was broken"}, {"key": "C", "text": "is broken"}, {"key": "D", "text": "broke"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'by Ben 表示「被 Ben」，所以要用被動語態；yesterday 表示過去，be 動詞用過去式 was，加上 break 的過去分詞 broken，所以是 was broken。', '["空格後面的 by Ben 是什麼意思？", "yesterday 提示要用什麼時態？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "broke 是主動的過去式，後面接 by Ben 文法不通；窗戶是被 Ben 打破的。", "C": "is broken 是現在式被動，但句中有 yesterday，要用過去式 was。", "A": "breaks 是現在式主動，時態和語態都不對。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-2-21', 'EN-9A-2', 'active-passive', 'Ms. Lin ＿＿＿ this English song to us last week.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "was taught"}, {"key": "B", "text": "teaches"}, {"key": "C", "text": "is taught"}, {"key": "D", "text": "taught"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '林老師是「教」這首歌的人，是主動去做動作，所以用主動語態；last week 表示過去，用 teach 的過去式 taught。', '["林老師是教歌的人，還是被教的人？", "last week 提示要用什麼時態？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "林老師是主動教歌的人，不是被教，不能用被動語態。", "C": "is taught 是被動語態，而且是現在式，時態和語態都不對。", "B": "teaches 是現在式，但句中有 last week，要用過去式。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-2-22', 'EN-9A-2', 'passive-voice', 'Is this classroom ＿＿＿ by the students every day?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "clean"}, {"key": "B", "text": "cleaning"}, {"key": "C", "text": "cleaned"}, {"key": "D", "text": "cleans"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '教室是「被打掃」的，被動語態是 be + 過去分詞。句首已有 be 動詞 Is，空格要填過去分詞 cleaned。', '["教室是打掃的人，還是被打掃的東西？", "被動語態的結構是 be 動詞加上動詞的哪一種形式？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "be 動詞 Is 後面不能接原形動詞 clean。", "B": "Is…cleaning 是進行式，表示教室正在打掃別的東西，意思不對；而且後面有 by the students。", "D": "be 動詞後面不能再接加 s 的一般動詞。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-2-23', 'EN-9A-2', 'passive-tense', 'Books can ＿＿＿ from the school library for two weeks.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "borrow"}, {"key": "B", "text": "be borrowed"}, {"key": "C", "text": "borrowed"}, {"key": "D", "text": "be borrowing"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '書是「被借」的，要用被動語態。有助動詞 can 時，被動語態是 can + be + 過去分詞，所以是 can be borrowed（可以被借兩週）。', '["書會自己去借東西嗎？", "助動詞後面要接原形，被動語態的 be 動詞原形是什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "can borrow 是主動語態，變成「書可以借東西」，意思不對。", "C": "助動詞 can 後面要接原形動詞，不能直接接過去分詞，要先加 be。", "D": "be borrowing 是進行式，不是被動語態。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-2-24', 'EN-9A-2', 'passive-tense', 'The pictures on the wall ＿＿＿ by the art club last year.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "were drawn"}, {"key": "B", "text": "are drawn"}, {"key": "C", "text": "drew"}, {"key": "D", "text": "was drawn"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '畫是「被畫」的，要用被動語態。主詞是 The pictures（複數），last year 表示過去，所以 be 動詞用 were，加上 draw 的過去分詞 drawn：were drawn。', '["主詞是 the pictures 還是 the wall？", "last year 提示要用什麼時態？", "draw 的過去分詞是什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "drew 是主動過去式，畫不會自己畫東西，而且後面有 by the art club。", "D": "主詞是 The pictures（複數），不是 the wall，be 動詞要用 were。", "B": "are drawn 是現在式，但句中有 last year，要用過去式。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-2-25', 'EN-9A-2', 'active-passive', 'The cat ate the fish on the table. → The fish on the table ＿＿＿ by the cat.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "ate"}, {"key": "B", "text": "eaten"}, {"key": "C", "text": "was ate"}, {"key": "D", "text": "was eaten"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '主動改被動：原來的受詞 the fish 變成主詞，動詞改成 be + 過去分詞。原句是過去式 ate，fish 在這裡指一條魚，所以用 was；eat 的過去分詞是 eaten，答案是 was eaten。', '["主動句改成被動句時，時態要不要改變？", "eat 的三態是 eat – ate – ？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "ate 是主動語態，變成「魚吃了東西」，意思不對。", "B": "被動語態少了 be 動詞，只有過去分詞 eaten 不能當句子的動詞。", "C": "被動語態要用過去分詞 eaten，不能用過去式 ate。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-2-26', 'EN-9A-2', 'passive-voice', 'My cousin ＿＿＿ in Kaohsiung in 2012, and he still lives there.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "born"}, {"key": "B", "text": "is born"}, {"key": "C", "text": "was born"}, {"key": "D", "text": "has born"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '「出生」在英文用被動語態 be born 表示。in 2012 是過去的時間，所以用 was born（在 2012 年出生）。', '["英文的「出生」要怎麼說？是主動還是被動？", "in 2012 提示要用什麼時態？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "born 是過去分詞，前面一定要有 be 動詞，不能單獨當動詞。", "B": "出生是過去發生的事，又有 in 2012，要用過去式 was born。", "D": "「出生」要用 be born，has born 不是正確的說法。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-2-27', 'EN-9A-2', 'reading-detail', 'Taipei 101 was finished in 2004. For a few years, it was the tallest building in the world. Every New Year''s Eve, fireworks are shot from the building, and the show is watched by thousands of people. Inside, there is a huge ball. It is used to keep the building safe during strong winds and earthquakes.

What is the huge ball inside Taipei 101 used for?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "To welcome visitors from around the world"}, {"key": "B", "text": "To protect the building from wind and earthquakes"}, {"key": "C", "text": "To show people the time every hour"}, {"key": "D", "text": "To shoot fireworks every New Year''s Eve"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '文中說 Inside, there is a huge ball. It is used to keep the building safe during strong winds and earthquakes.（大球被用來在強風和地震時保護大樓安全），也就是用來保護大樓不受強風和地震影響，所以答案是 A。煙火是從大樓上施放的，和大球無關。', '["找出文中提到 huge ball 的句子。", "be used to + 原形動詞 表示「被用來做……」。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "文中說煙火是從大樓施放的，但沒有說是用大球放煙火。", "C": "文章沒有提到大球用來報時。", "A": "文章沒有提到大球用來歡迎各地來的遊客。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-2-28', 'EN-9A-2', 'passive-tense', 'Sorry, sir. Smoking ＿＿＿ in this restaurant.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "not allowed"}, {"key": "B", "text": "isn''t allowing"}, {"key": "C", "text": "is not allowed"}, {"key": "D", "text": "doesn''t allow"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '抽菸是「被允許」或「不被允許」的事，要用被動語態 be + allowed。這是餐廳現在的規定，用現在式，主詞 Smoking 是動名詞，視為單數，所以是 is not allowed。', '["抽菸是去允許別人，還是被允許？", "動名詞當主詞時，視為單數還是複數？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "doesn''t allow 是主動語態，變成「抽菸不允許……」，意思不對。", "A": "被動語態不能省略 be 動詞，not allowed 前面要有 is。", "B": "isn''t allowing 是進行式的主動語態，意思不對。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-2-29', 'EN-9A-2', 'passive-voice', 'My grandma has a small farm. Every spring, many kinds of vegetables (1)＿＿＿ there. Last Sunday, my family visited her, and we (2)＿＿＿ some tomatoes and carrots. Grandma cooked them for dinner, and they were delicious.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "plant; were picked"}, {"key": "B", "text": "are planted; were picked"}, {"key": "C", "text": "planted; picked"}, {"key": "D", "text": "are planted; picked"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '(1) 蔬菜是「被種」的，要用被動語態；Every spring 表示每年都會發生的事，用現在式，主詞複數，所以是 are planted。(2) 主詞 we 是採蔬菜的人，用主動語態；Last Sunday 表示過去，所以用過去式 picked。', '["(1) 蔬菜是去種東西，還是被種？Every spring 是習慣還是一次的事？", "(2) 主詞 we 是採蔬菜的人，還是被採的東西？", "每一格分別判斷主動或被動，再判斷時態。"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "(1) 蔬菜是被種的，要用被動語態；(2) 我們是去採的人，要用主動語態，兩格都弄反了。", "B": "(1) 正確，但 (2) 的主詞 we 是採的人，不是被採，不能用被動語態。", "C": "(1) 少了 be 動詞，planted 單獨用會變成「蔬菜種了東西」的主動過去式，而且 Every spring 要用現在式。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9A-2-30', 'EN-9A-2', 'reading-detail', 'Lost Cat!
My cat, Lucky, was last seen near Sunshine Park on May 3. He is white with a black tail. He was given to me by my grandpa three years ago, so he means a lot to me. He is very friendly and loves fish. If you find Lucky, please call Tina at 0911-222-333. You will be given a nice gift.

Which is TRUE about Lucky?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "He was a gift from Tina''s grandpa."}, {"key": "B", "text": "He is black with a white tail."}, {"key": "C", "text": "He was found in Sunshine Park on May 3."}, {"key": "D", "text": "He was bought by Tina three years ago."}]'::jsonb, 'A', '文中說 He was given to me by my grandpa three years ago.（三年前爺爺把他送給我），所以 Lucky 是 Tina 爺爺送的禮物，D 正確。Lucky 是白色、尾巴黑色；5 月 3 日是他最後一次被看到（last seen）的日子，不是被找到。', '["找出 was given to me by… 那一句，是誰把貓送給 Tina 的？", "was last seen 和 was found 的意思一樣嗎？", "注意 Lucky 的身體和尾巴分別是什麼顏色。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "文中說貓是爺爺送給 Tina 的（was given to me），不是 Tina 買的。", "B": "把顏色弄反了；文中說 white with a black tail（白色、黑尾巴）。", "C": "was last seen 是「最後一次被看到」，貓目前還沒找到，所以才要張貼尋貓啟事。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-1-19', 'EN-9B-1', 'relative-person', 'I have a friend ＿＿＿ can speak French and Japanese.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "whose"}, {"key": "B", "text": "which"}, {"key": "C", "text": "what"}, {"key": "D", "text": "who"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '先行詞 a friend 是人，空格後面直接接動詞 can speak，關係代名詞在子句裡當主詞，所以用 who。', '["空格前面的名詞是人還是物？", "空格後面缺的是主詞還是所有格？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "which 用來修飾事物或動物，先行詞 a friend 是人，要用 who。", "A": "whose 表示「……的」，後面要接名詞；這裡空格後面接的是動詞 can speak。", "C": "what 本身已經包含先行詞，前面不能再有名詞 a friend。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-1-20', 'EN-9B-1', 'relative-thing', 'This is the cake ＿＿＿ my dad made for my birthday.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "where"}, {"key": "B", "text": "which"}, {"key": "C", "text": "whose"}, {"key": "D", "text": "who"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '先行詞 the cake 是物，空格後面的 my dad made 缺少受詞（爸爸做了什麼），所以用代替事物的關係代名詞 which。', '["先行詞 the cake 是人還是物？", "my dad made 後面是不是少了「做了什麼」？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "who 只能修飾人，cake 是物，要用 which。", "C": "whose 後面要接名詞表示所有關係，這裡後面接的是 my dad made。", "A": "where 用來修飾地點，cake 不是地點。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-1-21', 'EN-9B-1', 'relative-agreement', 'The boy who ＿＿＿ next to me in class is Leo.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "sit"}, {"key": "B", "text": "are sitting"}, {"key": "C", "text": "sits"}, {"key": "D", "text": "sitting"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '關係代名詞 who 代替先行詞 The boy，所以子句的動詞要和 The boy 一致。The boy 是第三人稱單數，現在簡單式動詞要加 s：who sits。', '["who 代替的是哪一個名詞？", "那個名詞是單數還是複數？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "who 代替的是單數的 The boy，現在簡單式動詞要加 s。", "D": "關係子句需要一個完整的動詞，sitting 前面少了 be 動詞。", "B": "The boy 是單數，進行式要用 is sitting，不能用 are。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-1-22', 'EN-9B-1', 'relative-person', 'Ms. Wang is a teacher ＿＿＿ all the students like very much.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "what"}, {"key": "B", "text": "who"}, {"key": "C", "text": "whose"}, {"key": "D", "text": "which"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '先行詞 a teacher 是人，子句 all the students like 少了受詞（學生喜歡的人），用代替人的關係代名詞 who。', '["先行詞 a teacher 是人還是物？", "空格後面 all the students like 少了什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "which 用來修飾事物，a teacher 是人。", "C": "whose 後面要接名詞，這裡後面接的是 all the students like。", "A": "what 不能放在先行詞後面當關係代名詞。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-1-23', 'EN-9B-1', 'relative-thing', 'I live in a house ＿＿＿ door is painted red.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "which"}, {"key": "B", "text": "where"}, {"key": "C", "text": "whose"}, {"key": "D", "text": "who"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '空格後面接名詞 door，表示「房子的門」，是所有關係，要用 whose。whose 可以修飾人，也可以修飾物：a house whose door is painted red（一間門漆成紅色的房子）。', '["空格後面直接接了什麼詞性的字？", "door 和 house 之間是什麼關係？", "表示「……的」的關係代名詞是哪一個？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "which 後面不能直接接名詞 door 表示「它的門」，要用 whose。", "D": "who 只能修飾人，而且後面不能接名詞表示所有關係。", "B": "where 後面要接完整的句子，door is painted red 缺少「誰的門」，要用 whose。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-1-24', 'EN-9B-1', 'relative-agreement', 'The girl who ＿＿＿ long hair is my cousin, Nina.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "having"}, {"key": "B", "text": "has"}, {"key": "C", "text": "have"}, {"key": "D", "text": "is"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'who 代替先行詞 The girl（第三人稱單數），所以子句動詞要用單數形 has。「有長頭髮」英文說 has long hair。', '["who 代替的是單數還是複數的名詞？", "「有長頭髮」要用 be 動詞還是 have？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "The girl 是第三人稱單數，現在式要用 has，不能用 have。", "A": "關係子句需要完整的動詞，having 不能單獨當動詞。", "D": "「有長頭髮」要用 have / has，is long hair 意思變成「是長頭髮」。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-1-25', 'EN-9B-1', 'relative-thing', 'The bus ＿＿＿ goes to the zoo is No. 5. It comes every ten minutes.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "where"}, {"key": "B", "text": "which"}, {"key": "C", "text": "who"}, {"key": "D", "text": "whose"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '先行詞 The bus 是物，空格後面接動詞 goes，關係代名詞當子句的主詞，所以用 which。', '["先行詞是人還是物？", "空格後面接的是動詞還是名詞？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "who 只能修飾人，bus 是物。", "A": "where 用來修飾地點，而且後面要接完整的句子；這裡 goes 前面缺少主詞。", "D": "whose 後面要接名詞，這裡後面接的是動詞 goes。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-1-26', 'EN-9B-1', 'relative-person', 'I know the man. He is talking to my mom. → I know the man ＿＿＿.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "who is talking to my mom"}, {"key": "B", "text": "which is talking to my mom"}, {"key": "C", "text": "whose is talking to my mom"}, {"key": "D", "text": "who he is talking to my mom"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '第二句的 He 指的就是 the man，合併時用關係代名詞 who 取代 He，原來的 He 要刪掉，所以是 who is talking to my mom。', '["第二句的 He 指的是誰？", "用關係代名詞合併兩句時，被取代的代名詞還要留著嗎？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "the man 是人，要用 who，不能用 which。", "C": "whose 後面要接名詞，這裡後面接的是 is talking。", "D": "who 已經代替了 He，子句裡不能再重複寫 he。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-1-27', 'EN-9B-1', 'reading-detail', 'School Notice Board
- Kelly: I''m looking for someone who can teach me to play the guitar on Saturday mornings.
- Tom: I have a bike which I don''t use anymore. It''s free for anyone who needs it.
- Ruby: I need a classmate who can help me with math. I can help you with English, too.

Jack is good at math, and he needs a bike. Which two people should he talk to?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Tom and Ruby"}, {"key": "B", "text": "Kelly and Tom"}, {"key": "C", "text": "Kelly and Ruby"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Kelly, Tom, and Ruby"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Tom 有一台不再用的腳踏車，送給需要的人，Jack 需要腳踏車；Ruby 需要一位能教數學的同學，Jack 擅長數學。Kelly 要找會教吉他的人，和 Jack 無關，所以應該找 Tom 和 Ruby。', '["每個人的留言各自在找什麼樣的人？", "Jack 能提供什麼？又需要什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "Kelly 要找會教吉他的人，文中沒有說 Jack 會彈吉他。", "C": "Kelly 要找的是吉他老師，和 Jack 的需求、專長都無關。", "D": "Kelly 要找的是會教吉他的人，Jack 只符合 Tom 和 Ruby 兩人的留言。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-1-28', 'EN-9B-1', 'relative-agreement', 'The man who ＿＿＿ my bike yesterday was caught by the police this morning.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "steal"}, {"key": "B", "text": "stealing"}, {"key": "C", "text": "stole"}, {"key": "D", "text": "steals"}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'who 代替先行詞 The man，子句裡有 yesterday，偷車是昨天發生的事，所以要用過去式 stole。', '["關係子句裡有沒有表示時間的字？", "偷車是過去、現在還是未來發生的？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "子句有 yesterday，要用過去式，不能用現在式 steals。", "B": "關係子句需要完整的動詞，stealing 不能單獨當動詞。", "A": "子句有 yesterday 要用過去式，而且 The man 是單數，原形 steal 也不對。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-1-29', 'EN-9B-1', 'relative-thing', 'Yesterday I went to a new restaurant (1)＿＿＿ is near my school. The waiter (2)＿＿＿ served us was very kind, and the noodles which I ordered were delicious.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "which; who"}, {"key": "B", "text": "where; who"}, {"key": "C", "text": "which; whose"}, {"key": "D", "text": "who; which"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '(1) 先行詞 a new restaurant 是物，空格後面接動詞 is，當子句主詞，用 which。(2) 先行詞 The waiter 是人，空格後面接動詞 served，當子句主詞，用 who。', '["(1) 和 (2) 的先行詞分別是什麼？是人還是物？", "空格後面直接接動詞，表示關係代名詞在子句裡當什麼？", "where 後面要接完整句子，(1) 後面的 is near my school 有主詞嗎？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "人和物用反了：restaurant 是物要用 which，waiter 是人要用 who。", "C": "(2) whose 後面要接名詞，這裡後面接的是動詞 served。", "B": "(1) where 後面要接完整的句子，但 is near my school 缺少主詞，要用 which。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-1-30', 'EN-9B-1', 'reading-detail', 'Our class took a photo on Sports Day. The tall boy who is holding the cup is Mark; he won the 100-meter race. The girl whose shoes are red is Wendy. She is the one who drew our class flag. The boy who is standing next to Wendy is Ivan. He is holding the flag.

Which is TRUE?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Ivan drew the class flag that he is holding."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Mark is the boy whose shoes are red."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Wendy drew the flag which Ivan is holding."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Ivan is the boy who won the 100-meter race."}]'::jsonb, 'C', '文中說 Wendy is the one who drew our class flag（Wendy 畫了班旗），又說 Ivan is holding the flag（Ivan 拿著班旗），所以 Ivan 拿的旗子是 Wendy 畫的，D 正確。贏得 100 公尺的是 Mark；穿紅鞋的是 Wendy。', '["分別找出 Mark、Wendy、Ivan 的描述。", "whose shoes are red 修飾的是誰？", "誰畫了班旗？誰拿著班旗？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "拿著獎盃、贏得 100 公尺賽跑的是 Mark，不是 Ivan。", "B": "whose shoes are red 修飾的是 Wendy，不是 Mark。", "A": "Ivan 只是拿著班旗，畫班旗的人是 Wendy。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-2-19', 'EN-9B-2', 'indirect-question', 'Do you know who ＿＿＿? She looks like a movie star.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "that girl is"}, {"key": "B", "text": "that girl"}, {"key": "C", "text": "does that girl"}, {"key": "D", "text": "is that girl"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '間接問句要用「疑問詞 + 主詞 + 動詞」的直述句語序。Who is that girl? 放進 Do you know 後面，要變成 who that girl is。', '["間接問句的語序和一般疑問句一樣嗎？", "主詞 that girl 要放在動詞 is 的前面還是後面？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "這是直接問句的語序；放在 Do you know 後面要改成直述句語序 that girl is。", "C": "間接問句不用助動詞 does，而且 does that girl 後面少了動詞。", "B": "少了動詞 is，句子不完整。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-2-20', 'EN-9B-2', 'indirect-question', 'Please tell me where ＿＿＿. I want to send you a card.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "you live"}, {"key": "B", "text": "do you live"}, {"key": "C", "text": "you lives"}, {"key": "D", "text": "are you live"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Where do you live? 變成間接問句時，要去掉助動詞 do，改成直述句語序「where + 主詞 + 動詞」，所以是 where you live。', '["間接問句還需要助動詞 do / does / did 嗎？", "主詞 you 搭配的動詞要不要加 s？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "do you live 是直接問句語序；放進句子裡要去掉 do，改成 you live。", "C": "主詞是 you，動詞不能加 s。", "D": "be 動詞 are 和一般動詞 live 不能同時當動詞，而且語序也錯了。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-2-21', 'EN-9B-2', 'indirect-question', 'I wonder ＿＿＿ Amy is so happy today. Did she get a present?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "why"}, {"key": "B", "text": "who"}, {"key": "C", "text": "which"}, {"key": "D", "text": "what"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '後面接著猜「她是不是收到禮物？」，說話者想知道的是 Amy 這麼開心的「原因」，所以用 why：I wonder why Amy is so happy today.（我想知道 Amy 今天為什麼這麼開心）。', '["說話者接著猜 Amy 收到禮物，這是在猜開心的什麼？", "問「原因」要用哪個疑問詞？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "what 問「什麼」，但 Amy is so happy 已經是完整的句子，不缺東西，不能用 what。", "C": "which 用來在幾個選項中選一個，這裡沒有選項。", "B": "who 問「誰」，但 Amy 已經是主詞，句子沒有缺少人。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-2-22', 'EN-9B-2', 'reading-detail', 'Movie Night
Time: Friday, 6:30 p.m.
Place: School Hall
Movie: The Lost Island
Tickets: Free for students; NT$50 for parents
Please bring your student card.

How much does a student need to pay?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "NT$50"}, {"key": "B", "text": "NT$30"}, {"key": "C", "text": "NT$100"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Nothing"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '公告寫 Tickets: Free for students（學生免費），所以學生不用付錢。NT$50 是家長的票價。', '["找到 Tickets 那一行。", "free 是什麼意思？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "NT$50 是家長的票價，學生是免費的。", "B": "公告中沒有出現 NT$30 這個價錢。", "C": "公告中沒有出現 NT$100，可能是誤把兩個家長的票價加起來。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-2-23', 'EN-9B-2', 'indirect-question', 'Can you tell me ＿＿＿ last night? You look tired.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "what you do did"}, {"key": "B", "text": "what did you do"}, {"key": "C", "text": "what do you did"}, {"key": "D", "text": "what you did"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'What did you do last night? 變成間接問句時，去掉助動詞 did，動詞 do 改成過去式 did（時態保留在動詞上），語序改成「what + 主詞 + 動詞」：what you did。', '["間接問句要去掉助動詞 did，那「過去」的時態要放在哪裡？", "do 的過去式是什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "what did you do 是直接問句語序；放進 Can you tell me 後面要改成 what you did。", "A": "do 和 did 不能同時出現當動詞，要把時態放在動詞上，改成 did。", "C": "間接問句不用助動詞 do，而且 do 後面不能接過去式 did。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-2-24', 'EN-9B-2', 'indirect-question', 'I''m not sure ＿＿＿ this book. Let''s ask him before we buy it.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "if Tom likes"}, {"key": "B", "text": "if Tom like"}, {"key": "C", "text": "if likes Tom"}, {"key": "D", "text": "does Tom like"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Does Tom like this book? 是 Yes/No 問句，變成間接問句時要用 if（是否）開頭，去掉 does，動詞因主詞 Tom 是第三人稱單數而加 s：if Tom likes this book。', '["原本的問題可以用 Yes 或 No 回答嗎？這種問句變成間接問句要加哪個字？", "去掉 does 之後，動詞 like 要不要加 s？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "這是直接問句語序；Yes/No 問句放進句子裡要用 if，並去掉 does。", "B": "去掉 does 之後，主詞 Tom 是第三人稱單數，動詞要加 s 變成 likes。", "C": "間接問句要用「主詞 + 動詞」的語序，likes 不能放在 Tom 前面。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-2-25', 'EN-9B-2', 'indirect-question', 'Excuse me. Do you know how much ＿＿＿?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "is this shirt cost"}, {"key": "B", "text": "this shirt costs"}, {"key": "C", "text": "this shirt cost"}, {"key": "D", "text": "does this shirt cost"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'How much does this shirt cost? 放進 Do you know 後面，要去掉 does，改成直述句語序；主詞 this shirt 是單數，現在式動詞加 s：how much this shirt costs。', '["間接問句要用直接問句語序還是直述句語序？", "去掉 does 後，主詞是單數，cost 要不要加 s？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "這是直接問句語序；放在 Do you know 後面要去掉 does。", "A": "be 動詞 is 和一般動詞 cost 不能同時當動詞。", "C": "去掉 does 之後，主詞 this shirt 是第三人稱單數，現在式要用 costs。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-2-26', 'EN-9B-2', 'reading-inference', 'Mom: Did you take your umbrella this morning?
Amy: No. The sky was blue when I left home.
Mom: Look outside now! I wonder how you will get home.
Amy: Don''t worry. My friend Kelly always brings one, and she lives on our street.

What is probably happening outside now?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "It is getting dark."}, {"key": "B", "text": "It is raining."}, {"key": "C", "text": "It is sunny."}, {"key": "D", "text": "It is very hot."}]'::jsonb, 'B', '媽媽問 Amy 有沒有帶傘，又叫她看外面、擔心她怎麼回家；Amy 回答朋友 Kelly 總是帶傘（one 指 umbrella），可以和她一起走。可見外面正在下雨。', '["媽媽一開始問 Amy 帶了什麼東西？", "Amy 說 Kelly always brings one，one 指的是什麼？", "什麼樣的天氣會讓人擔心沒帶傘回不了家？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "很熱不會讓媽媽擔心 Amy 沒帶傘回不了家；而且 Amy 的回答提到的是傘。", "C": "早上出門時才是晴天（The sky was blue），媽媽叫她看「現在」的外面，天氣已經變了。", "A": "天黑不需要用傘，媽媽和 Amy 談的都是雨傘，表示外面在下雨。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-2-27', 'EN-9B-2', 'reading-main-idea', 'Do you know how much water you use every day? Many people leave the water running while they brush their teeth. If you turn it off, you can save a lot of water. You can also take shorter showers and use the water from washing vegetables to water plants. Small changes can make a big difference.

What is the main idea of this passage?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "People should take more showers."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Brushing teeth is important for our health."}, {"key": "C", "text": "There are easy ways to save water at home."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Plants need a lot of water every day."}]'::jsonb, 'C', '文章舉了刷牙時關水、縮短淋浴時間、用洗菜水澆花等例子，最後說 Small changes can make a big difference.（小改變能帶來大不同），主旨是「在家裡有簡單的方法可以省水」。', '["文章舉的每一個例子都和什麼有關？", "最後一句 Small changes can make a big difference. 在總結什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "刷牙只是省水的例子之一，文章重點不是刷牙對健康的好處。", "D": "用洗菜水澆花是省水的方法，文章不是在介紹植物需要多少水。", "A": "文章建議縮短淋浴時間（take shorter showers），不是多洗澡。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-2-28', 'EN-9B-2', 'indirect-question', 'When will the movie start? → Do you know ＿＿＿?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "when does the movie start"}, {"key": "B", "text": "when the movie will start"}, {"key": "C", "text": "when the movie starts will"}, {"key": "D", "text": "when will the movie start"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '直接問句 When will the movie start? 改成間接問句時，助動詞 will 要放回主詞後面，變成「when + 主詞 + will + 動詞」：when the movie will start。', '["間接問句中，助動詞 will 要放在主詞前面還是後面？", "will 後面接的動詞要用什麼形式？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "這是直接問句的語序，放進 Do you know 後面要把 will 移到主詞後面。", "C": "will 是助動詞，要放在動詞 start 前面，不能放在句尾。", "A": "改成了另一個直接問句，而且間接問句不能用 does 倒裝。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-2-29', 'EN-9B-2', 'reading-inference', 'For ten years, Mr. Lee was always the first person to arrive at our school. He opened the gate, watered the flowers, and said "Good morning" to every student. When it rained, he stood at the gate with a big umbrella and helped the little kids. Last week, he left our school for a new job. On his last day, we gave him a card with everyone''s names on it. Many of us cried when we said goodbye.

How do the students probably feel about Mr. Lee?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "They don''t know him well."}, {"key": "B", "text": "They love him and will miss him."}, {"key": "C", "text": "They think he is too strict."}, {"key": "D", "text": "They are afraid of him."}]'::jsonb, 'B', '李先生十年來每天最早到校、和每位學生打招呼、下雨時撐傘照顧小朋友；他離開時，學生送他簽滿名字的卡片，很多人道別時都哭了。由這些細節可推論學生很喜愛他，也會想念他。', '["李先生平常為學生做了哪些事？", "他離開的那天，學生做了什麼？有什麼反應？", "人在什麼情況下會在道別時哭？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "文中沒有任何李先生讓人害怕的描述，他每天親切地和學生打招呼。", "C": "文中描述的是他照顧學生的行為，沒有提到他很嚴格。", "A": "他在學校十年、每天和每位學生打招呼，學生還一起寫卡片給他，可見大家都認識他。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-9B-2-30', 'EN-9B-2', 'indirect-question', 'Ms. Chen: Somebody broke the window in our classroom. Do you know (1)＿＿＿ it?
Tony: I''m not sure. But I found a ball under my desk this morning. Maybe some students were playing ball.
Ms. Chen: I see. Can you tell me (2)＿＿＿ the ball?
Tony: It''s still in my desk. I''ll bring it to you.

Which is the best choice for (1) and (2)?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "who broke; where did you put"}, {"key": "B", "text": "who broke; where you put"}, {"key": "C", "text": "who breaks; where you put"}, {"key": "D", "text": "who it broke; where you put"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '(1) 疑問詞 who 本身當主詞時（Who broke it?），語序本來就是「疑問詞 + 動詞」，放進間接問句不用改變：who broke it。(2) Where did you put the ball? 變成間接問句要去掉 did，動詞改過去式，語序改成「where + 主詞 + 動詞」：where you put。', '["(1) 直接問句 Who broke it? 中，誰是主詞？", "疑問詞當主詞時，變成間接問句語序要不要改？", "(2) 間接問句要去掉 did，put 的過去式是什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "(1) who 是主詞，後面直接接動詞 broke；who it broke 變成「它打破了誰」，意思和語序都錯。", "A": "(2) where did you put 是直接問句語序，放進 Can you tell me 後面要去掉 did。", "C": "(1) 窗戶已經被打破了，是過去發生的事，要用過去式 broke，不能用現在式 breaks。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('EN-7L-1-13', 'EN-7L-1', 'basic-response', '請聽一句話，選出最適當的回應。（在文具店）', '[{"key": "A", "text": "I have two pens."}, {"key": "B", "text": "It''s on the desk."}, {"key": "C", "text": "It''s thirty dollars."}, {"key": "D", "text": "It''s blue and white."}]'::jsonb, 'C', '聽力原文是「How much is this pen?」（這支筆多少錢？），How much 問價錢，所以要回答金額：It''s thirty dollars.（三十元）。', '["先聽清楚問句開頭是哪兩個字。", "How much 和 What color、How many、Where 問的事情各不相同。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "這是回答 What color is it?（什麼顏色），不是問價錢。", "A": "這是回答 How many pens do you have?（有幾支筆），把 How much 聽成 How many。", "B": "這是回答 Where is it?（在哪裡），問句沒有問位置。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', 'W: How much is this pen?', null),
  ('EN-7L-1-14', 'EN-7L-1', 'basic-response', '請聽一句話，選出最適當的回應。（打電話時）', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Hold on, please."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Judy is my good friend."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Yes, I can speak English."}, {"key": "D", "text": "No, she doesn''t."}]'::jsonb, 'A', '聽力原文是「Hello, may I speak to Judy?」（喂，請問 Judy 在嗎？），這是電話中要找人的說法，接電話的人請對方稍等、去叫 Judy：Hold on, please.（請稍等）最適當。', '["說話的人正在做什麼事？是面對面聊天還是講電話？", "May I speak to...? 在電話裡是什麼意思？接電話的人通常怎麼回應？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "聽到 speak 就以為是問「會不會說英語」，但 speak to Judy 是「找 Judy 講電話」。", "B": "只介紹 Judy 是好朋友，沒有回應對方要找 Judy 講話的請求。", "D": "May I...? 問句不能用 she doesn''t 回答，主詞和助動詞都對不上。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', 'M: Hello, may I speak to Judy?', null),
  ('EN-7L-1-15', 'EN-7L-1', 'basic-response', '請聽一句話，選出最適當的回應。（在公園）', '[{"key": "A", "text": "He is fine, thanks."}, {"key": "B", "text": "He is my cousin, Tom."}, {"key": "C", "text": "He is very tall."}, {"key": "D", "text": "He is in the park."}]'::jsonb, 'B', '聽力原文是「Who is that tall boy over there?」（那邊那個高高的男孩是誰？），Who 問「誰」，要回答他的身分或名字：He is my cousin, Tom.（他是我表哥 Tom）。', '["問句開頭的疑問詞是什麼？", "Who 是問人的身分，回答要說出「他是誰」。"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "聽到 tall 就選有 tall 的句子，但對方已經知道他很高，想知道的是他是誰。", "D": "這是回答 Where is he?（他在哪裡），不是問身分。", "A": "這是回答 How is he?（他好嗎），不是問他是誰。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', 'W: Who is that tall boy over there?', null),
  ('EN-7L-1-16', 'EN-7L-1', 'basic-response', '請聽一句話，選出最適當的回應。（週末早上）', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Yes, I am."}, {"key": "B", "text": "I do my homework every day."}, {"key": "C", "text": "I''m making breakfast."}, {"key": "D", "text": "I''m a student."}]'::jsonb, 'C', '聽力原文是「What are you doing?」（你正在做什麼？），用現在進行式問「此刻正在做的事」，所以回答 I''m making breakfast.（我正在做早餐）。', '["問句用的是 are you doing，表示在問什麼時候的事？", "What 問句要回答「做什麼」，而且時態要跟著問句。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "這是說每天的習慣（現在簡單式），問句問的是「現在正在做」的事。", "D": "這是回答 What do you do?（你是做什麼的）或身分，不是正在做的事。", "A": "What 開頭的問句不能用 Yes 或 No 回答。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', 'M: What are you doing?', null),
  ('EN-7L-1-17', 'EN-7L-1', 'basic-response', '請聽一句話，選出最適當的回應。（在路上相遇）', '[{"key": "A", "text": "I went to the zoo with my sister."}, {"key": "B", "text": "I''m going by bus with my brother."}, {"key": "C", "text": "To the bookstore. I need a dictionary."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Yes, I''m going there right now."}]'::jsonb, 'C', '聽力原文是「Where are you going?」（你要去哪裡？），Where 問地點，要說出要去的地方：To the bookstore. I need a dictionary.（去書店，我需要一本字典）。', '["問句開頭的疑問詞是什麼？", "are you going 是問已經去過的地方，還是現在要去的地方？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "went 是過去式，說的是已經去過的地方，但對方問的是現在要去哪裡。", "B": "by bus 是回答 How are you going?（怎麼去），不是去哪裡。", "D": "Where 問句不能用 Yes 回答，也沒有說出地點。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'W: Where are you going?', null),
  ('EN-7L-1-18', 'EN-7L-1', 'basic-response', '請聽一句話，選出最適當的回應。（早自習時）', '[{"key": "A", "text": "That''s great! Have a nice day."}, {"key": "B", "text": "I''m sorry to hear that. Take care."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Me, too. I like it very much."}, {"key": "D", "text": "It''s cold outside. Wear your coat."}]'::jsonb, 'B', '聽力原文是「I have a bad cold today.」（我今天重感冒），對方說自己生病了，要表示關心：I''m sorry to hear that. Take care.（聽到這消息真難過，保重喔）。', '["對方說的是好消息還是壞消息？", "a bad cold 的 cold 在這裡是「冷」還是「感冒」？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "對方生病是壞消息，回答「太好了」很不禮貌。", "D": "把 cold（感冒）聽成天氣「冷」，所以回答外面很冷。", "C": "生病不是令人喜歡的事，說「我也是，我喜歡」不合理。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'M: I have a bad cold today.', null),
  ('EN-7L-1-19', 'EN-7L-1', 'basic-response', '請聽一句話，選出最適當的回應。（在餐廳點餐）', '[{"key": "A", "text": "I''d like a hamburger and a cola, please."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Here you are. It''s on the table."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Yes, you can take it. I don''t need it."}, {"key": "D", "text": "I''m sorry. It''s not mine. It''s Ben''s."}]'::jsonb, 'A', '聽力原文是「Can I take your order?」（我可以幫您點餐了嗎？），這是店員請客人點餐的說法，所以回答想吃什麼：I''d like a hamburger and a cola, please.（我要一個漢堡和一杯可樂）。', '["說話的人可能是什麼身分？", "在餐廳裡，take your order 是要拿走東西，還是要幫你點餐？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "把 take 想成「拿走」，以為對方要拿走某樣東西。", "D": "聽到 your 以為是在問東西是不是你的，但 order 是「點餐」。", "B": "Here you are. 是把東西遞給別人時說的，店員是要聽你點什麼。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'W: Can I take your order?', null),
  ('EN-7L-1-20', 'EN-7L-1', 'basic-response', '請聽一句話，選出最適當的回應。（打掃教室時）', '[{"key": "A", "text": "It''s twenty dollars. It''s cheap."}, {"key": "B", "text": "It''s Mark''s. He left it here."}, {"key": "C", "text": "It''s a red cap with a star."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Yes, it is. It''s a nice cap."}]'::jsonb, 'B', '聽力原文是「Whose cap is this?」（這是誰的帽子？），Whose 問「誰的」，要說出擁有者：It''s Mark''s. He left it here.（是 Mark 的，他忘在這裡了）。', '["問句開頭的疑問詞是 Who 還是 Whose？", "Whose 是問「誰的」，回答要說出東西屬於哪一個人。"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "這是回答 How much is it?（多少錢），不是問誰的。", "C": "只描述帽子的顏色，沒有說是誰的。", "D": "Whose 開頭的問句不能用 Yes 回答。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'M: Whose cap is this?', null),
  ('EN-7L-1-21', 'EN-7L-1', 'basic-response', '請聽一句話，選出最適當的回應。（星期六上午）', '[{"key": "A", "text": "I swim very well."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Sounds great. What time?"}, {"key": "C", "text": "The swimming pool is big."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Yes, I can swim."}]'::jsonb, 'B', '聽力原文是「Let''s go swimming this afternoon.」（我們今天下午去游泳吧），Let''s... 是提議一起做某事，適當的回應是表示贊成或拒絕：Sounds great. What time?（聽起來很棒，幾點？）', '["Let''s... 是在問問題，還是在提議？", "朋友提議一起去做某件事，你可以怎麼表示同意？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "只說自己很會游泳，沒有回應要不要一起去。", "D": "Yes, I can swim. 是回答 Can you swim?（你會游泳嗎），對方沒有問你會不會。", "C": "聽到 swimming 就選有 swimming 的句子，但沒有回應對方的提議。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'W: Let''s go swimming this afternoon.', null),
  ('EN-7L-1-22', 'EN-7L-1', 'basic-response', '請聽一句話，選出最適當的回應。（在圖書館）', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Yes, it''s my seat. Go ahead."}, {"key": "B", "text": "No, it isn''t. Please sit down."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Sure, I''ll take it home."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Yes, please take it."}]'::jsonb, 'B', '聽力原文是「Excuse me, is this seat taken?」（請問這個座位有人坐嗎？），seat taken 是「座位已經有人了」。回答 No, it isn''t.（沒有人坐）再請對方坐下，前後一致，最適當。', '["is this seat taken 的 taken 在這裡是什麼意思？", "如果座位沒有人，要回答 Yes 還是 No？後面的話要和前面一致。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "Yes 表示「有人坐了」，後面卻請對方坐，前後矛盾。", "C": "把 take 想成「拿走」，座位不能帶回家。", "A": "Yes, it''s my seat. 表示這是我的位子，後面卻說請便，前後矛盾。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', 'M: Excuse me, is this seat taken?', null),
  ('EN-7L-1-23', 'EN-7L-1', 'dialogue-detail', 'Where is the boy''s cat?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Behind the door."}, {"key": "B", "text": "On the bed."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Under the sofa."}, {"key": "D", "text": "In the kitchen."}]'::jsonb, 'C', '媽媽說「She''s sleeping under the sofa.」，男孩再問「Not on my bed?」，媽媽說「No, not today.」，所以貓在沙發底下。', '["媽媽第一次回答時說貓在哪裡？", "男孩問的 on my bed，媽媽怎麼回答？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "床是男孩猜的地方，媽媽說 No, not today，今天不在床上。", "D": "對話中沒有提到廚房。", "A": "對話中沒有提到門後面。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', 'M: Mom, where is my cat?
W: She''s sleeping under the sofa.
M: Not on my bed?
W: No, not today.
N: Question: Where is the boy''s cat?', null),
  ('EN-7L-1-24', 'EN-7L-1', 'dialogue-detail', 'What is Kelly''s favorite subject?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "English."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Music."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Math."}, {"key": "D", "text": "P.E."}]'::jsonb, 'A', '男孩問 Kelly 喜不喜歡數學，Kelly 說「It''s OK, but I like English best.」，like...best 是「最喜歡」，所以她最喜歡英文；喜歡體育的是男孩。', '["Kelly 對數學的感覺是什麼？", "注意 but 後面的 like... best。"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "Kelly 說數學 It''s OK（還可以），不是最喜歡。", "D": "P.E.（體育）是男孩喜歡的科目，不是 Kelly。", "B": "對話中沒有提到音樂。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', 'M: Do you like math, Kelly?
W: It''s OK, but I like English best.
M: Really? I like P.E.
N: Question: What is Kelly''s favorite subject?', null),
  ('EN-7L-1-25', 'EN-7L-1', 'dialogue-detail', 'How many people are there in Tony''s family?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Six."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Five."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Four."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Three."}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'Tony 說「Five. My parents, my two sisters, and me.」，爸媽 2 人、兩個姊妹 2 人，再加上他自己 1 人，共 5 人；狗是寵物，不算家庭成員的人數。', '["Tony 一開始直接說了一個數字，是多少？", "把他列出來的人數算一算，別忘了他自己，也注意寵物算不算人。"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "算人數時忘了加上 Tony 自己（and me）。", "A": "把小狗也算進去了，但題目問的是 people（人）。", "D": "只算了兩個姊妹和 Tony，漏掉了父母。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'W: Tony, how many people are there in your family?
M: Five. My parents, my two sisters, and me.
W: Do you have any pets?
M: Yes, a dog.
N: Question: How many people are there in Tony''s family?', null),
  ('EN-7L-1-26', 'EN-7L-1', 'dialogue-detail', 'What will the boy buy for his sister?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "A doll."}, {"key": "B", "text": "A dress."}, {"key": "C", "text": "A storybook."}, {"key": "D", "text": "A notebook."}]'::jsonb, 'C', '女士先建議買娃娃，男孩說妹妹已經有很多娃娃，而且她喜歡閱讀；女士再建議「Then buy her a storybook.」，男孩說「Good idea.」，所以他要買故事書。', '["女士第一次建議買什麼？男孩同意嗎？", "男孩說妹妹喜歡做什麼？最後他接受了哪個建議？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "娃娃是第一個建議，但男孩說 She has many dolls，沒有接受。", "B": "對話中沒有提到洋裝。", "D": "妹妹喜歡閱讀，最後買的是 storybook（故事書），不是筆記本。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'M: I want to buy a present for my sister.
W: How about a doll?
M: She has many dolls. She likes reading.
W: Then buy her a storybook.
M: Good idea.
N: Question: What will the boy buy for his sister?', null),
  ('EN-7L-1-27', 'EN-7L-1', 'dialogue-detail', 'What day is it today?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Saturday."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Wednesday."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Friday."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Thursday."}]'::jsonb, 'D', '男孩說英文考試「No, it''s tomorrow, on Friday.」，考試在明天，明天是星期五，所以今天是星期四。', '["英文考試是今天還是明天？", "明天是星期幾？那今天呢？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "星期五是明天（考試那天），不是今天。", "B": "把「前一天」多算了一天，星期五的前一天是星期四。", "A": "往後推而不是往前推，星期六是考試的後一天。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'W: Is the English test today?
M: No, it''s tomorrow, on Friday.
W: Great. I have one more day to study.
N: Question: What day is it today?', null),
  ('EN-7L-1-28', 'EN-7L-1', 'dialogue-detail', 'Where does the woman want to go?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "To the hospital."}, {"key": "B", "text": "To the bus stop."}, {"key": "C", "text": "To the park."}, {"key": "D", "text": "To the bank."}]'::jsonb, 'A', '女士問「Is there a hospital near here?」，她想找醫院；男士報路時提到的銀行是轉彎的地標，公園是醫院旁邊的地標。', '["女士一開始問附近有沒有什麼地方？", "男士說的 bank 和 park 是目的地，還是用來報路的地標？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "銀行是轉彎的地方（turn left at the bank），只是報路的地標。", "C": "公園在醫院旁邊（next to the park），也是地標，不是目的地。", "B": "對話中沒有提到公車站。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'W: Excuse me. Is there a hospital near here?
M: Yes. Go straight and turn left at the bank. It''s next to the park.
W: Thank you.
N: Question: Where does the woman want to go?', null),
  ('EN-7L-1-29', 'EN-7L-1', 'dialogue-detail', 'How much does the boy need to pay?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "50 dollars."}, {"key": "B", "text": "60 dollars."}, {"key": "C", "text": "40 dollars."}, {"key": "D", "text": "30 dollars."}]'::jsonb, 'A', '蘋果一顆 20 元、香蕉一根 10 元，男孩說「I''ll take two apples and one banana.」，所以要付 20 × 2 + 10 × 1 = 50 元。', '["蘋果和香蕉各一個多少錢？", "男孩最後各買了幾個？把錢加起來。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "只算了一顆蘋果加一根香蕉（20 + 10），漏了第二顆蘋果。", "C": "只算了兩顆蘋果（20 × 2），忘了加香蕉。", "B": "以為兩種水果都買兩個（20 × 2 + 10 × 2）。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', 'M: How much are the apples?
W: They''re twenty dollars each.
M: And the bananas?
W: Ten dollars each.
M: I''ll take two apples and one banana.
N: Question: How much does the boy need to pay?', null),
  ('EN-7L-1-30', 'EN-7L-1', 'dialogue-detail', 'What time does Nina get up on Sundays?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "At seven."}, {"key": "B", "text": "At six."}, {"key": "C", "text": "At eight."}, {"key": "D", "text": "At nine."}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Nina 說平日（weekdays）六點起床，「on Saturdays I get up at seven, and on Sundays I sleep until nine」，星期天睡到九點，所以星期天九點起床。', '["對話中出現了三個時間，各是哪幾天起床的時間？", "注意 on Sundays 後面的 sleep until...。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "六點是平日（星期一到星期五）起床的時間。", "A": "七點是星期六起床的時間。", "C": "對話中沒有提到八點。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', 'M: Do you get up at six every day, Nina?
W: On weekdays, yes. But on Saturdays I get up at seven, and on Sundays I sleep until nine.
M: Lucky you!
N: Question: What time does Nina get up on Sundays?', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-13', 'EN-8L-1', 'basic-response', '請聽一句話，選出最適當的回應。（放學後）', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Yes, I''ll watch it tonight."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Yes, I go every week."}, {"key": "C", "text": "No, I had to help my mom at home."}, {"key": "D", "text": "The game is at the gym."}]'::jsonb, 'C', '聽力原文是「Did you go to the basketball game last night?」（你昨晚有去看籃球賽嗎？），用過去式問昨晚的事，No, I had to help my mom at home.（沒有，我得在家幫媽媽）時態和意思都正確。', '["問句的時間是 last night，用的是哪一種時態？", "回答要用過去式，而且 Yes／No 後面的內容要一致。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "go every week 是現在的習慣，沒有回答昨晚的事。", "A": "說 Yes（有去）卻講今晚要看，時間和意思都對不上。", "D": "這是回答比賽在哪裡，沒有回答昨晚有沒有去。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', 'W: Did you go to the basketball game last night?', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-14', 'EN-8L-1', 'basic-response', '請聽一句話，選出最適當的回應。（在百貨公司）', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Yes, I''m looking for a jacket."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Sure. Here you are."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Yes, I can help you."}, {"key": "D", "text": "No, I don''t help people."}]'::jsonb, 'A', '聽力原文是「May I help you?」（需要幫忙嗎？／有什麼需要嗎？），這是店員招呼客人的話，客人可以說明想買什麼：Yes, I''m looking for a jacket.（是的，我在找外套）。', '["在百貨公司裡，誰會說這句話？", "店員問你需不需要幫忙，你可以說自己想找什麼。"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "搞反了角色，是店員要幫你，不是你要幫店員。", "D": "把句子聽成問你幫不幫別人，回答也很沒禮貌。", "B": "Here you are. 是遞東西給別人時說的，店員沒有向你要東西。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', 'M: May I help you?', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-15', 'EN-8L-1', 'basic-response', '請聽一句話，選出最適當的回應。（考試結束後）', '[{"key": "A", "text": "I studied in the library."}, {"key": "B", "text": "I took the bus to school."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Not bad. I got eighty-five."}, {"key": "D", "text": "It''s next Monday."}]'::jsonb, 'C', '聽力原文是「How did you do on the science test?」（你自然考得怎麼樣？），How did you do on...? 是問表現或成績，所以回答 Not bad. I got eighty-five.（還不錯，我考 85 分）。', '["How did you do on the test? 是問方法，還是問結果？", "考完試，朋友最想知道的是什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "這是回答在哪裡讀書，不是考得怎麼樣。", "D": "這是回答考試是什麼時候，而且考試已經考完了（問句用 did）。", "B": "把 How did you...? 當成問交通方式，但對方問的是考試結果。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'W: How did you do on the science test?', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-16', 'EN-8L-1', 'basic-response', '請聽一句話，選出最適當的回應。（在朋友家）', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Sure, I can help you."}, {"key": "B", "text": "You''re welcome."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Yes, I made them myself."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Thanks. They look delicious."}]'::jsonb, 'D', '聽力原文是「Help yourself to some cookies.」（請自己拿餅乾吃），Help yourself to... 是請客人自便、自己取用，適當的回應是道謝：Thanks. They look delicious.（謝謝，看起來好好吃）。', '["Help yourself to... 真的是在請你幫忙嗎？", "主人請你吃東西時，客人應該怎麼回應？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "聽到 help 就以為對方需要幫忙，但 Help yourself 是「請自己取用」。", "B": "You''re welcome. 是回應別人的道謝，對方沒有說謝謝。", "C": "餅乾是主人準備的，客人說自己做的不合理。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'M: Help yourself to some cookies.', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-17', 'EN-8L-1', 'dialogue-detail', 'What did Andy do last Sunday?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "He visited his grandparents."}, {"key": "B", "text": "He went to the mountains."}, {"key": "C", "text": "He stayed home and watched TV."}, {"key": "D", "text": "He went to the beach."}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Andy 說「I went to the beach with my cousins.」，他上星期天和表兄弟去海邊，還游泳、打排球；待在家看電視的是女孩。', '["題目問的是誰做了什麼？", "Andy 說 I went to... 後面接的是哪裡？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "待在家看電視的是女孩（I just stayed home），不是 Andy。", "B": "對話中沒有提到山。", "A": "Andy 是和 cousins（表兄弟姊妹）出去，不是去看祖父母。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', 'W: What did you do last Sunday, Andy?
M: I went to the beach with my cousins. We swam and played volleyball.
W: Sounds fun. I just stayed home and watched TV.
N: Question: What did Andy do last Sunday?', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-18', 'EN-8L-1', 'dialogue-detail', 'Why can''t Jane see the movie tonight?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "She has too much homework to do tonight."}, {"key": "B", "text": "She needs to take care of her grandmother."}, {"key": "C", "text": "She is sick and has to stay in bed."}, {"key": "D", "text": "She doesn''t like to watch movies at all."}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'Jane 說「I''d love to, but I can''t. My grandma is sick, and I have to take care of her.」，生病的是奶奶，她要照顧奶奶，所以不能去看電影。', '["Jane 想不想去看電影？", "注意 but I can''t 後面的原因，生病的是誰？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "對話中沒有提到功課。", "C": "生病的是 Jane 的奶奶（My grandma is sick），不是 Jane；Jane 是要照顧奶奶，不是自己躺在床上休息。", "D": "Jane 說 I''d love to（我很想去），她是喜歡看電影的。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'M: Do you want to see a movie with us tonight, Jane?
W: I''d love to, but I can''t. My grandma is sick, and I have to take care of her.
M: I see. Maybe next time.
N: Question: Why can''t Jane see the movie tonight?', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-19', 'EN-8L-1', 'dialogue-detail', 'What will the weather be like tomorrow, according to the weather report?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Windy and cold."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Rainy and cool."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Cloudy and warm."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Hot and sunny."}]'::jsonb, 'B', '男士說「the weather report says it''ll be rainy and cool tomorrow」，氣象報告說明天會下雨又涼爽，所以女士說要帶傘；今天才是很熱。', '["對話裡說了哪兩天的天氣？", "注意 the weather report says 後面說的是明天的天氣。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "hot 是今天的天氣（It''s so hot today），不是明天。", "C": "對話中沒有提到多雲。", "A": "對話中沒有提到颳風和寒冷，cool 是涼爽不是冷。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'W: It''s so hot today.
M: Yes, but the weather report says it''ll be rainy and cool tomorrow.
W: Good. I''ll bring my umbrella.
N: Question: What will the weather be like tomorrow, according to the weather report?', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-20', 'EN-8L-1', 'dialogue-detail', 'Where are the man''s keys?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "In his jacket pocket."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Under the bed in his room."}, {"key": "C", "text": "On the kitchen table."}, {"key": "D", "text": "At the bottom of his bag."}]'::jsonb, 'A', '男士說他找過包包和桌上都沒有，女士問「Did you check your jacket pocket?」，男士說「Oh, here they are!」，表示鑰匙在外套口袋裡。', '["男士已經找過哪些地方？", "女士建議找哪裡？男士接著說了什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "男士說 I looked in my bag，包包已經找過，沒有。", "C": "桌上也找過了（and on the table），沒有。", "B": "對話中沒有提到床底下。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'M: I can''t find my keys. I looked in my bag and on the table.
W: Did you check your jacket pocket?
M: Oh, here they are! Thanks.
N: Question: Where are the man''s keys?', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-21', 'EN-8L-1', 'dialogue-detail', 'How many students will go to the science museum now?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "27."}, {"key": "B", "text": "25."}, {"key": "C", "text": "32."}, {"key": "D", "text": "30."}]'::jsonb, 'A', '原本有 30 人報名（Thirty signed up），其中 5 人生病不能去，又有 Tina 和 Ken 兩人想加入，所以現在是 30 − 5 + 2 = 27 人。', '["原本有幾個人報名？後來有幾個人不能去？", "又有誰說也想去？把人數加減算一算。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "只減掉生病的 5 人（30 − 5），忘了加上 Tina 和 Ken。", "D": "30 是原本報名的人數，沒有考慮後來的變化。", "C": "只加上 Tina 和 Ken（30 + 2），忘了減掉生病的 5 人。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', 'W: How many students are going to the science museum on Friday?
M: Thirty signed up, but five of them are sick now.
W: Oh, and Tina and Ken just told me they want to go, too.
M: OK, so I''ll change the number.
N: Question: How many students will go to the science museum now?', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-22', 'EN-8L-1', 'announcement', 'Where will the school meeting be this morning?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "On the playground."}, {"key": "B", "text": "In the library."}, {"key": "C", "text": "In their classrooms."}, {"key": "D", "text": "In the gym."}]'::jsonb, 'D', '廣播說「This morning''s school meeting will be in the gym, not on the playground, because it''s raining.」，因為下雨，朝會改在體育館，不在操場。', '["廣播說今天天氣怎麼樣？", "注意 in the gym, not on the playground 這一句。"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "廣播特別說 not on the playground，因為下雨不在操場。", "C": "廣播沒有說在教室開會。", "B": "廣播中沒有提到圖書館。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', 'N: Good morning, students. This morning''s school meeting will be in the gym, not on the playground, because it''s raining. Please go to the gym at ten o''clock. Thank you.
N: Question: Where will the school meeting be this morning?', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-23', 'EN-8L-1', 'announcement', 'Where should Leo''s parents go?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "To the restaurant on the first floor."}, {"key": "B", "text": "To the service center on the first floor."}, {"key": "C", "text": "To the third floor."}, {"key": "D", "text": "To the toy store."}]'::jsonb, 'B', '廣播說在三樓玩具店附近找到小男孩 Leo，並請「If you are Leo''s parents, please come to the service center on the first floor.」，所以父母要去一樓的服務中心。', '["廣播在哪裡找到 Leo？", "注意 please come to... 後面請父母去的地方。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "玩具店是找到 Leo 的地方，不是要父母去的地方。", "C": "三樓是找到 Leo 的樓層，服務中心在一樓。", "A": "樓層對了，但廣播說的是 service center（服務中心），沒有提到餐廳。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', 'N: Attention, please. We have found a little boy near the toy store on the third floor. His name is Leo, and he is wearing a yellow T-shirt. If you are Leo''s parents, please come to the service center on the first floor. Thank you.
N: Question: Where should Leo''s parents go?', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-24', 'EN-8L-1', 'announcement', 'Where are the people who hear this announcement?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "On a plane."}, {"key": "B", "text": "On a bus."}, {"key": "C", "text": "On a boat."}, {"key": "D", "text": "On a train."}]'::jsonb, 'A', '廣播由 captain（機長）發出，說「We will arrive in Tokyo in about forty minutes」，並請乘客「stay in your seats and fasten your seatbelts」（留在座位上、繫好安全帶）。由機長廣播又要繫安全帶，可以推論是在飛機上。', '["廣播的人說自己是誰？", "廣播請乘客做什麼？哪種交通工具會要乘客繫安全帶？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "火車的廣播不會由 captain 發出，也不會要乘客繫好安全帶。", "B": "公車是司機（driver）在開，不會有 captain 廣播。", "C": "船上雖然也有 captain，但不會要乘客留在座位上繫好安全帶。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'N: Good afternoon, passengers. This is your captain speaking. We will arrive in Tokyo in about forty minutes. The weather there is sunny, and the temperature is twenty degrees. Please stay in your seats and fasten your seatbelts.
N: Question: Where are the people who hear this announcement?', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-25', 'EN-8L-1', 'announcement', 'What do we know about the City Art Museum?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Students can get in for free with their student cards."}, {"key": "B", "text": "It closes at nine p.m. from Tuesday to Sunday."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Students pay less if they show their student cards."}, {"key": "D", "text": "It is open every day, from Monday to Sunday."}]'::jsonb, 'C', '廣播說「Students can get in for half price. Please show your student card at the ticket office.」，學生出示學生證可以半價，所以學生付比較少的錢。', '["博物館的開放時間是幾點到幾點？哪一天休息？", "學生有什麼優惠？要做什麼才能享有？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "廣播說 We are closed on Mondays，星期一休館，不是每天開。", "B": "博物館是早上九點開、下午五點關，不是晚上九點關。", "A": "學生是半價（half price），不是免費。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'N: Welcome to the City Art Museum. The museum is open from nine a.m. to five p.m. from Tuesday to Sunday. We are closed on Mondays. Students can get in for half price. Please show your student card at the ticket office.
N: Question: What do we know about the City Art Museum?', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-26', 'EN-8L-1', 'announcement', 'What will students do this Friday?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Stay home and rest."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Bring their P.E. clothes to school."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Have Sports Day."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Have the classes planned for next Wednesday."}]'::jsonb, 'D', '廣播說運動會不在這星期五舉行，改到下星期三；「Classes on that Wednesday will move to this Friday.」，下星期三原本的課移到這星期五上，所以這星期五要上下星期三的課。', '["運動會原本是哪一天？改到哪一天？", "原本下星期三的課怎麼辦？移到了哪一天？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "運動會已經改到下星期三，這星期五不舉行（will not be held this Friday）。", "A": "這星期五還是要上課，只是上的是下星期三的課，不是放假。", "B": "廣播要學生下星期三（運動會那天）帶運動服，不是這星期五。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', 'N: Attention, students. Because the playground is not ready yet, Sports Day will not be held this Friday. It will be held next Wednesday instead. Classes on that Wednesday will move to this Friday. Please bring your P.E. clothes next Wednesday.
N: Question: What will students do this Friday?', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-27', 'EN-8L-1', 'message', 'Why did Mrs. Chen call Tom?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "To invite Tom to her garden party."}, {"key": "B", "text": "To tell Tom his dog is sick."}, {"key": "C", "text": "To tell Tom she has his dog."}, {"key": "D", "text": "To ask Tom to walk her dog."}]'::jsonb, 'C', '陳太太說「I found your dog in my garden this morning. He''s fine and he''s with me now.」，她在花園找到 Tom 的狗，狗現在和她在一起，請 Tom 回家後來帶狗，所以留言是要告訴 Tom 狗在她那裡。', '["陳太太在哪裡發現了什麼？", "狗現在好不好？在誰那裡？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "狗是 Tom 的（your dog），不是陳太太的，她也沒有請 Tom 遛狗。", "A": "聽到 garden 就以為是花園派對，但留言沒有邀請。", "B": "留言說 He''s fine，狗很好，沒有生病。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', 'W: Hello, Tom. This is Mrs. Chen, your neighbor. I found your dog in my garden this morning. He''s fine, and he''s with me now. Please come and get him when you get home. Thank you.
N: Question: Why did Mrs. Chen call Tom?', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-28', 'EN-8L-1', 'message', 'What does Amy''s dad ask her to do?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Wait for him until nine for dinner."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Cook dinner for her mom at six."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Do her homework and eat dinner without him."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Go to a meeting with him."}]'::jsonb, 'C', '爸爸說「Please start your homework first and don''t wait for me for dinner.」，要 Amy 先寫功課，晚餐不用等他，所以是寫功課、不等他吃晚餐。', '["爸爸為什麼會晚回家？", "注意 Please... 和 don''t... 這兩個要求。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "六點是媽媽回家的時間，爸爸沒有要 Amy 煮晚餐。", "A": "爸爸說 don''t wait for me for dinner，不要等他吃晚餐。", "D": "開會的是爸爸自己，沒有要 Amy 一起去。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'M: Hi, Amy. It''s Dad. I''m going to be late tonight because I have a meeting. Mom will be home at six. Please start your homework first, and don''t wait for me for dinner. I''ll be home around nine.
N: Question: What does Amy''s dad ask her to do?', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-29', 'EN-8L-1', 'message', 'What time should Mr. Wang arrive at the dentist''s office?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "At two twenty."}, {"key": "B", "text": "At two forty."}, {"key": "C", "text": "At two o''clock."}, {"key": "D", "text": "At two thirty."}]'::jsonb, 'A', '留言說看牙時間是「tomorrow at two thirty」，並請他「come ten minutes early」（提早十分鐘到）填表格，2:30 提早 10 分鐘是 2:20。', '["預約的時間是幾點？", "ten minutes early 是要提早還是延後？差幾分鐘？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "兩點半是看診的時間，但留言要他提早十分鐘到。", "B": "把 early（提早）聽成延後，算成 2:40。", "C": "提早了三十分鐘，但留言只說提早十分鐘。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'W: Hello, this is Happy Dentist Office calling for Mr. Wang. Your appointment is tomorrow at two thirty. Please come ten minutes early to fill out a form. If you can''t come, please call us at 2345-6789.
N: Question: What time should Mr. Wang arrive at the dentist''s office?', null),
  ('EN-8L-1-30', 'EN-8L-1', 'message', 'What should Lucy bring to the class party?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "The drinks."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Some fruit."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Some fruit and the drinks."}, {"key": "D", "text": "The cake."}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Jack 一開始請 Lucy 帶水果，但後來 Peter 不能來，所以改請 Lucy「bring the drinks instead」，而且說「I''ll ask someone else about the fruit.」，水果會找別人帶，所以 Lucy 只要帶飲料。', '["Jack 一開始請 Lucy 帶什麼？後來發生了什麼事？", "注意 instead（改成）和最後一句水果要找誰帶。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "水果是一開始的安排，後來改了，Jack 會請別人帶水果。", "D": "蛋糕是 Jack 自己要帶的（I''ll bring the cake）。", "C": "Jack 說水果會問別人（ask someone else about the fruit），Lucy 不用兩樣都帶。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', 'M: Hi, Lucy. It''s Jack. About the class party on Saturday: Peter will bring the drinks, and I''ll bring the cake. Can you bring some fruit? Oh, wait. Peter just texted me. He can''t come, so could you bring the drinks instead? I''ll ask someone else about the fruit.
N: Question: What should Lucy bring to the class party?', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-13', 'EN-9L-1', 'basic-response', '請聽一句話，選出最適當的回應。（在超商）', '[{"key": "A", "text": "No, it''s not my bag."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Yes, I''d like to go."}, {"key": "C", "text": "No, thanks. I brought my own."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Yes, I bought it yesterday."}]'::jsonb, 'C', '聽力原文是「Would you like a bag for your things?」（你的東西需要袋子嗎？），店員在提供袋子，No, thanks. I brought my own.（不用了，謝謝，我有自己帶）是有禮貌的拒絕，並說明原因。', '["店員是在問問題，還是在提供東西？", "Would you like...? 可以怎麼接受或婉拒？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "把問句聽成 Would you like to go...?（想不想去），但店員問的是要不要袋子。", "A": "聽到 bag 以為在問袋子是不是你的。", "D": "用過去式說昨天買的，沒有回答現在要不要袋子。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', 'M: Would you like a bag for your things?', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-14', 'EN-9L-1', 'basic-response', '請聽一句話，選出最適當的回應。（午休時間）', '[{"key": "A", "text": "I lent it to you last week."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Not yet. I''ve read only half of it."}, {"key": "C", "text": "No, I''ve already finished it."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Yes, I''ll finish it tomorrow."}]'::jsonb, 'B', '聽力原文是「Have you finished reading the book I lent you?」（我借你的書看完了嗎？），用現在完成式問是否完成，Not yet. I''ve read only half of it.（還沒，我只看了一半）前後一致。', '["Have you finished...? 是在問什麼？", "Yes／No／Not yet 後面的話要和前面的意思一致。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "說 Yes（看完了）卻說明天才會看完，前後矛盾。", "A": "書是對方借給你的，搞反了借出和借入的人。", "C": "說 No（沒看完）卻說已經看完了，前後矛盾。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', 'W: Have you finished reading the book I lent you?', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-15', 'EN-9L-1', 'basic-response', '請聽一句話，選出最適當的回應。（社團活動時）', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Great. See you tomorrow, then."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Don''t be afraid. It''s not dangerous."}, {"key": "C", "text": "That''s all right. Hope everything is OK."}, {"key": "D", "text": "I''m afraid of dogs, too."}]'::jsonb, 'C', '聽力原文是「I''m afraid I can''t come to practice tomorrow.」，I''m afraid... 在這裡是「恐怕……」的委婉說法，對方是說明天不能來練習，適當的回應是表示沒關係並關心：That''s all right. Hope everything is OK.', '["I''m afraid... 在這句話裡真的是「害怕」嗎？", "對方說明天不能來，你可以怎麼回應？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "把 I''m afraid 當成「害怕」，但這裡是委婉的「恐怕」。", "A": "對方說明天不能來，回答「明天見」不合理。", "D": "把 afraid 當成「害怕」，又扯到怕狗，和不能來練習無關。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'M: I''m afraid I can''t come to practice tomorrow.', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-16', 'EN-9L-1', 'basic-response', '請聽一句話，選出最適當的回應。（在旅館櫃檯）', '[{"key": "A", "text": "About forty minutes by MRT."}, {"key": "B", "text": "It leaves every ten minutes."}, {"key": "C", "text": "I''ll go to the airport tomorrow."}, {"key": "D", "text": "It''s about thirty kilometers."}]'::jsonb, 'A', '聽力原文是「How long does it take to get to the airport from here?」（從這裡到機場要多久？），How long does it take 問花費的時間，所以回答 About forty minutes by MRT.（搭捷運大約四十分鐘）。', '["How long does it take... 問的是時間、距離還是頻率？", "回答要說出「需要多少時間」。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "every ten minutes 是回答 How often（多久一班），不是要花多久。", "D": "thirty kilometers 是距離，回答的是 How far，不是 How long。", "C": "只說自己明天要去機場，沒有回答需要多少時間。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'W: How long does it take to get to the airport from here?', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-17', 'EN-9L-1', 'dialogue-inference', 'Who is the woman most likely to be?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "A police officer."}, {"key": "B", "text": "A cook."}, {"key": "C", "text": "A teacher."}, {"key": "D", "text": "A doctor."}]'::jsonb, 'D', '女士問「What seems to be the problem?」，男士說頭痛、發燒，女士幫他檢查（Open your mouth），說他感冒了，還告訴他藥一天吃三次，所以她最可能是醫生。', '["男士說自己哪裡不舒服？", "女士做了哪些事？誰會檢查身體、告訴你怎麼吃藥？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "對話中沒有和上課有關的內容。", "B": "雖然有說到喝水、吃藥，但廚師不會幫人檢查身體。", "A": "警察不會幫人看病、開藥。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', 'W: Good morning. What seems to be the problem?
M: I''ve had a headache and a fever since last night.
W: Let me check. Open your mouth, please. Well, you have a cold. Take this medicine three times a day and drink lots of water.
N: Question: Who is the woman most likely to be?', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-18', 'EN-9L-1', 'dialogue-inference', 'What can we learn about the girl?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "She can''t walk well right now."}, {"key": "B", "text": "She will go hiking this Saturday."}, {"key": "C", "text": "She doesn''t like hiking."}, {"key": "D", "text": "She has basketball practice on Saturday."}]'::jsonb, 'A', '女孩說「I''d love to, but I hurt my foot during basketball practice yesterday.」，她想去，但昨天練球時腳受傷了，可以推論她現在沒辦法好好走路，所以不能去爬山。', '["女孩想不想去爬山？", "她說自己哪裡受傷了？腳受傷會影響什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "女孩說 I''d love to，還說下次可以一起去，她是喜歡爬山的。", "B": "她腳受傷了，說 Maybe I can join you next time，這次不會去。", "D": "籃球練習是昨天（yesterday），對話沒有說星期六要練球。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'M: Do you want to go hiking with us this Saturday?
W: I''d love to, but I hurt my foot during basketball practice yesterday.
M: Oh, I''m sorry.
W: Maybe I can join you next time.
N: Question: What can we learn about the girl?', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-19', 'EN-9L-1', 'dialogue-inference', 'What does the woman think?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "English movies are too hard to understand."}, {"key": "B", "text": "The man''s ways of learning English work well."}, {"key": "C", "text": "The man should watch more movies."}, {"key": "D", "text": "The man''s cousin speaks better English than him."}]'::jsonb, 'B', '女士先稱讚「your English has really improved」，男士說明他每週看英文電影、和加拿大的表哥練習說英文，女士回答「No wonder.」（難怪），表示她認為這些方法讓他進步，也就是他的學習方法很有效。', '["女士一開始怎麼評價男士的英文？", "No wonder. 是「難怪」的意思，女士覺得是什麼讓他進步？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "女士沒有建議他多看電影，她是認同他已經在做的方法。", "D": "對話中沒有比較男士和表哥誰的英文比較好。", "A": "男士每週看英文電影而且進步了，女士沒有說電影太難。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'W: Wow, your English has really improved!
M: Thanks. I''ve watched an English movie every week, and I''ve practiced speaking with my cousin from Canada.
W: No wonder.
N: Question: What does the woman think?', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-20', 'EN-9L-1', 'dialogue-inference', 'What will the man probably do next?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Cross the street to wait for Bus 25."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Ask the bus driver for help."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Take this bus to the city hall."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Walk to the train station."}]'::jsonb, 'A', '男士想去火車站，女士說這班公車是去市政府的，「You need Bus 25. It stops across the street.」，男士道謝，所以他接下來最可能過馬路去等 25 號公車。', '["男士想去哪裡？這班公車會到嗎？", "女士建議他搭哪一班車？在哪裡搭？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "這班公車去市政府，不到火車站，男士不會搭。", "D": "女士建議搭 25 號公車，沒有說要走路去。", "B": "女士已經告訴他要怎麼搭車了，不需要再問司機。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'M: Excuse me. Does this bus go to the train station?
W: No, this one goes to the city hall. You need Bus 25. It stops across the street.
M: Thank you very much.
N: Question: What will the man probably do next?', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-21', 'EN-9L-1', 'dialogue-inference', 'If they leave now, what time will they arrive at the concert?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "At 7:30."}, {"key": "B", "text": "At 7:35."}, {"key": "C", "text": "At 7:20."}, {"key": "D", "text": "At 7:05."}]'::jsonb, 'C', '現在是 6:45，男士原本想搭計程車（20 分鐘），但女士說星期五晚上會塞車，改搭捷運，「It takes thirty-five minutes.」，男士同意現在出發，所以 6:45 + 35 分鐘 = 7:20 到達。', '["現在幾點？他們最後決定搭什麼交通工具？", "那種交通工具要花多久？從現在開始算。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "用計程車的 20 分鐘來算（6:45 + 20），但他們最後決定搭捷運。", "A": "7:30 是演唱會開始的時間，不是到達的時間。", "B": "從 7:00 開始加 35 分鐘，但現在是 6:45。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', 'W: Hurry up, Ken! The concert starts at seven thirty.
M: Don''t worry. It''s only six forty-five. It takes twenty minutes to get there by taxi.
W: But it''s Friday night. The traffic will be terrible. Let''s take the MRT. It''s slower, but it''s never late. It takes thirty-five minutes.
M: OK. Let''s go now.
N: Question: If they leave now, what time will they arrive at the concert?', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-22', 'EN-9L-1', 'announcement', 'Where can people hear this announcement?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "At a hospital."}, {"key": "B", "text": "At a train station."}, {"key": "C", "text": "At a bookstore."}, {"key": "D", "text": "At a swimming pool."}]'::jsonb, 'D', '廣播說「We will close in fifteen minutes. Please get out of the water and go to the changing rooms now.」，要大家離開水中（get out of the water）、去更衣室（changing rooms），還提醒別忘了毛巾，由這些線索可以推論是在游泳池聽到的。', '["廣播要大家離開哪裡、去哪裡？", "get out of the water、changing rooms 會在哪裡出現？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "書店不會要人離開水中、去更衣室。", "B": "火車站的廣播會說班次和月臺，不會叫人離開水中。", "A": "醫院不會說要關門、請大家離開水中。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', 'N: Attention, please. We will close in fifteen minutes. Please get out of the water and go to the changing rooms now. Don''t forget your towels. We will open again tomorrow at six a.m. Thank you.
N: Question: Where can people hear this announcement?', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-23', 'EN-9L-1', 'announcement', 'Which of the following is NOT allowed during the show?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Arriving before eight fifteen."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Taking photos of the singers."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Bringing a bottle of water."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Sitting in your seat quietly."}]'::jsonb, 'B', '廣播說「During the show, please turn off your cellphones and do not take pictures.」，表演中不能拍照，所以拍歌手的照片是不被允許的；廣播也說 Drinks are allowed，可以帶水。', '["廣播一共說了哪些規定？哪些可以、哪些不行？", "注意 do not... 後面接的事情。"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "廣播說 Drinks are allowed，可以帶飲料（水），不能帶的是食物。", "D": "安靜坐在位子上是看表演的正常行為，廣播沒有禁止。", "A": "表演延到 8:15 開始，提早到並沒有被禁止。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'N: Good evening, everyone. Tonight''s show will start a little late, at eight fifteen instead of eight. During the show, please turn off your cellphones and do not take pictures. Drinks are allowed, but food is not. Thank you for your understanding.
N: Question: Which of the following is NOT allowed during the show?', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-24', 'EN-9L-1', 'announcement', 'What can passengers to Hong Kong do while they wait?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Get a free drink near Gate 12."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Get on the plane at Gate 12 now."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Take a different flight at 3:20."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Get a free meal at Gate 21."}]'::jsonb, 'A', '廣播說飛往香港的 3:20 班機因天氣不好延誤到 5:10，「Passengers on this flight can get a free drink at the coffee shop near Gate 12.」，所以乘客等待時可以到 12 號登機門附近拿免費飲料。', '["班機原本幾點？延到幾點？為什麼？", "廣播說乘客可以在哪裡得到什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "3:20 是原本的起飛時間，班機已經延誤了，沒有說可以換班機。", "D": "廣播說的是免費飲料（drink），不是餐點，而且是 Gate 12 不是 21。", "B": "12 號登機門附近是咖啡店，班機延誤到 5:10，現在還不能登機。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'N: Attention, all passengers. The three-twenty flight to Hong Kong has been delayed because of bad weather. The new time is five-ten. Passengers on this flight can get a free drink at the coffee shop near Gate 12. We''re sorry for the trouble.
N: Question: What can passengers to Hong Kong do while they wait?', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-25', 'EN-9L-1', 'message', 'What does Eric''s mother want him to do?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Pick her up at the bus stop."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Bring her wallet to her office."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Make lunch for her."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Look for her wallet in the office."}]'::jsonb, 'B', '媽媽說「I left my wallet on the kitchen table. Could you bring it to my office before lunch?」，她把錢包忘在廚房桌上，請 Eric 在午餐前送到她的辦公室。', '["媽媽把什麼東西忘在哪裡？", "注意 Could you... 後面請 Eric 做的事。"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "before lunch 是送錢包的時間，媽媽沒有要他做午餐。", "A": "媽媽是要 Eric 搭公車去，不是去公車站接她。", "D": "錢包在家裡的廚房桌上，不用去辦公室找。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', 'W: Hi, Eric. It''s Mom. I left my wallet on the kitchen table. Could you bring it to my office before lunch? Take the bus, and call me when you get to the building. Thanks, honey.
N: Question: What does Eric''s mother want him to do?', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-26', 'EN-9L-1', 'message', 'Why did Max call?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "To tell the customer the order is ready."}, {"key": "B", "text": "To tell the customer the price is higher."}, {"key": "C", "text": "To say the pizza will be late because of traffic."}, {"key": "D", "text": "To ask the customer to choose a different pizza."}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Max 說「we don''t have any more mushroom pizzas today」，蘑菇披薩賣完了，可以改成起司或雞肉披薩，「Please call us back and tell us which one you want.」，所以他打電話是請客人改選別的披薩。', '["客人原本點了什麼披薩？店裡還有嗎？", "Max 請客人回電告訴他什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "留言中沒有提到塞車或送餐延誤。", "B": "Max 說 at the same price，價錢一樣，沒有變貴。", "A": "披薩要等客人回電後三十分鐘才會好，現在還沒做好。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'M: Hello, this is Max from Sunny Pizza. I''m sorry, but we don''t have any more mushroom pizzas today. We can give you a cheese pizza or a chicken pizza at the same price. Please call us back and tell us which one you want. Your order will be ready thirty minutes after you call.
N: Question: Why did Max call?', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-27', 'EN-9L-1', 'message', 'What do we know about Mia''s plan?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Mia will take the bus to visit her grandfather."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Mia will visit her grandfather on Sunday afternoon."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Mia''s dance contest is on Sunday afternoon."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Mia can''t visit her grandfather this weekend."}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'Mia 說星期六有兩天的舞蹈比賽，不能去看爺爺；比賽「ends at noon on Sunday, so I can come that afternoon instead」，所以她改在星期天下午去看爺爺，而且是媽媽開車載她。', '["Mia 為什麼星期六不能去？比賽什麼時候結束？", "she can come that afternoon 的 that 指哪一天？她怎麼去？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "比賽在星期天中午就結束了（ends at noon），星期天下午是去看爺爺的時間。", "A": "Mia 說 Mom will drive me there，是媽媽開車載她，不是搭公車。", "D": "她只是星期六不能去，星期天下午還是會去，週末仍會見到爺爺。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', 'W: Hi, Grandpa. It''s Mia. I''m sorry, but I can''t visit you this Saturday because I have a two-day dance contest. It ends at noon on Sunday, so I can come that afternoon instead. Mom will drive me there, and we''ll stay for dinner. Please call me back if that time doesn''t work for you.
N: Question: What do we know about Mia''s plan?', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-28', 'EN-9L-1', 'short-talk', 'What does Kevin do every morning?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "He runs by the river with his father."}, {"key": "B", "text": "He walks his dog in the park."}, {"key": "C", "text": "He joins a running race."}, {"key": "D", "text": "He runs in the park."}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Kevin 說「Every morning, I get up at six and run in the park near my home for thirty minutes.」，他每天早上在家附近的公園跑步；和爸爸在河邊跑步是週末的事。', '["短文裡說了 Kevin 哪些不同時間做的事？", "注意 Every morning 後面接的活動和地點。"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "和爸爸在河邊跑步是週末（On weekends）的事，不是每天早上。", "C": "跑步比賽是下個月（Next month）才要參加的。", "B": "短文中沒有提到遛狗。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', 'N: My name is Kevin. I''m fifteen, and I live in Taichung. Every morning, I get up at six and run in the park near my home for thirty minutes. Running makes me feel healthy and happy. On weekends, I often run with my father by the river. Next month, we are going to join a running race together.
N: Question: What does Kevin do every morning?', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-29', 'EN-9L-1', 'short-talk', 'Why did Amy feel nervous at first?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "She had never traveled by plane."}, {"key": "B", "text": "She couldn''t speak French."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Sophie''s family wasn''t friendly."}, {"key": "D", "text": "She got lost in France."}]'::jsonb, 'B', '短文說「At first, Amy felt nervous because she couldn''t speak French.」，because 後面說出原因：她不會說法語。後來 Sophie 的家人很親切，還教她法語單字。', '["Amy 去哪裡拜訪筆友？", "注意 felt nervous because... 後面的原因。"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "短文中沒有提到她沒搭過飛機。", "C": "短文說 Sophie''s family was very kind，他們很親切。", "D": "短文中沒有提到她迷路。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', 'N: Last summer, Amy visited her pen pal, Sophie, in France. At first, Amy felt nervous because she couldn''t speak French. But Sophie''s family was very kind. They spoke English slowly to her and taught her some French words every day. Before she left, Amy could say "thank you" and "good night" in French. Now she wants to learn more French in high school.
N: Question: Why did Amy feel nervous at first?', null),
  ('EN-9L-1-30', 'EN-9L-1', 'short-talk', 'What is the main idea of this talk?', '[{"key": "A", "text": "Shopping bags are better than plastic bags."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Lily''s class sold new clothes at the school fair."}, {"key": "C", "text": "Old clothes should all be given to children''s homes."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Lily''s class found useful ways to reuse old clothes."}]'::jsonb, 'D', '短文說 Lily 的班級收集舊衣服：還很好的拿到園遊會賣，錢捐給兒童之家；太舊不能穿的剪開做成購物袋，最後幾乎沒有丟掉任何東西。整篇都在說他們把舊衣服重新利用的好方法，所以主旨是 Lily 的班級找到再利用舊衣的方法。', '["短文一開始提到很多人怎麼處理舊衣服？Lily 的班級有什麼不同？", "主旨要能包含整篇的內容，不能只是其中一個細節，也不能說錯細節。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "園遊會賣的是收集來的舊衣服，不是新衣服。", "C": "衣服沒有全部捐出，捐的是賣衣服得到的錢，太舊的衣服做成了購物袋。", "A": "購物袋只是其中一個細節，短文也沒有和塑膠袋比較。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', 'N: Many people throw away old clothes when they don''t want them anymore. But Lily''s class found a better idea. They collected old clothes from students and parents. Clothes in good condition were sold at the school fair, and the money was given to a children''s home. Clothes that were too old to wear were cut into pieces and made into shopping bags. In the end, almost nothing was thrown away.
N: Question: What is the main idea of this talk?', null),
  ('SC-7A-1-01', 'SC-7A-1', 'cell-structure', '下列哪一種構造是植物細胞具有，而動物細胞沒有的？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "粒線體"}, {"key": "B", "text": "細胞核"}, {"key": "C", "text": "細胞膜"}, {"key": "D", "text": "細胞壁"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '細胞壁位於植物細胞膜的外側，可以支持和保護細胞，動物細胞沒有細胞壁。細胞膜、粒線體和細胞核則是動物細胞和植物細胞都有的構造。', '["想一想：哪一種構造讓植物細胞的形狀比較固定？", "這個構造位在細胞膜的外面。"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "動物細胞和植物細胞都有細胞膜。", "A": "動物細胞也要進行呼吸作用，所以也有粒線體。", "B": "動物細胞和植物細胞一般都有細胞核。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7A-1-02', 'SC-7A-1', 'cell-structure', '細胞需要能量才能進行各種生命活動。細胞中負責進行呼吸作用、把養分分解並釋放能量的主要構造是哪一個？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "葉綠體"}, {"key": "B", "text": "細胞壁"}, {"key": "C", "text": "粒線體"}, {"key": "D", "text": "液胞"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '粒線體是細胞進行呼吸作用的主要場所，能把葡萄糖等養分分解，釋放出能量供細胞使用。葉綠體負責光合作用，液胞儲存水分與物質，細胞壁負責支持保護。', '["「製造養分」和「分解養分釋放能量」是不同構造負責的。", "動物細胞沒有葉綠體，但動物細胞一樣需要能量。"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "葉綠體是進行光合作用、製造養分的構造，不是分解養分的構造。", "D": "液胞主要是儲存水分和物質。", "B": "細胞壁的功能是支持和保護，與能量釋放無關。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7A-1-03', 'SC-7A-1', 'cell-structure', '小玲用顯微鏡觀察洋蔥鱗葉的表皮細胞，看得到細胞壁和細胞核，卻找不到葉綠體。最合理的原因是什麼？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "葉綠體太小，光學顯微鏡無法看到"}, {"key": "B", "text": "染色時碘液把葉綠體溶解了"}, {"key": "C", "text": "洋蔥鱗葉表皮細胞本身不含葉綠體"}, {"key": "D", "text": "洋蔥屬於真菌，所以沒有葉綠體"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '並不是所有植物細胞都有葉綠體。洋蔥鱗葉埋在土中、照不到光，表皮細胞本身就沒有葉綠體。葉綠體在光學顯微鏡下是看得到的，例如觀察水蘊草葉片就能看到綠色顆粒。', '["光學顯微鏡下看水蘊草葉片，能不能看到綠色的葉綠體？", "洋蔥鱗葉平常長在什麼位置？照得到光嗎？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "葉綠體在光學顯微鏡下看得到，例如水蘊草葉片的綠色顆粒。", "B": "碘液是讓細胞核等構造更清楚的染色劑，並不會溶解葉綠體。", "D": "洋蔥是植物，不是真菌；植物細胞也不一定都有葉綠體。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7A-1-04', 'SC-7A-1', 'microscope', '使用複式顯微鏡時，目鏡上標示「10×」，物鏡上標示「40×」，此時觀察到的影像放大倍率是多少？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "50 倍"}, {"key": "B", "text": "4 倍"}, {"key": "C", "text": "30 倍"}, {"key": "D", "text": "400 倍"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '複式顯微鏡的放大倍率 = 目鏡倍率 × 物鏡倍率 = 10 × 40 = 400 倍。', '["總放大倍率和目鏡、物鏡的倍率有什麼關係？", "是相加還是相乘？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "把兩個倍率相加了，應該相乘。", "B": "把兩個倍率相除了。", "C": "把兩個倍率相減了。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7A-1-05', 'SC-7A-1', 'microscope', '用複式顯微鏡觀察玻片時，發現要觀察的細胞影像位在視野的左上方。要把這個細胞移到視野中央，玻片應該往哪個方向移動？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "左下方"}, {"key": "B", "text": "右下方"}, {"key": "C", "text": "右上方"}, {"key": "D", "text": "左上方"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '複式顯微鏡看到的影像上下、左右都顛倒，所以玻片移動的方向和影像移動的方向相反。影像在左上方，要讓影像往右下方移到中央，玻片就要往左上方移動。簡單記法：影像偏哪裡，玻片就往哪裡移。', '["顯微鏡下的影像和實物的方向有什麼關係？", "玻片往左移時，視野中的影像會往哪邊跑？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "以為玻片和影像移動方向相同，忘了影像是顛倒的。", "C": "只考慮了左右顛倒，沒有考慮上下也顛倒。", "A": "只考慮了上下顛倒，沒有考慮左右也顛倒。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7A-1-06', 'SC-7A-1', 'microscope', '小華用目鏡 10×、物鏡 10× 觀察一排細胞，視野直徑上剛好排了 16 個細胞。若他只把物鏡換成 40×，其他條件不變，視野直徑上大約可以看到幾個細胞？視野亮度會如何改變？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "約 4 個，視野變亮"}, {"key": "B", "text": "約 64 個，視野變亮"}, {"key": "C", "text": "約 1 個，視野變暗"}, {"key": "D", "text": "約 4 個，視野變暗"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '物鏡由 10× 換成 40×，放大倍率變為原來的 4 倍，每個細胞在視野中看起來的長度變為 4 倍，所以直徑上的細胞數變為 16 ÷ 4 = 4 個。倍率越高，進入眼睛的光越少，視野會變暗。', '["倍率變大後，每個細胞看起來變大還是變小？可以看到的範圍變大還是變小？", "細胞排成「一直線」，只要看長度放大幾倍。", "高倍率時通常要把光圈開大，這代表亮度怎麼了？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "細胞數算對了，但高倍率時視野會變暗，不是變亮。", "C": "把直線上的細胞數當成面積來算（16 ÷ 4²），而且這題是排成一直線。", "B": "以為倍率變大能看到更多細胞，其實看到的範圍變小了。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7A-1-07', 'SC-7A-1', 'organization-level', '人體的組成層次由小到大排列，下列何者正確？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "細胞 → 組織 → 器官系統 → 器官 → 個體"}, {"key": "B", "text": "細胞 → 組織 → 器官 → 器官系統 → 個體"}, {"key": "C", "text": "組織 → 細胞 → 器官 → 器官系統 → 個體"}, {"key": "D", "text": "細胞 → 器官 → 組織 → 器官系統 → 個體"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '許多形態、功能相似的細胞組成組織；不同組織組成器官；多個器官合作組成器官系統；各器官系統共同組成一個個體。所以順序是細胞 → 組織 → 器官 → 器官系統 → 個體。', '["最小的生命單位是什麼？", "胃是一個器官，胃是由什麼組成的？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "組織比器官小，器官是由不同組織組成的。", "C": "細胞是最小的單位，組織是由細胞組成的。", "A": "器官系統是由多個器官組成的，所以器官比器官系統小。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7A-1-08', 'SC-7A-1', 'organization-level', '下列哪一項屬於人體組成層次中的「器官」？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "神經細胞"}, {"key": "B", "text": "消化系統"}, {"key": "C", "text": "胃"}, {"key": "D", "text": "血液"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '胃是由上皮組織、肌肉組織、神經組織等不同組織組成，能完成消化食物的功能，屬於器官。血液屬於組織（結締組織），神經細胞屬於細胞，消化系統屬於器官系統。', '["器官是由什麼組成的？", "想一想：哪一個選項是由好幾種不同組織組成，並且有特定形狀與功能？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "血液屬於結締組織，是組織層次。", "A": "神經細胞是細胞層次。", "B": "消化系統由口腔、胃、小腸等多個器官組成，屬於器官系統層次。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7A-1-09', 'SC-7A-1', 'diffusion-osmosis', '把人類的紅血球放入大量清水中，一段時間後，紅血球最可能發生什麼變化？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "大小幾乎不變"}, {"key": "B", "text": "被細胞壁保護而不會破裂"}, {"key": "C", "text": "失水而皺縮"}, {"key": "D", "text": "吸水脹大，甚至破裂"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '清水中的水分子濃度比紅血球內高，水會經由滲透作用進入紅血球，使紅血球脹大。動物細胞沒有細胞壁保護，吸水太多就會破裂。', '["水分子會從水分子濃度高的地方往哪裡移動？", "紅血球是動物細胞，它有沒有細胞壁？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "在濃鹽水中才會失水皺縮，清水中是吸水。", "A": "清水和紅血球內的水分子濃度不同，會發生滲透。", "B": "紅血球是動物細胞，沒有細胞壁。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7A-1-10', 'SC-7A-1', 'diffusion-osmosis', '實驗：取兩條大小、質量相同的新鮮蘿蔔條，一條放入裝清水的甲杯，另一條放入裝濃鹽水的乙杯。30 分鐘後取出擦乾，發現甲杯的蘿蔔條變硬、質量增加；乙杯的蘿蔔條變軟、質量減少。下列解釋何者最合理？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "蘿蔔細胞的細胞膜不讓水通過，質量變化是鹽造成的"}, {"key": "B", "text": "乙杯蘿蔔細胞中的水分經由滲透作用移到鹽水中"}, {"key": "C", "text": "甲杯蘿蔔條變重，是因為清水中的鹽分進入細胞"}, {"key": "D", "text": "甲杯蘿蔔細胞吸水後細胞壁破裂，所以變硬"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '滲透作用是水分子由水分子濃度高處往低處移動。乙杯濃鹽水的水分子濃度比細胞內低，細胞內的水移到鹽水中，所以蘿蔔條失水變軟、變輕；甲杯清水的水分子濃度高，水進入細胞，蘿蔔條吸水變硬、變重。植物細胞有細胞壁，吸水後不會破裂。', '["這個實驗中，移動的主要是水還是鹽？", "比較鹽水和細胞內，哪一邊的水分子濃度比較高？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "清水中沒有鹽分，甲杯變重是因為吸水。", "A": "細胞膜可以讓水分子通過，這正是滲透作用發生的原因。", "D": "植物細胞有細胞壁支撐，吸水後變硬但不會破裂。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7A-2-01', 'SC-7A-2', 'photosynthesis', '綠色植物進行光合作用時，所需要的原料是什麼？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "二氧化碳和水"}, {"key": "B", "text": "氧和葡萄糖"}, {"key": "C", "text": "二氧化碳和氧"}, {"key": "D", "text": "水和葡萄糖"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '光合作用是植物利用光能，把二氧化碳和水合成葡萄糖（醣類），同時釋放氧氣。所以原料是二氧化碳和水，產物是葡萄糖和氧。', '["光合作用的原料是從哪裡來的？一個從葉片的氣孔進入，一個由根吸收。", "氧和葡萄糖是原料還是產物？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "氧和葡萄糖是光合作用的產物，不是原料。", "C": "氧是光合作用產生的，不是需要的原料。", "D": "葡萄糖是光合作用的產物。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7A-2-02', 'SC-7A-2', 'photosynthesis', '關於光合作用的敘述，下列何者正確？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "主要在粒線體中進行，會消耗氧氣"}, {"key": "B", "text": "只要有水，在黑暗中也能持續進行"}, {"key": "C", "text": "植物只在夜晚進行光合作用"}, {"key": "D", "text": "主要在葉綠體中進行，會產生氧氣"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '光合作用主要在含有葉綠素的葉綠體中進行，需要光能，把二氧化碳和水合成醣類，並釋放氧氣。粒線體是進行呼吸作用的地方。', '["光合作用需要吸收光的色素，這種色素在哪一種構造裡？", "光合作用會讓空氣中的哪一種氣體增加？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "粒線體進行的是呼吸作用，呼吸作用才消耗氧氣。", "B": "光合作用需要光能，黑暗中無法進行。", "C": "夜晚沒有光，植物無法進行光合作用。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7A-2-03', 'SC-7A-2', 'photosynthesis', '實驗：把一盆天竺葵放在黑暗處一整天，再用鋁箔紙把其中一片葉子的一半上下包住（遮光），其餘不遮。照光 6 小時後摘下這片葉子，放入酒精中隔水加熱，再用清水沖洗後滴上碘液。結果未遮光的部分呈藍黑色，遮光的部分不呈藍黑色。這個實驗最能支持下列哪一個結論？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "光合作用需要二氧化碳"}, {"key": "B", "text": "植物需要光才能進行光合作用產生澱粉"}, {"key": "C", "text": "被遮光的部分原本就沒有葉綠素"}, {"key": "D", "text": "光合作用會產生氧氣"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '同一片葉子中，唯一不同的條件是有沒有照光（變因是光）。照光部分遇碘液呈藍黑色，表示有澱粉；遮光部分沒有澱粉，所以結論是光合作用需要光才能產生澱粉。先放黑暗處一天是為了把葉片原有的澱粉消耗掉；酒精隔水加熱是為了溶出葉綠素，讓顏色變化更清楚。', '["這個實驗中，遮光與不遮光兩部分只有哪一個條件不同？", "碘液遇到什麼物質會變成藍黑色？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "實驗中沒有改變二氧化碳的量，無法得到這個結論。", "D": "實驗沒有測量氧氣，碘液只能檢驗澱粉。", "C": "同一片葉子都含有葉綠素，遮光只是讓那部分照不到光。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7A-2-04', 'SC-7A-2', 'enzyme', '生物體內的酵素能加快化學反應的速率，酵素的主要成分是什麼？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "醣類"}, {"key": "B", "text": "維生素"}, {"key": "C", "text": "蛋白質"}, {"key": "D", "text": "脂質"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '酵素的主要成分是蛋白質，因此容易受到溫度、酸鹼度影響。高溫會使酵素失去活性。', '["為什麼酵素煮沸後就沒有作用了？想想哪一類物質遇高溫會改變性質。", "蛋煮熟後會凝固，蛋白的主要成分是什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "脂質是構成細胞膜和儲存能量的物質，不是酵素的主要成分。", "A": "醣類主要是提供能量的物質。", "B": "維生素是調節生理作用的養分，不是酵素的主要成分。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7A-2-05', 'SC-7A-2', 'enzyme', '實驗：甲、乙、丙三支試管都加入 5 毫升澱粉液和 1 毫升唾液。甲放在 37°C 溫水中；乙放在 0°C 冰水中；丙的唾液先煮沸再冷卻，然後放在 37°C 溫水中。10 分鐘後滴入碘液，甲不呈藍黑色，乙、丙都呈藍黑色。另外準備與乙、丙完全相同但未滴碘液的兩支試管，把它們都移到 37°C 溫水中再放 10 分鐘後滴入碘液，預期結果為何？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "乙、丙都不呈藍黑色"}, {"key": "B", "text": "乙、丙都呈藍黑色"}, {"key": "C", "text": "乙呈藍黑色，丙不呈藍黑色"}, {"key": "D", "text": "乙不呈藍黑色，丙呈藍黑色"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '唾液中的酵素能分解澱粉。低溫只會使酵素活性降低，回到適當溫度後活性可以恢復，所以乙的澱粉被分解，不呈藍黑色；高溫煮沸會破壞酵素，即使冷卻回 37°C 也無法恢復，所以丙仍有澱粉，呈藍黑色。', '["低溫和高溫對酵素的影響一樣嗎？", "哪一種溫度造成的影響是「可以恢復」的？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "高溫已經破壞了丙的酵素，冷卻後也不會恢復。", "C": "把低溫和高溫的影響弄反了。", "B": "以為低溫也會永久破壞酵素，其實回溫後活性可以恢復。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7A-2-06', 'SC-7A-2', 'digestion', '我們吃進的米飯中含有澱粉，澱粉最早在哪一個消化器官開始被消化？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "口腔"}, {"key": "B", "text": "胃"}, {"key": "C", "text": "小腸"}, {"key": "D", "text": "大腸"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '口腔中的唾液含有能分解澱粉的酵素，所以澱粉在口腔就開始被消化，最後在小腸完成消化。', '["飯在嘴裡咀嚼久了會有甜味，為什麼？", "唾液是在哪裡分泌的？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "胃主要開始消化的是蛋白質，而且澱粉在這之前已經開始被消化。", "C": "小腸是完成澱粉消化的地方，不是開始的地方。", "D": "大腸主要吸收水分，不負責消化澱粉。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7A-2-07', 'SC-7A-2', 'digestion', '人體吸收養分的主要器官是哪一個？它有什麼構造可以幫助吸收？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "大腸，內壁有許多絨毛"}, {"key": "B", "text": "小腸，內壁有許多皺褶和絨毛"}, {"key": "C", "text": "食道，內壁可以蠕動"}, {"key": "D", "text": "胃，內壁有許多胃腺"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '小腸是消化和吸收養分的主要器官。小腸內壁有許多皺褶，皺褶上又有許多絨毛，大大增加了吸收養分的表面積。大腸主要吸收水分。', '["消化完成後的小分子養分主要在哪裡進入血液？", "增加表面積的構造有什麼好處？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "胃主要是消化，吸收的養分很少。", "A": "大腸主要吸收水分，絨毛是小腸的構造。", "C": "食道只負責把食物送到胃，不吸收養分。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7A-2-08', 'SC-7A-2', 'digestion', '關於膽汁的敘述，下列何者正確？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "由膽囊製造，能分解蛋白質"}, {"key": "B", "text": "含有脂肪酶，能把脂肪分解成脂肪酸"}, {"key": "C", "text": "不含消化酵素，能把脂肪乳化成小油滴"}, {"key": "D", "text": "由胰臟分泌，能分解澱粉"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '膽汁由肝臟製造、儲存在膽囊，再送到小腸。膽汁不含消化酵素，它能把大油滴乳化成小油滴，增加脂肪和酵素接觸的面積，幫助脂肪消化。', '["膽汁是在哪個器官製造的？膽囊只負責什麼？", "膽汁本身能不能把脂肪分解成小分子？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "膽汁由肝臟製造，膽囊只負責儲存，而且膽汁不分解蛋白質。", "D": "胰臟分泌的是胰液，不是膽汁。", "B": "膽汁不含消化酵素，脂肪酶在胰液和腸液中。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7A-2-09', 'SC-7A-2', 'respiration', '關於生物的呼吸作用，下列敘述何者正確？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "只有動物細胞會進行呼吸作用"}, {"key": "B", "text": "呼吸作用只在肺臟中進行"}, {"key": "C", "text": "植物只在夜晚才進行呼吸作用"}, {"key": "D", "text": "主要在粒線體中分解養分，釋放能量並產生二氧化碳"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '呼吸作用是細胞在粒線體中把葡萄糖等養分分解，釋放能量，並產生二氧化碳和水。動物和植物的活細胞無論白天晚上都會進行呼吸作用；肺臟只是交換氣體的器官。', '["呼吸作用是在「器官」進行，還是在「每一個活細胞」中進行？", "植物白天有光合作用，那它的細胞還需要能量嗎？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "植物細胞也有粒線體，也會進行呼吸作用。", "C": "植物白天和夜晚都會進行呼吸作用，只是白天光合作用較明顯。", "B": "肺臟是交換氣體的器官，呼吸作用在全身的細胞中進行。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7A-2-10', 'SC-7A-2', 'respiration', '實驗：甲瓶放入正在萌發的綠豆，乙瓶放入等量煮熟後冷卻的綠豆，兩瓶都密封並放在相同環境。數小時後把兩瓶中的氣體分別通入澄清石灰水，結果何者正確？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "兩瓶的氣體都使石灰水變混濁"}, {"key": "B", "text": "兩瓶的氣體都不會使石灰水變化"}, {"key": "C", "text": "甲瓶的氣體使石灰水變混濁"}, {"key": "D", "text": "乙瓶的氣體使石灰水變混濁"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '萌發中的種子是活的，會進行呼吸作用產生二氧化碳，二氧化碳會使澄清石灰水變混濁。煮熟的綠豆細胞已經死亡，不會進行呼吸作用。', '["澄清石灰水是用來檢驗哪一種氣體？", "煮熟的綠豆還是活的嗎？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "煮熟的綠豆已經死亡，不會進行呼吸作用。", "A": "煮熟的綠豆不會產生二氧化碳，兩瓶結果應該不同。", "B": "萌發中的種子會進行呼吸作用產生二氧化碳。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7A-3-01', 'SC-7A-3', 'plant-transport', '植物的根吸收的水分，主要經由維管束中的哪一種構造向上運送到葉？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "表皮"}, {"key": "B", "text": "韌皮部"}, {"key": "C", "text": "形成層"}, {"key": "D", "text": "木質部"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '維管束中的木質部負責運送水分和礦物質，由根往上運送到莖和葉；韌皮部則負責運送葉片製造的養分。', '["維管束裡有兩種運輸構造，一種運水、一種運養分。", "運送水分的構造，在木本植物中構成了「木材」的大部分。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "韌皮部主要運送葉片製造的養分，不是水分。", "C": "形成層負責細胞分裂使莖變粗，不負責運輸。", "A": "表皮主要是保護作用。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7A-3-02', 'SC-7A-3', 'plant-transport', '果農在樹幹上把樹皮環狀剝除一圈（包含韌皮部），但保留內部的木質部。一段時間後，切口上方的樹皮明顯膨大。最主要的原因是什麼？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "葉片製造的養分無法經韌皮部向下運送，堆積在切口上方"}, {"key": "B", "text": "切口上方的細胞因為缺水而膨大"}, {"key": "C", "text": "根吸收的水分無法向上運送，堆積在切口上方"}, {"key": "D", "text": "切口讓空氣進入樹幹，使樹幹膨脹"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '韌皮部負責把葉片製造的養分往下運送。環狀剝皮切斷了韌皮部，養分無法往下運送，只能堆積在切口上方，使那裡膨大。木質部被保留，所以水分仍能向上運送。', '["剝掉的是哪一種運輸構造？它負責運送什麼？", "葉片製造的養分要往哪個方向運送到根部？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "木質部被保留，水分仍能向上運送。", "B": "水分運送沒有被切斷，而且缺水不會讓組織膨大。", "D": "膨大是因為養分堆積，與空氣無關。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7A-3-03', 'SC-7A-3', 'circulation', '人類的心臟共有幾個腔室？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "6 個"}, {"key": "B", "text": "2 個"}, {"key": "C", "text": "3 個"}, {"key": "D", "text": "4 個"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '人類心臟有左心房、右心房、左心室、右心室，共 4 個腔室。心房接收回心臟的血液，心室把血液送出心臟。', '["心臟分成心房和心室，左右各有幾個？", "左右兩邊各一個心房、一個心室。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "只算了心房或只算了心室。", "C": "可能想成了兩生類的心臟（二心房一心室）。", "A": "把連接心臟的大血管也算進去了。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7A-3-04', 'SC-7A-3', 'circulation', '血液中負責運送氧氣的主要是哪一種成分？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "紅血球"}, {"key": "B", "text": "血小板"}, {"key": "C", "text": "白血球"}, {"key": "D", "text": "血漿"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '紅血球中含有血紅素，能與氧結合，把氧從肺運送到全身細胞。白血球負責抵抗病原體，血小板幫助血液凝固，血漿主要運送養分、廢物和二氧化碳等。', '["血液中哪一種成分含有能和氧結合的紅色物質？", "血液看起來是紅色的，主要是哪一種細胞造成的？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "白血球負責防禦、抵抗病原體。", "B": "血小板負責幫助血液凝固止血。", "D": "血漿主要運送養分和廢物，氧主要由紅血球運送。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7A-3-05', 'SC-7A-3', 'circulation', '一個紅血球從右心室出發，經過肺循環回到心臟。它依序經過的路徑，下列何者正確？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "右心室 → 主動脈 → 肺部微血管 → 大靜脈 → 左心房"}, {"key": "B", "text": "右心室 → 肺動脈 → 肺部微血管 → 肺靜脈 → 右心房"}, {"key": "C", "text": "右心室 → 肺靜脈 → 肺部微血管 → 肺動脈 → 左心房"}, {"key": "D", "text": "右心室 → 肺動脈 → 肺部微血管 → 肺靜脈 → 左心房"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '動脈是把血液帶離心臟的血管，靜脈是把血液帶回心臟的血管。肺循環：右心室 → 肺動脈 → 肺部微血管（在此排出二氧化碳、得到氧）→ 肺靜脈 → 左心房。之後血液再由左心室送往全身。', '["離開心臟的血管叫動脈還是靜脈？", "從肺回來的充氧血，會先回到心臟的左邊還是右邊？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "把動脈和靜脈弄反了：離開心臟的是肺動脈。", "B": "肺靜脈回到的是左心房，右心房接收的是全身回來的血液。", "A": "主動脈和大靜脈屬於體循環，不是肺循環。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7A-3-06', 'SC-7A-3', 'nervous', '構成神經系統，並負責接收與傳導訊息的基本單位是什麼？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "腦"}, {"key": "B", "text": "脊髓"}, {"key": "C", "text": "神經元"}, {"key": "D", "text": "受器"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '神經元（神經細胞）是神經系統構造和功能的基本單位，能接收刺激並傳導訊息。腦和脊髓是由許多神經元組成的中樞神經。', '["「基本單位」通常是指哪一個層次？", "細胞是生物體的基本單位，那神經系統的細胞叫什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "脊髓是由許多神經元組成的器官，屬於中樞神經。", "A": "腦是由大量神經元組成的器官，不是基本單位。", "D": "受器是接收刺激的構造，不是整個神經系統的基本單位。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7A-3-07', 'SC-7A-3', 'nervous', '手不小心碰到很燙的鍋子，會在還沒感覺到痛之前就立刻縮回。這種縮手反射的主要控制中樞是哪裡？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "腦幹"}, {"key": "B", "text": "大腦"}, {"key": "C", "text": "小腦"}, {"key": "D", "text": "脊髓"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '縮手反射是不需要經過大腦思考的反射動作，由脊髓直接控制，反應很快，能保護身體。痛覺之後才傳到大腦，所以會先縮手，再感覺到痛。', '["反射動作需不需要經過思考？", "不經過大腦時，訊息在哪裡就直接轉給運動神經？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "大腦負責有意識的行為和感覺，反射動作不需要大腦決定。", "C": "小腦主要負責身體平衡與協調動作。", "A": "腦幹控制呼吸、心跳等，縮手反射的中樞是脊髓。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7A-3-08', 'SC-7A-3', 'nervous', '打球時，小明看到球朝自己飛來，經過判斷後伸手把球接住。這個有意識的反應，神經訊息傳導的主要路徑為何？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "受器 → 感覺神經 → 脊髓 → 運動神經 → 動器"}, {"key": "B", "text": "受器 → 運動神經 → 大腦 → 感覺神經 → 動器"}, {"key": "C", "text": "動器 → 感覺神經 → 脊髓 → 運動神經 → 受器"}, {"key": "D", "text": "受器 → 感覺神經 → 大腦 → 運動神經 → 動器"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '眼睛（受器）接收到球的影像後，訊息由感覺神經傳到大腦，大腦判斷後下達命令，經運動神經傳到手部肌肉（動器）完成接球。這是有意識的行為，由大腦判斷；若只經過脊髓而不經大腦，則是反射動作的路徑。', '["接球需要經過判斷，判斷是由哪裡負責？", "把訊息「送進」中樞的是感覺神經還是運動神經？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "感覺神經和運動神經的位置弄反了。", "C": "受器接收刺激，動器做出反應，順序弄反了。", "A": "這是反射動作的路徑，接球需要大腦判斷。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7A-3-09', 'SC-7A-3', 'endocrine-homeostasis', '吃完一大碗飯後血糖濃度上升，這時胰臟會分泌較多哪一種激素，使血糖濃度下降？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "腎上腺素"}, {"key": "B", "text": "甲狀腺素"}, {"key": "C", "text": "胰島素"}, {"key": "D", "text": "升糖素"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '胰臟分泌的胰島素能促進細胞吸收和利用葡萄糖、並使肝臟把葡萄糖轉成肝醣儲存，因此能降低血糖。升糖素的作用則是提高血糖。', '["胰臟能分泌兩種調節血糖的激素，作用剛好相反。", "哪一種激素的作用是讓血糖「下降」？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "升糖素是在血糖太低時使血糖上升。", "A": "腎上腺素由腎上腺分泌，會使血糖上升、心跳加快。", "B": "甲狀腺素主要調節新陳代謝速率。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7A-3-10', 'SC-7A-3', 'endocrine-homeostasis', '天氣炎熱時，人體會如何調節以維持體溫恆定？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "皮膚微血管收縮，汗液分泌增加"}, {"key": "B", "text": "皮膚微血管擴張，汗液分泌增加"}, {"key": "C", "text": "骨骼肌顫抖，產生更多熱"}, {"key": "D", "text": "皮膚微血管收縮，汗液分泌減少"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '天氣熱時，皮膚微血管擴張，讓更多血液流經皮膚散熱；同時汗液分泌增加，汗水蒸發時會帶走熱量，所以能使體溫維持恆定。', '["天氣熱時，身體要「散熱」還是「保熱」？", "汗水蒸發時會帶走熱還是帶來熱？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "這是天氣冷時減少散熱的方式。", "A": "微血管收縮會減少散熱，和熱天的需求相反。", "C": "顫抖是天冷時產生熱的方式。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-1-01', 'SC-7B-1', 'reproduction', '下列哪一種繁殖方式屬於無性生殖？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "豌豆開花後結出種子"}, {"key": "B", "text": "雞蛋受精後孵出小雞"}, {"key": "C", "text": "草莓以走莖長出新的植株"}, {"key": "D", "text": "青蛙在水中產卵並完成受精"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '無性生殖不需要精子和卵結合，由親代的一部分直接產生新個體，例如草莓的走莖。種子、受精卵都來自精卵結合，屬於有性生殖。', '["無性生殖需不需要精子和卵結合？", "種子裡的胚是怎麼形成的？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "種子是花經過授粉、受精後形成的，屬於有性生殖。", "D": "青蛙的卵要和精子結合，屬於有性生殖。", "B": "受精卵發育成小雞，屬於有性生殖。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-1-02', 'SC-7B-1', 'reproduction', '和無性生殖相比，有性生殖對物種最主要的好處是什麼？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "子代的變異較多，較能適應環境的變化"}, {"key": "B", "text": "只需要一個親代就能繁殖"}, {"key": "C", "text": "繁殖速度一定比較快"}, {"key": "D", "text": "子代的特徵和親代完全相同"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '有性生殖的子代分別得到父方和母方的遺傳物質，組合多樣，子代之間差異（變異）較大。當環境改變時，比較有可能有些個體能適應而存活。無性生殖的子代則和親代幾乎相同。', '["有性生殖的子代，遺傳物質來自幾個親代？", "如果所有個體都一模一樣，環境突然改變時會怎樣？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "這是無性生殖的特色。", "C": "無性生殖通常繁殖得比較快。", "B": "只需要一個親代是無性生殖的特色。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-1-03', 'SC-7B-1', 'reproduction', '人類體細胞中有 46 條染色體。經過減數分裂產生的精子，其中含有幾條染色體？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "23 條"}, {"key": "B", "text": "46 條"}, {"key": "C", "text": "92 條"}, {"key": "D", "text": "12 條"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '減數分裂產生的生殖細胞，染色體數目是體細胞的一半，所以精子有 46 ÷ 2 = 23 條。精子和卵受精後，受精卵又恢復成 46 條。', '["減數分裂後，染色體數目會怎麼改變？", "精子和卵結合後要恢復成 46 條，那兩者各帶幾條？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "46 條是體細胞的染色體數，減數分裂後會減半。", "C": "染色體數目加倍是錯的，應該減半。", "D": "減半一次就好，不是變成四分之一。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-1-04', 'SC-7B-1', 'mendel', '豌豆的高莖（T）對矮莖（t）為顯性。基因型為 Tt 的豌豆，外表會長成什麼樣子？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "介於高莖與矮莖之間"}, {"key": "B", "text": "矮莖"}, {"key": "C", "text": "一半枝條高、一半枝條矮"}, {"key": "D", "text": "高莖"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '只要有一個顯性基因 T，就會表現出顯性性狀，所以 Tt 表現為高莖。只有 tt 才會表現矮莖。', '["顯性基因和隱性基因在一起時，表現出哪一個？", "大寫字母代表顯性還是隱性？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "有顯性基因 T 時，隱性的矮莖不會表現出來。", "A": "孟德爾的豌豆高矮性狀是完全顯性，不會出現中間高度。", "C": "同一株植物的基因型相同，不會一半高一半矮。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-1-05', 'SC-7B-1', 'mendel', '豌豆的高莖（T）對矮莖（t）為顯性。將兩株基因型都是 Tt 的豌豆雜交，子代是矮莖的機率是多少？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "1/2"}, {"key": "B", "text": "1/4"}, {"key": "C", "text": "0"}, {"key": "D", "text": "3/4"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'Tt × Tt 的子代基因型比例為 TT : Tt : tt = 1 : 2 : 1。只有 tt 是矮莖，所以機率為 1/4。也可以這樣算：每個親代給出 t 的機率各是 1/2，1/2 × 1/2 = 1/4。', '["矮莖的基因型是什麼？", "每個 Tt 親代把 t 傳給子代的機率是多少？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "1/2 是 Tt 的機率，不是矮莖（tt）的機率。", "D": "3/4 是高莖的機率。", "C": "兩個親代都帶有 t，子代有可能是 tt。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-1-06', 'SC-7B-1', 'mendel', '豌豆的高莖（T）對矮莖（t）為顯性。將基因型 Tt 的高莖豌豆和矮莖豌豆雜交，得到 200 株子代。理論上，子代中高莖大約有幾株？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "50 株"}, {"key": "B", "text": "200 株"}, {"key": "C", "text": "100 株"}, {"key": "D", "text": "150 株"}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'Tt × tt，子代基因型為 Tt : tt = 1 : 1，高莖（Tt）占 1/2，所以約 200 × 1/2 = 100 株。', '["矮莖豌豆的基因型是什麼？它能給子代哪種基因？", "列出 Tt × tt 的所有組合。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "用了 Tt × Tt 的 3/4 比例。", "A": "用了 1/4 的比例，把親代基因型弄錯了。", "B": "以為高莖親代的子代全部都是高莖。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-1-07', 'SC-7B-1', 'mendel', '豌豆種子的圓形（R）對皺皮（r）為顯性。將一株圓形豌豆和皺皮豌豆雜交，子代中圓形與皺皮的數量大約是 1 : 1。這株圓形親代的基因型是什麼？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "rr"}, {"key": "B", "text": "無法由子代推測"}, {"key": "C", "text": "RR"}, {"key": "D", "text": "Rr"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '皺皮親代是 rr，只能給 r。若圓形親代是 RR，子代全是 Rr（全圓形）；若是 Rr，子代為 Rr : rr = 1 : 1。所以圓形親代是 Rr。', '["皺皮豌豆的基因型一定是什麼？", "分別假設圓形親代是 RR 或 Rr，看看子代的比例。"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "RR × rr 的子代全部是圓形，不會出現皺皮。", "A": "rr 是皺皮，題目說這株親代是圓形。", "B": "由子代 1 : 1 的比例可以推測出親代基因型。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-1-08', 'SC-7B-1', 'mendel', '某植物的紫花（P）對白花（p）為顯性。兩株紫花植株雜交，子代中出現了白花。若從子代的紫花植株中隨機取一株，它的基因型是 Pp 的機率是多少？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "2/3"}, {"key": "B", "text": "1/2"}, {"key": "C", "text": "1/4"}, {"key": "D", "text": "3/4"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '紫花親代的子代出現白花（pp），表示兩個親代都是 Pp。Pp × Pp 的子代為 PP : Pp : pp = 1 : 2 : 1。題目只在「紫花」中挑選，紫花是 PP 和 Pp，共 1 + 2 = 3 份，其中 Pp 占 2 份，所以機率是 2/3。', '["子代出現白花，代表兩個紫花親代都帶有什麼基因？", "注意題目只從「紫花」子代中挑，範圍不是全部子代。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "1/2 是 Pp 在「全部子代」中的機率，沒有把白花排除。", "C": "1/4 是白花在全部子代中的機率。", "D": "3/4 是紫花在全部子代中的機率，不是紫花中 Pp 的機率。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-1-09', 'SC-7B-1', 'human-genetics', '某種人類遺傳疾病由一對等位基因控制，正常（A）對患病（a）為顯性。一對外表都正常的夫妻，生下了一個患病的孩子。這對夫妻的基因型最可能是？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "一人 Aa、一人 aa"}, {"key": "B", "text": "兩人都是 AA"}, {"key": "C", "text": "一人 AA、一人 Aa"}, {"key": "D", "text": "兩人都是 Aa"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '患病孩子的基因型是 aa，兩個 a 分別來自父親和母親，所以父母都帶有 a；而父母外表正常，一定帶有 A。因此父母都是 Aa。', '["患病孩子的基因型是什麼？", "孩子的兩個基因分別來自誰？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "AA 的父母不能給孩子 a，孩子不會患病。", "C": "AA 的一方只能給 A，孩子不可能是 aa。", "A": "aa 的人會患病，但題目說父母外表都正常。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-1-10', 'SC-7B-1', 'human-genetics', '某種人類遺傳疾病由一對等位基因控制，正常（A）對患病（a）為顯性，且這對基因與性別無關。一對基因型都是 Aa 的夫妻打算再生一個孩子，這個孩子是「患病女孩」的機率是多少？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "1/8"}, {"key": "B", "text": "1/4"}, {"key": "C", "text": "1/2"}, {"key": "D", "text": "3/8"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Aa × Aa 生出 aa（患病）的機率是 1/4；生男生女的機率各是 1/2。兩件事互不影響，所以「患病且是女孩」的機率 = 1/4 × 1/2 = 1/8。', '["先算孩子患病的機率。", "生女孩的機率是多少？兩個條件要同時成立時，機率怎麼算？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "只算了患病的機率，沒有乘上生女孩的機率。", "C": "只考慮了生女孩的機率。", "D": "把「正常女孩」（3/4 × 1/2）算成答案了。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-2-01', 'SC-7B-2', 'evolution', '科學家研究生物演化時，下列哪一項是最直接的證據？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "化石"}, {"key": "B", "text": "生物的棲息地"}, {"key": "C", "text": "生物的食性"}, {"key": "D", "text": "生物的壽命長短"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '化石是古代生物的遺骸或遺跡保存在地層中形成的，能讓我們直接看到過去生物的樣子，以及生物隨時間的改變，是生物演化最直接的證據。', '["要知道很久以前的生物長什麼樣子，要靠什麼？", "這種證據通常保存在地層（岩層）中。"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "食性只能說明現在生物吃什麼，無法直接顯示過去的生物。", "B": "棲息地是現存生物的資料，不能直接證明演化。", "D": "壽命長短和演化證據無關。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-2-02', 'SC-7B-2', 'evolution', '在一處沒有被翻轉擾動過的沉積岩層中，比較深層和淺層發現的化石，一般而言下列敘述何者正確？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "化石年代與地層深淺沒有關係"}, {"key": "B", "text": "深層的化石年代較久遠，生物構造通常較簡單"}, {"key": "C", "text": "深層的化石年代較近，生物構造通常較複雜"}, {"key": "D", "text": "深層的化石年代較久遠，生物構造通常較複雜"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '沉積岩是一層一層堆積而成的，沒有被擾動時，下面的地層先堆積，年代較久遠。從化石紀錄來看，越古老地層中的生物構造通常越簡單，越新的地層出現越多構造複雜的生物。', '["沉積岩層是怎麼形成的？先堆積的在上面還是下面？", "生物的演化大致是從簡單到複雜，還是從複雜到簡單？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "下層比較早堆積，年代應該比較久遠。", "D": "年代判斷正確，但古老地層中的生物構造通常較簡單。", "A": "未受擾動的沉積岩層，深度和年代有關。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-2-03', 'SC-7B-2', 'evolution', '依照達爾文的天擇說，現今長頸鹿的脖子普遍很長，最合理的解釋是什麼？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "長頸鹿的祖先努力伸長脖子吃高處的葉子，脖子越伸越長並遺傳給後代"}, {"key": "B", "text": "祖先族群中脖子長短本來就有差異，脖子較長的個體較容易存活並繁殖，這個特徵逐代累積"}, {"key": "C", "text": "長頸鹿因為需要吃高處的葉子，所以身體主動產生了長脖子"}, {"key": "D", "text": "長頸鹿的脖子是一代之間突然變長的"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '天擇說認為：同種生物的個體之間原本就有差異（變異），能適應環境的個體比較容易存活、繁殖，把有利的特徵遺傳給後代，經過很多代後，族群中具有這種特徵的個體比例增加。', '["天擇說認為變異是「本來就有」還是「因為需要才產生」？", "「用進廢退」是誰的說法？和天擇說一樣嗎？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "這是拉馬克「用進廢退」的想法，後天練出來的特徵不會遺傳。", "C": "生物不會因為「需要」就主動產生新的特徵。", "D": "天擇造成的改變是經過很多世代慢慢累積的。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-2-04', 'SC-7B-2', 'evolution', '某地區的農田多年來一直使用同一種殺蟲劑。剛開始效果很好，但幾年後，同樣劑量的殺蟲劑只能殺死少數害蟲。依照天擇的觀點，最合理的解釋是什麼？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "殺蟲劑噴灑後，讓每一隻害蟲的體內都產生了抗藥的基因，所以後代都有抗藥性"}, {"key": "B", "text": "害蟲為了對抗殺蟲劑，主動讓自己的身體產生抗藥性，再把抗藥性遺傳給後代"}, {"key": "C", "text": "害蟲族群中原本就有少數具抗藥性的個體，牠們存活並繁殖，使抗藥性個體的比例增加"}, {"key": "D", "text": "害蟲在噴藥的過程中學會躲避殺蟲劑，並把這個躲避的方法教給牠們的後代"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '害蟲族群中本來就存在差異，少數個體天生較能抵抗殺蟲劑。每次噴藥後，不具抗藥性的個體死亡，具抗藥性的個體存活並繁殖後代。一代一代下來，族群中具抗藥性的個體越來越多，殺蟲劑效果就變差了。殺蟲劑扮演的是「篩選」的角色。', '["殺蟲劑是「製造」了抗藥性，還是「篩選」出有抗藥性的個體？", "噴藥之後，哪些害蟲能活下來留下後代？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "生物不會為了需要而主動產生新特徵。", "A": "殺蟲劑不會讓害蟲產生特定基因，而是淘汰沒有抗藥性的個體。", "D": "學會的行為不能透過遺傳傳給後代，也不符合天擇的說法。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-2-05', 'SC-7B-2', 'classification', '生物分類的階層由大到小排列，下列何者正確？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "界、門、綱、科、目、屬、種"}, {"key": "B", "text": "種、屬、科、目、綱、門、界"}, {"key": "C", "text": "界、綱、門、目、科、屬、種"}, {"key": "D", "text": "界、門、綱、目、科、屬、種"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '生物分類的階層由大到小依序是：界、門、綱、目、科、屬、種。「種」是最基本的分類單位。', '["最大的分類階層是什麼？最小的呢？", "「目」和「科」哪一個比較大？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "「門」比「綱」大，順序弄反了。", "B": "這是由小到大的順序。", "A": "「目」比「科」大，順序弄反了。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-2-06', 'SC-7B-2', 'classification', '目前科學界通用的生物「學名」，採用林奈提出的二名法。關於學名，下列敘述何者正確？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "各國用自己的語言命名，不需統一"}, {"key": "B", "text": "由屬名和種小名組成，以拉丁文書寫"}, {"key": "C", "text": "由界名和種小名組成，以英文書寫"}, {"key": "D", "text": "由科名和屬名組成，以拉丁文書寫"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '二名法的學名由「屬名 + 種小名」組成，以拉丁文（或拉丁化的文字）書寫，全世界通用，可以避免同物異名或同名異物的混淆。', '["「二名」指的是哪兩個分類階層的名稱？", "學名的目的是讓全世界科學家使用同一個名字。"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "學名的第一個字是屬名，不是界名；而且使用拉丁文。", "D": "學名由屬名和種小名組成，不包含科名。", "A": "學名就是為了全世界統一使用。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-2-07', 'SC-7B-2', 'classification', '甲、乙、丙、丁四種生物中：甲和乙同屬不同種；甲和丙同科但不同屬；甲和丁同目但不同科。下列敘述何者一定正確？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "乙和甲的親緣關係比丙和甲更遠"}, {"key": "B", "text": "丁和甲屬於不同的目"}, {"key": "C", "text": "丙和丁屬於同一科"}, {"key": "D", "text": "乙和丙屬於同一科"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '甲乙同屬，同屬一定同科，所以乙和甲同科；丙也和甲同科，因此乙和丙屬於同一科。丁和甲不同科，而丙和甲同科，所以丙和丁不同科。分類階層越小相同，親緣關係越近，乙和甲同屬，比丙（只同科）更近。丁和甲同目。', '["同一個「屬」的生物，一定也屬於同一個「科」嗎？", "分類上共同的階層越小，親緣關係越近還是越遠？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "丙和甲同科，丁和甲不同科，所以丙和丁一定不同科。", "A": "乙和甲同屬，比只同科的丙親緣關係更近。", "B": "題目說甲和丁同目。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-2-08', 'SC-7B-2', 'kingdoms', '依照五界分類，細菌屬於哪一界？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "原生生物界"}, {"key": "B", "text": "植物界"}, {"key": "C", "text": "原核生物界"}, {"key": "D", "text": "真菌界"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '細菌的細胞沒有由核膜包圍的細胞核，屬於原核生物界。原生生物界、真菌界、植物界的生物細胞都有細胞核。', '["細菌的細胞有沒有細胞核？", "沒有細胞核的生物屬於哪一界？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "原生生物（如草履蟲）有細胞核。", "D": "真菌（如酵母菌、黴菌）有細胞核。", "B": "細菌不是植物，也沒有細胞核。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-2-09', 'SC-7B-2', 'kingdoms', '香菇沒有葉綠素，不能行光合作用，身體由菌絲構成，靠分解有機物吸收養分。依五界分類，香菇屬於哪一界？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "原生生物界"}, {"key": "B", "text": "植物界"}, {"key": "C", "text": "原核生物界"}, {"key": "D", "text": "真菌界"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '香菇屬於真菌界。真菌的細胞有細胞核和細胞壁，但沒有葉綠素，不能自己製造養分，多數由菌絲構成，靠分解其他有機物獲得養分。', '["香菇能不能自己製造養分？", "黴菌和酵母菌屬於哪一界？香菇和它們很像。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "植物有葉綠素、能行光合作用，香菇不能。", "C": "香菇的細胞有細胞核，不是原核生物。", "A": "香菇是由菌絲構成的真菌，不屬於原生生物界。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-2-10', 'SC-7B-2', 'kingdoms', '原核生物界和其他四界生物的主要差異是什麼？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "原核生物的細胞沒有細胞膜"}, {"key": "B", "text": "原核生物都是多細胞生物"}, {"key": "C", "text": "原核生物沒有遺傳物質"}, {"key": "D", "text": "原核生物的細胞沒有由核膜包圍的細胞核"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '原核生物（如細菌）的細胞有細胞膜，也有遺傳物質（DNA），但遺傳物質沒有被核膜包住，所以沒有細胞核。其他四界生物的細胞都有細胞核（真核細胞）。', '["「原核」這個名字和哪一個構造有關？", "細菌能繁殖，代表它有沒有遺傳物質？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "所有細胞都有細胞膜。", "C": "原核生物也有遺傳物質，只是沒有被核膜包住。", "B": "原核生物多為單細胞生物。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-3-01', 'SC-7B-3', 'population-community', '在生態學中，下列哪一項可以稱為一個「族群」？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "某池塘中所有的魚"}, {"key": "B", "text": "某池塘中的水、陽光和所有生物"}, {"key": "C", "text": "某池塘中所有的吳郭魚"}, {"key": "D", "text": "某池塘中所有的生物"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '族群是指在同一地區、同一時間內，同一種生物的所有個體。某池塘中所有的吳郭魚是同一種生物，屬於族群。「所有的魚」包含很多種魚，不是族群。', '["族群中的個體必須是同一種生物嗎？", "「魚」是一種生物，還是很多種生物？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "池塘中的魚有很多種，不是同一種生物。", "D": "所有的生物是群集。", "B": "生物加上非生物環境是生態系。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-3-02', 'SC-7B-3', 'population-community', '某森林中生活著松鼠、藍鵲、樟樹、蕨類、蕈類和各種昆蟲等所有生物。這些生物合在一起，在生態學中稱為什麼？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "族群"}, {"key": "B", "text": "群集"}, {"key": "C", "text": "生物圈"}, {"key": "D", "text": "生態系"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '同一地區內所有族群（所有種類的生物）的集合稱為群集。若再加上陽光、空氣、水、土壤等非生物因子，才稱為生態系。', '["題目只提到生物，有沒有提到陽光、水等非生物？", "許多不同種的族群合在一起叫什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "族群只包含同一種生物。", "D": "生態系還要包含非生物環境。", "C": "生物圈是地球上所有生態系的總和。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-3-03', 'SC-7B-3', 'food-web', '在「草 → 蚱蜢 → 青蛙 → 蛇」這條食物鏈中，哪一種生物是生產者？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "蛇"}, {"key": "B", "text": "草"}, {"key": "C", "text": "蚱蜢"}, {"key": "D", "text": "青蛙"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '生產者是能行光合作用、自己製造養分的生物，通常是綠色植物。草是這條食物鏈中的生產者，其他都是消費者。', '["哪一種生物能自己製造養分？", "食物鏈的第一個生物通常是什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "蚱蜢吃草，是初級消費者。", "D": "青蛙吃蚱蜢，是次級消費者。", "A": "蛇吃青蛙，是三級消費者。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-3-04', 'SC-7B-3', 'food-web', '在「草 → 蚱蜢 → 青蛙 → 蛇」這條食物鏈中，青蛙屬於第幾級消費者？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "次級消費者"}, {"key": "B", "text": "初級消費者"}, {"key": "C", "text": "生產者"}, {"key": "D", "text": "三級消費者"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '草是生產者；直接吃生產者的蚱蜢是初級消費者；吃初級消費者的青蛙是次級消費者；蛇則是三級消費者。', '["直接吃植物的動物是第幾級消費者？", "青蛙吃的是哪一種生物？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "初級消費者是直接吃生產者的蚱蜢。", "D": "把生產者也算成消費者，多算了一級。", "C": "青蛙不能行光合作用，不是生產者。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-3-05', 'SC-7B-3', 'food-web', '某草原的食物關係如下：兔子和蚱蜢都吃草；青蛙和鳥都吃蚱蜢；蛇吃青蛙和兔子；老鷹吃兔子和蛇。沒有其他取食關係。關於這個食物網，下列敘述何者正確？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "老鷹只屬於三級消費者"}, {"key": "B", "text": "蚱蜢是次級消費者"}, {"key": "C", "text": "共有 4 條食物鏈"}, {"key": "D", "text": "蛇只吃一種生物"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '從草出發找出每條到最高層的路徑：① 草 → 兔子 → 老鷹；② 草 → 兔子 → 蛇 → 老鷹；③ 草 → 蚱蜢 → 青蛙 → 蛇 → 老鷹；④ 草 → 蚱蜢 → 鳥。共 4 條。老鷹在①是次級、在②是三級、在③是四級消費者；蛇吃青蛙和兔子兩種；蚱蜢吃草，是初級消費者。', '["從生產者「草」開始，一條一條往上走到沒有天敵的生物為止。", "鳥有沒有被其他生物吃？", "老鷹在不同的食物鏈中，位置一樣嗎？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "老鷹吃兔子時是次級消費者，吃蛇時是三級或四級消費者，不只一種。", "D": "蛇吃青蛙和兔子兩種生物。", "B": "蚱蜢直接吃草，是初級消費者。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-3-06', 'SC-7B-3', 'energy-flow', '在大多數的生態系中，所有生物所需能量最初的來源是什麼？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "分解者分解的有機物"}, {"key": "B", "text": "生產者製造的氧氣"}, {"key": "C", "text": "太陽的光能"}, {"key": "D", "text": "土壤中的礦物質"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '生產者行光合作用，把太陽的光能轉換成化學能儲存在養分中，再經由食物鏈傳給消費者。所以生態系能量最初來自太陽。', '["生產者製造養分時需要哪一種能量？", "沒有這種能量，植物就不能行光合作用。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "礦物質是物質，不是能量的最初來源。", "B": "氧氣是光合作用的產物，不是能量來源。", "A": "分解者分解的有機物，其能量最初也是來自太陽。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-3-07', 'SC-7B-3', 'energy-flow', '能量沿著食物鏈從一個營養階層傳到下一個營養階層時，會有什麼變化？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "逐級增加，越高階層得到越多能量"}, {"key": "B", "text": "可以在生態系中不斷循環再利用"}, {"key": "C", "text": "保持不變，全部傳給下一階層"}, {"key": "D", "text": "逐級減少，大部分能量在各階層以熱的形式散失"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '每個營養階層的生物會經由呼吸作用消耗能量，並以熱的形式散失到環境中，還有部分沒被吃掉，所以只有一小部分能量能傳到下一階層。能量是單向流動、逐級減少的，無法循環；會循環的是物質。', '["生物活動時會消耗能量嗎？消耗掉的能量變成什麼？", "在生態系中，會循環的是「物質」還是「能量」？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "能量在傳遞過程中會散失，所以越往上越少。", "C": "每一階層都會消耗、散失能量，不可能全部傳下去。", "B": "物質可以循環，能量是單向流動、無法循環。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-3-08', 'SC-7B-3', 'energy-flow', '在「草 → 蚱蜢 → 青蛙 → 蛇」這條食物鏈中，假設每一營養階層只有 10% 的能量能傳到下一個營養階層。若草固定了 50000 單位的能量，蛇最多大約能獲得多少單位的能量？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "5 單位"}, {"key": "B", "text": "50 單位"}, {"key": "C", "text": "500 單位"}, {"key": "D", "text": "5000 單位"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '草 → 蚱蜢：50000 × 10% = 5000；蚱蜢 → 青蛙：5000 × 10% = 500；青蛙 → 蛇：500 × 10% = 50。共傳遞 3 次，所以蛇約獲得 50 單位。', '["從草到蛇，能量一共傳遞了幾次？", "每傳一次就乘以 10%。"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "只傳遞到青蛙，少算了一次。", "D": "只傳遞到蚱蜢，少算了兩次。", "A": "多算了一次傳遞（乘了 4 次 10%）。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-3-09', 'SC-7B-3', 'ecosystem-conservation', '下列陸域生態系中，哪一種通常生物種類最多、生物多樣性最高？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "草原"}, {"key": "B", "text": "沙漠"}, {"key": "C", "text": "凍原"}, {"key": "D", "text": "熱帶雨林"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '熱帶雨林終年高溫多雨、陽光充足，植物生長茂盛，能提供多樣的棲地和食物，因此生物種類非常多，是陸域生態系中生物多樣性最高的。', '["哪一種生態系的溫度和雨量最有利植物生長？", "植物越多，能提供給動物的食物和棲地就越多還是越少？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "沙漠雨量很少，生物種類較少。", "A": "草原雨量較少，缺乏高大樹木，生物種類不如熱帶雨林。", "C": "凍原氣溫極低，生物種類很少。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-7B-3-10', 'SC-7B-3', 'ecosystem-conservation', '外來入侵種可能與本土生物競爭食物和棲地，甚至造成本土生物滅絕。下列哪一種做法最有助於保護本地的生物多樣性？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "把溼地填平，改建成停車場"}, {"key": "B", "text": "引進大量外來魚種放入溪流，增加物種數量"}, {"key": "C", "text": "到野外捕捉稀有動物帶回家飼養"}, {"key": "D", "text": "不任意把寵物或外來物種野放到野外"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '任意野放寵物或外來種，可能使牠們成為入侵種，排擠本土生物。不隨意放生、不野放寵物，是保護生物多樣性的做法。引進外來種、破壞棲地、捕捉野生動物都會傷害生態。', '["哪一個做法可以避免外來入侵種出現？", "破壞棲地對生物多樣性有什麼影響？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "外來魚種可能成為入侵種，排擠本土魚類。", "A": "填平溼地會破壞許多生物的棲地。", "C": "捕捉野生稀有動物會使野外族群減少。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-1-01', 'SC-8A-1', 'measurement', '用最小刻度為 0.1 公分（1 毫米）的直尺測量一支鉛筆的長度，下列哪一個記錄最合理？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "12.350 公分"}, {"key": "B", "text": "12.35 公分"}, {"key": "C", "text": "12 公分"}, {"key": "D", "text": "12.3 公分"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '測量時要記錄到最小刻度的下一位（估計值）。最小刻度是 0.1 公分，所以要記錄到 0.01 公分，例如 12.35 公分，其中最後一位 5 是估計值。', '["測量記錄時，要讀到最小刻度，還是再多估計一位？", "最小刻度 0.1 公分的下一位是哪一位？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "只記錄到 1 公分，沒有讀到最小刻度。", "D": "只讀到最小刻度，沒有多估計一位。", "A": "多寫了一位，這位數字無法從直尺估計出來。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-1-02', 'SC-8A-1', 'measurement', '用排水法測量一顆小石頭的體積：量筒內原本裝有 30.0 毫升的水，把石頭完全沉入水中後，水面上升到 42.5 毫升。這顆石頭的體積是多少？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "42.5 立方公分"}, {"key": "B", "text": "12.5 立方公分"}, {"key": "C", "text": "30.0 立方公分"}, {"key": "D", "text": "72.5 立方公分"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '石頭沉入水中會排開與自身體積相同的水，所以石頭體積 = 42.5 − 30.0 = 12.5 毫升 = 12.5 立方公分（1 毫升 = 1 立方公分）。', '["水面上升的部分代表什麼？", "1 毫升等於多少立方公分？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "42.5 是水加石頭的總體積，要減去原本的水。", "D": "把兩個讀數相加了，應該相減。", "C": "30.0 是原本水的體積。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-1-03', 'SC-8A-1', 'density', '一塊金屬的質量是 54 公克，體積是 20 立方公分，它的密度是多少？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "2.7 公克/立方公分"}, {"key": "B", "text": "0.37 公克/立方公分"}, {"key": "C", "text": "74 公克/立方公分"}, {"key": "D", "text": "1080 公克/立方公分"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '密度 = 質量 ÷ 體積 = 54 ÷ 20 = 2.7 公克/立方公分。', '["密度的公式是什麼？", "看單位：公克/立方公分，是誰除以誰？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "把體積除以質量，公式顛倒了。", "D": "把質量乘以體積了。", "C": "把質量和體積相加了。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-1-04', 'SC-8A-1', 'density', '有甲、乙、丙三個不吸水的實心物體：甲的質量 20 公克、體積 25 立方公分；乙的質量 30 公克、體積 20 立方公分；丙的質量 45 公克、體積 50 立方公分。已知水的密度是 1 公克/立方公分，把它們分別放入水中，哪一個會沉到水底？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "三個都會浮在水面"}, {"key": "B", "text": "甲"}, {"key": "C", "text": "乙"}, {"key": "D", "text": "丙"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '甲的密度 = 20 ÷ 25 = 0.8；乙 = 30 ÷ 20 = 1.5；丙 = 45 ÷ 50 = 0.9（單位都是公克/立方公分）。密度比水大的物體會下沉，所以只有乙會沉到水底。', '["物體浮沉要比較什麼？", "先算出三者的密度，再和水的密度比較。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "甲的密度 0.8，比水小，會浮起來。", "D": "丙質量最大，但密度 0.9 比水小，會浮起來。浮沉看密度，不是看質量。", "A": "乙的密度 1.5 比水大，會下沉。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-1-05', 'SC-8A-1', 'density', '一塊金屬的質量是 158 公克。把它放入裝有 50.0 毫升水的量筒中完全浸沒，水面上升到 70.0 毫升。已知幾種金屬的密度（公克/立方公分）：鋁 2.7、鐵 7.9、銅 8.9、鉛 11.3。這塊金屬最可能是哪一種？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "銅"}, {"key": "B", "text": "鐵"}, {"key": "C", "text": "鋁"}, {"key": "D", "text": "鉛"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '金屬體積 = 70.0 − 50.0 = 20.0 立方公分；密度 = 158 ÷ 20 = 7.9 公克/立方公分，和鐵的密度相同。密度是物質的特性，可以用來判斷物質的種類。', '["要算密度，還缺哪一個量？可以用排水法求出來。", "把算出來的密度和表中數值比對。"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "把 70.0 當成金屬體積：158 ÷ 70 ≈ 2.3，最接近鋁；應該用水面上升的量。", "A": "沒有實際計算密度就猜測；算出的 7.9 與銅的 8.9 不符。", "D": "以為質量大密度就一定大；算出的 7.9 與鉛的 11.3 不符。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-1-06', 'SC-8A-1', 'states-mixture', '下列哪一種物質是純物質？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "空氣"}, {"key": "B", "text": "汽水"}, {"key": "C", "text": "蒸餾水"}, {"key": "D", "text": "海水"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '純物質只由一種物質組成，有固定的性質，例如蒸餾水。空氣含有氮、氧等多種氣體；海水含有水和多種鹽類；汽水含有水、糖、二氧化碳等，都是混合物。', '["純物質由幾種物質組成？", "海水裡除了水，還有什麼？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "空氣由氮氣、氧氣等多種氣體組成，是混合物。", "D": "海水溶有鹽類，是混合物。", "B": "汽水含有糖、二氧化碳和水等，是混合物。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-1-07', 'SC-8A-1', 'states-mixture', '有一包混有沙子的食鹽，想從中得到純的食鹽，下列步驟順序何者最正確？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "蒸發 → 溶解 → 過濾"}, {"key": "B", "text": "過濾 → 溶解 → 蒸發"}, {"key": "C", "text": "溶解 → 過濾 → 蒸發"}, {"key": "D", "text": "溶解 → 蒸發 → 過濾"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '食鹽可以溶於水，沙子不溶於水。先加水溶解食鹽；再過濾，把不溶的沙子留在濾紙上；最後加熱蒸發濾液中的水，就能得到食鹽。', '["食鹽和沙子，哪一個能溶於水？", "過濾可以分開哪兩類東西？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "還沒溶解就過濾，食鹽和沙子都是固體，會一起留在濾紙上。", "A": "一開始就蒸發沒有意義，因為還沒有加水。", "D": "先蒸發會讓食鹽又和沙子混在一起，無法用過濾分開。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-1-08', 'SC-8A-1', 'concentration', '把 20 公克的糖完全溶解在 80 公克的水中，這杯糖水的重量百分濃度是多少？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "80%"}, {"key": "B", "text": "20%"}, {"key": "C", "text": "0.2%"}, {"key": "D", "text": "25%"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '重量百分濃度 = 溶質質量 ÷ 溶液質量 × 100%。溶液質量 = 20 + 80 = 100 公克，所以濃度 = 20 ÷ 100 × 100% = 20%。', '["溶液的質量包含哪些部分？", "分母是溶劑的質量，還是溶液的質量？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "用溶質 ÷ 溶劑（20 ÷ 80），分母應該是溶液質量。", "A": "把水占的百分比當成濃度了。", "C": "算出 0.2 後忘了乘以 100%，就直接加上百分號。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-1-09', 'SC-8A-1', 'concentration', '300 公克、重量百分濃度 15% 的食鹽水中，含有多少公克的食鹽？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "255 公克"}, {"key": "B", "text": "20 公克"}, {"key": "C", "text": "45 公克"}, {"key": "D", "text": "15 公克"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '溶質質量 = 溶液質量 × 濃度 = 300 × 15% = 45 公克。', '["濃度 15% 代表每 100 公克溶液中有多少公克溶質？", "300 公克是溶液的質量，用它乘以濃度。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "用 300 ÷ 15 計算，方法錯誤。", "A": "255 公克是水的質量，不是食鹽。", "D": "把百分比數字直接當成公克數。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-1-10', 'SC-8A-1', 'concentration', '有 200 公克、重量百分濃度 10% 的食鹽水，要加入多少公克的水，才能稀釋成重量百分濃度 8% 的食鹽水？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "250 公克"}, {"key": "B", "text": "20 公克"}, {"key": "C", "text": "50 公克"}, {"key": "D", "text": "40 公克"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '加水時溶質（食鹽）的質量不變：200 × 10% = 20 公克。稀釋後溶液質量 = 20 ÷ 8% = 250 公克，所以要加入 250 − 200 = 50 公克的水。', '["加水稀釋時，哪一個量不會改變？", "先求出食鹽有幾公克，再算出 8% 時溶液應有多重。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "用 200 × (10 − 8) ÷ 10 計算，分母應該用稀釋後的濃度 8。", "B": "20 公克是食鹽的質量，不是要加入的水量。", "A": "250 公克是稀釋後溶液的總質量，還要減去原本的 200 公克。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-2-01', 'SC-8A-2', 'wave-speed', '一個水波的頻率是 5 赫（Hz），波長是 2 公尺，這個水波的波速是多少？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "0.4 公尺/秒"}, {"key": "B", "text": "7 公尺/秒"}, {"key": "C", "text": "10 公尺/秒"}, {"key": "D", "text": "2.5 公尺/秒"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '波速 = 頻率 × 波長，v = fλ = 5 × 2 = 10 公尺/秒。', '["波速、頻率和波長之間的關係式是什麼？", "頻率 5 赫代表每秒產生幾個完整的波？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "用頻率除以波長（5 ÷ 2），應該相乘。", "B": "把頻率和波長相加了。", "A": "用波長除以頻率。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-2-02', 'SC-8A-2', 'wave-speed', '小明手握繩子的一端上下抖動，每秒抖動 4 次，繩上相鄰兩個波峰之間的距離是 0.5 公尺。繩波的波速是多少？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "0.125 公尺/秒"}, {"key": "B", "text": "8 公尺/秒"}, {"key": "C", "text": "4.5 公尺/秒"}, {"key": "D", "text": "2 公尺/秒"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '每秒抖動 4 次，頻率 f = 4 赫；相鄰兩波峰的距離就是一個波長，λ = 0.5 公尺。波速 v = fλ = 4 × 0.5 = 2 公尺/秒。', '["相鄰兩個波峰的距離是什麼物理量？", "每秒抖動 4 次，頻率是多少？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "用 4 ÷ 0.5 計算，應該相乘。", "A": "用 0.5 ÷ 4 計算，應該相乘。", "C": "把頻率和波長相加了。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-2-03', 'SC-8A-2', 'wave-speed', '在同一條繩子上（拉繩子的力量不變），小華以 2 赫的頻率抖動時，繩波的波長是 1.2 公尺。若改用 4 赫的頻率抖動，繩波的波長會變成多少？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "0.3 公尺"}, {"key": "B", "text": "2.4 公尺"}, {"key": "C", "text": "1.2 公尺"}, {"key": "D", "text": "0.6 公尺"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '波速由介質決定，同一條繩子、拉力不變，波速不變。原波速 v = 2 × 1.2 = 2.4 公尺/秒。頻率變為 4 赫時，波長 λ = v ÷ f = 2.4 ÷ 4 = 0.6 公尺。頻率加倍，波長變為一半。', '["同一條繩子，改變抖動頻率時，哪一個量不會變？", "先算出原本的波速。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "以為頻率變大，波長也跟著變大。", "C": "以為波長不會改變，其實不變的是波速。", "A": "把波長變成四分之一，計算錯誤。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-2-04', 'SC-8A-2', 'sound', '聲音無法在下列哪一種環境中傳播？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "真空中"}, {"key": "B", "text": "空氣中"}, {"key": "C", "text": "鋼鐵中"}, {"key": "D", "text": "水中"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '聲音是一種力學波，需要介質（固體、液體或氣體）才能傳播。真空中沒有介質，所以聲音無法傳播。', '["聲音傳播需不需要介質？", "太空中的太空人為什麼要用無線電溝通？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "水是液體介質，聲音可以在水中傳播。", "C": "固體可以傳播聲音，而且傳得比空氣快。", "B": "我們平常聽到的聲音大多就是經由空氣傳播的。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-2-05', 'SC-8A-2', 'sound', '彈吉他時，用更大的力量撥同一根弦，聲音聽起來更大聲。這時主要改變的是什麼？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "振幅變大，響度變大"}, {"key": "B", "text": "波速變快，聲音傳得更遠"}, {"key": "C", "text": "波形改變，音色改變"}, {"key": "D", "text": "頻率變高，音調變高"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '用更大的力量撥弦，弦振動的幅度（振幅）變大，聲音的響度就變大。音調由頻率決定，音色由波形決定，撥同一根弦時這兩者基本不變；聲音在空氣中的波速也不會因此改變。', '["聲音的大小（響度）和波的哪一個特性有關？", "撥同一根弦，振動的快慢會明顯改變嗎？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "音調由頻率決定，撥同一根弦，頻率不會因為用力而明顯改變。", "C": "音色由樂器的材質和構造決定，同一把吉他音色不變。", "B": "聲速由介質決定，與撥弦力量無關。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-2-06', 'SC-8A-2', 'sound', '小玲站在一座山壁前大喊一聲，2 秒後聽到回聲。若當時聲音在空氣中的速率是 340 公尺/秒，小玲和山壁之間的距離大約是多少？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "170 公尺"}, {"key": "B", "text": "1360 公尺"}, {"key": "C", "text": "340 公尺"}, {"key": "D", "text": "680 公尺"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '回聲是聲音碰到山壁反射回來，2 秒內聲音走了一個來回。來回距離 = 340 × 2 = 680 公尺，單程距離 = 680 ÷ 2 = 340 公尺。', '["聽到回聲時，聲音走了多遠？是單程還是來回？", "先算出 2 秒內聲音走的總距離。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "680 公尺是來回的距離，還要除以 2。", "A": "多除了一次 2。", "B": "把時間當成單程時間又乘了 2。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-2-07', 'SC-8A-2', 'reflection-refraction', '一束光射向平面鏡，入射光與鏡面的夾角是 30°。反射角是多少度？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "30°"}, {"key": "B", "text": "120°"}, {"key": "C", "text": "90°"}, {"key": "D", "text": "60°"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '入射角和反射角都是光線與「法線」的夾角，法線和鏡面垂直。入射光與鏡面夾 30°，所以入射角 = 90° − 30° = 60°。依反射定律，反射角 = 入射角 = 60°。', '["入射角是光線和鏡面的夾角，還是和法線的夾角？", "法線和鏡面的夾角是幾度？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "把光線和鏡面的夾角當成入射角，應該用和法線的夾角。", "C": "把法線和鏡面的夾角當成反射角了。", "B": "把入射角和反射角相加成 120°，那是入射光和反射光的夾角。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-2-08', 'SC-8A-2', 'reflection-refraction', '一束光由空氣斜射入水中時，光的行進方向會如何改變？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "偏向法線，折射角小於入射角"}, {"key": "B", "text": "不改變方向，直線前進"}, {"key": "C", "text": "偏離法線，折射角大於入射角"}, {"key": "D", "text": "全部反射回空氣中"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '光由空氣斜射入水中時，因為光在水中的速率比在空氣中慢，行進方向會偏向法線，折射角小於入射角。', '["光在空氣和水中，哪裡跑得比較慢？", "光進入跑得比較慢的物質時，會偏向還是偏離法線？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "只有垂直入射時才不改變方向，斜射時會折射。", "C": "這是光由水中射入空氣時的情況。", "D": "光由空氣射入水中時，大部分光會進入水中，不會全部反射。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-2-09', 'SC-8A-2', 'lens-mirror', '小明站在一面大平面鏡前 2 公尺處，他在鏡中的像和他本人之間的距離是多少？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "8 公尺"}, {"key": "B", "text": "4 公尺"}, {"key": "C", "text": "1 公尺"}, {"key": "D", "text": "2 公尺"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '平面鏡成像時，像到鏡面的距離等於物體到鏡面的距離。小明離鏡子 2 公尺，像在鏡子後方 2 公尺，所以像和小明相距 2 + 2 = 4 公尺。', '["平面鏡的像在鏡子後面多遠？", "題目問的是像到「人」的距離，不是像到鏡子的距離。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "2 公尺是像到鏡子的距離。", "C": "以為像在人和鏡子的中間。", "A": "把距離多乘了一次 2。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-2-10', 'SC-8A-2', 'lens-mirror', '一個凸透鏡的焦距是 10 公分。把一支點燃的蠟燭放在透鏡前 30 公分處，在透鏡另一側移動紙屏，可以在紙屏上看到清楚的像。這個像的性質為何？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "倒立、放大的實像"}, {"key": "B", "text": "正立、縮小的虛像"}, {"key": "C", "text": "正立、放大的虛像"}, {"key": "D", "text": "倒立、縮小的實像"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '物距 30 公分大於兩倍焦距（20 公分）。凸透鏡的物體在兩倍焦距之外時，會在另一側的一倍焦距與兩倍焦距之間形成倒立、縮小的實像，可以用紙屏接收。照相機就是利用這個原理。', '["先比較物距和焦距、兩倍焦距的大小。", "能在紙屏上接收到的像是實像還是虛像？實像是正立還是倒立？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "物體在一倍焦距和兩倍焦距之間時才成倒立放大的實像。", "C": "物體在焦點以內才成正立放大的虛像，而且虛像無法用紙屏接收。", "B": "凸透鏡不會形成正立縮小的虛像；而且這個像能用紙屏接收，是實像。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-3-01', 'SC-8A-3', 'thermometer', '常見的酒精溫度計能用來測量溫度，主要是利用什麼原理？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "液體熱脹冷縮"}, {"key": "B", "text": "玻璃受熱會導電"}, {"key": "C", "text": "液體受熱會沸騰"}, {"key": "D", "text": "液體受熱會變色"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '液體溫度計是利用液體（例如酒精或水銀）熱脹冷縮的性質：溫度升高時液體體積膨脹，液柱上升；溫度降低時液柱下降，由液柱高度讀出溫度。', '["溫度計的液柱為什麼會上升或下降？", "物體受熱時體積通常會怎麼變？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "酒精溫度計的液體通常是染色的，顏色不會隨溫度改變。", "C": "溫度計中的液體在測量範圍內不會沸騰。", "B": "玻璃不是導體，溫度計也不是利用導電原理。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-3-02', 'SC-8A-3', 'thermometer', '攝氏溫度 C 和華氏溫度 F 的換算關係是 F = 9/5 × C + 32。攝氏 40 度相當於華氏幾度？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "4.4 度"}, {"key": "B", "text": "40 度"}, {"key": "C", "text": "72 度"}, {"key": "D", "text": "104 度"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '代入公式：F = 9/5 × 40 + 32 = 72 + 32 = 104，所以攝氏 40 度等於華氏 104 度。', '["把 C = 40 代入公式。", "先算乘法，再加 32。"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "只算了 9/5 × 40，忘了加 32。", "B": "以為兩種溫標的數值相同。", "A": "把公式用反了：(40 − 32) × 5/9 ≈ 4.4。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-3-03', 'SC-8A-3', 'specific-heat', '要把 200 公克的水從 20°C 加熱到 50°C，水需要吸收多少卡的熱量？（水的比熱為 1 卡/(公克·°C)）', '[{"key": "A", "text": "10000 卡"}, {"key": "B", "text": "4000 卡"}, {"key": "C", "text": "6000 卡"}, {"key": "D", "text": "30 卡"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '熱量 H = m × s × ΔT = 200 × 1 × (50 − 20) = 200 × 30 = 6000 卡。', '["熱量的公式是什麼？", "溫度變化 ΔT 是末溫減初溫。"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "把末溫 50°C 當成溫度變化。", "B": "把初溫 20°C 當成溫度變化。", "D": "只算了溫度變化，忘了乘上質量。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-3-04', 'SC-8A-3', 'specific-heat', '夏天中午在海邊，沙灘摸起來很燙，海水卻比較涼。沙子和海水照到的陽光差不多，造成這種差異的主要原因是什麼？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "水完全不吸收太陽的熱"}, {"key": "B", "text": "沙子的比熱比水大，吸收相同熱量時溫度上升較多"}, {"key": "C", "text": "沙子的比熱比水小，吸收相同熱量時溫度上升較多"}, {"key": "D", "text": "沙子的質量一定比海水大"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '由 H = m × s × ΔT 可知，質量和吸收熱量相同時，比熱越小，溫度變化越大。沙子的比熱比水小很多，所以同樣照太陽，沙子溫度上升得比海水多。', '["吸收相同熱量時，比熱大的物質溫度變化大還是小？", "用 H = m × s × ΔT 想一想，s 越小，ΔT 會怎樣？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "比熱越大，溫度越不容易改變，應該是沙子比熱較小。", "A": "水也會吸收太陽的熱，只是溫度上升較少。", "D": "海水的量遠比表層沙子多，而且質量不是這題的主因。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-3-05', 'SC-8A-3', 'specific-heat', '某金屬塊的質量是 100 公克，吸收了 450 卡的熱量後，溫度由 20°C 上升到 70°C。這種金屬的比熱是多少？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "0.09 卡/(公克·°C)"}, {"key": "B", "text": "約 0.064 卡/(公克·°C)"}, {"key": "C", "text": "4.5 卡/(公克·°C)"}, {"key": "D", "text": "0.9 卡/(公克·°C)"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '由 H = m × s × ΔT，s = H ÷ (m × ΔT) = 450 ÷ (100 × 50) = 450 ÷ 5000 = 0.09 卡/(公克·°C)。', '["溫度變化是多少？", "把 H = m × s × ΔT 改寫成求 s 的式子。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "分母算錯，例如 450 ÷ 500 = 0.9，應該是 450 ÷ (100 × 50) = 0.09，小數點差了一位。", "B": "把末溫 70°C 當成溫度變化：450 ÷ (100 × 70)。", "C": "忘了除以溫度變化，只算了 450 ÷ 100。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-3-06', 'SC-8A-3', 'specific-heat', '甲、乙兩物體的質量比為 2 : 1，比熱比為 1 : 3。若兩者吸收相同的熱量（沒有狀態改變），甲、乙上升的溫度比是多少？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "2 : 3"}, {"key": "B", "text": "3 : 2"}, {"key": "C", "text": "1 : 6"}, {"key": "D", "text": "6 : 1"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '由 H = m × s × ΔT，得 ΔT = H ÷ (m × s)。熱量相同時，ΔT 與 m × s 成反比。甲的 m × s = 2 × 1 = 2，乙的 m × s = 1 × 3 = 3，所以 ΔT甲 : ΔT乙 = 1/2 : 1/3 = 3 : 2。', '["熱量相同時，溫度變化和質量、比熱的乘積成正比還是反比？", "先算出甲、乙的 m × s 各是多少。"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "把 m × s 的比當成溫度變化比，忘了是反比。", "D": "把質量比和比熱比相除後直接當答案。", "C": "計算反比時弄錯。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-3-07', 'SC-8A-3', 'thermal-equilibrium', '把 100 公克、80°C 的熱水和 300 公克、20°C 的冷水混合。若不考慮熱量散失，達到熱平衡時的溫度是多少？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "35°C"}, {"key": "B", "text": "65°C"}, {"key": "C", "text": "50°C"}, {"key": "D", "text": "20°C"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '熱水放出的熱量 = 冷水吸收的熱量。設末溫為 T：100 × 1 × (80 − T) = 300 × 1 × (T − 20)，8000 − 100T = 300T − 6000，400T = 14000，T = 35°C。', '["熱平衡時，熱水放熱和冷水吸熱有什麼關係？", "冷水比較多，末溫會比較接近哪一個溫度？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "直接取 80 和 20 的平均，沒有考慮兩者質量不同。", "B": "把熱水和冷水的質量對調了。", "D": "以為冷水比較多，末溫就等於冷水的溫度；熱水放熱後一定會使冷水升溫。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-3-08', 'SC-8A-3', 'thermal-equilibrium', '實驗：把 500 公克、加熱到 90°C 的金屬塊，放入裝有 450 公克、20°C 水的保溫杯中，攪拌後水和金屬塊的最終溫度都是 27°C。若不考慮熱量散失及杯子吸熱，這種金屬的比熱是多少？（水的比熱為 1 卡/(公克·°C)）', '[{"key": "A", "text": "0.9 卡/(公克·°C)"}, {"key": "B", "text": "0.09 卡/(公克·°C)"}, {"key": "C", "text": "0.1 卡/(公克·°C)"}, {"key": "D", "text": "10 卡/(公克·°C)"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '水吸收的熱量 = 450 × 1 × (27 − 20) = 3150 卡。金屬放出的熱量 = 500 × s × (90 − 27) = 31500 × s。熱平衡時兩者相等：31500s = 3150，s = 0.1 卡/(公克·°C)。', '["先算水吸收了多少熱量。", "金屬放出的熱量等於水吸收的熱量，金屬的溫度下降了多少？"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "把金屬的溫度變化算成 90 − 20 = 70°C，金屬是從 90°C 降到 27°C。", "A": "把金屬的溫度變化也當成 7°C，結果只剩質量比 450 ÷ 500。", "D": "把等式兩邊弄反，算成 (500 × 63) ÷ (450 × 7)。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-3-09', 'SC-8A-3', 'heat-transfer', '把金屬湯匙放進熱湯中，過一會兒，露在湯外面的湯匙柄也變熱了。這主要是哪一種熱的傳播方式？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "對流"}, {"key": "B", "text": "蒸發"}, {"key": "C", "text": "輻射"}, {"key": "D", "text": "傳導"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '熱沿著固體由高溫處傳到低溫處，物質本身不流動，這種方式叫傳導。金屬是熱的良導體，所以湯匙柄很快變熱。', '["湯匙是固體還是流體？", "熱在固體中傳播時，物質本身會流動嗎？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "對流是液體或氣體流動傳熱，湯匙是固體。", "C": "輻射不需要介質，例如太陽的熱傳到地球；這裡熱是沿著湯匙傳遞。", "B": "蒸發是液體變成氣體的現象，不是熱的傳播方式。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8A-3-10', 'SC-8A-3', 'heat-transfer', '房間裡的冷氣機通常裝在牆壁的高處，這樣設計的主要原因是什麼？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "冷空氣密度較大會下沉，能形成對流使整個房間變涼"}, {"key": "B", "text": "冷氣機裝在高處可以增加熱的傳導"}, {"key": "C", "text": "高處較容易進行熱輻射"}, {"key": "D", "text": "冷空氣密度較小會上升，所以要從高處吹出"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '冷空氣密度較大，會往下沉；熱空氣密度較小，會上升。冷氣機裝在高處，吹出的冷空氣下沉、熱空氣上升，形成對流，讓整個房間的溫度較快降低。', '["冷空氣和熱空氣，哪一個比較重（密度較大）？", "空氣流動傳熱屬於哪一種熱的傳播方式？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "冷空氣密度較大，是會下沉而不是上升。", "C": "冷氣使房間變涼主要靠空氣對流，不是輻射。", "B": "空氣是熱的不良導體，冷氣主要靠對流，不是傳導。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8B-1-01', 'SC-8B-1', 'mass-conservation', '在一個完全密閉的玻璃瓶中放入少量鋼絲絨和空氣，連同瓶子一起稱重為 250.0 公克。用放大鏡聚光使鋼絲絨燃燒，冷卻後再稱一次，質量應為多少？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "大於 250.0 公克"}, {"key": "B", "text": "小於 250.0 公克"}, {"key": "C", "text": "250.0 公克"}, {"key": "D", "text": "無法判斷，要看鋼絲絨燒掉多少"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '化學反應遵守質量守恆定律：反應前後原子的種類和數目都不變，所以總質量不變。瓶子完全密閉，沒有物質進出，因此稱得的總質量仍是 250.0 公克。', '["瓶子是密閉的，有沒有物質跑出去或跑進來？", "想一想質量守恆定律：反應前後原子的數目會改變嗎？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "以為鋼絲絨和氧結合後會「多出」質量，忽略瓶內的氧氣本來就被算在總質量裡。", "B": "以為燃燒會讓東西「燒掉不見」。", "D": "以為總質量和反應程度有關，其實密閉系統不論反應多少總質量都不變。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8B-1-02', 'SC-8B-1', 'mass-conservation', '將 2.4 公克的鎂帶在空氣中完全燃燒，得到 4.0 公克的白色氧化鎂。參與反應的氧氣質量是多少公克？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "2.4 公克"}, {"key": "B", "text": "4.0 公克"}, {"key": "C", "text": "6.4 公克"}, {"key": "D", "text": "1.6 公克"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '依質量守恆定律：鎂的質量 + 氧氣的質量 = 氧化鎂的質量。所以氧氣質量 = 4.0 − 2.4 = 1.6 公克。燃燒後質量變大，是因為鎂和空氣中的氧結合了。', '["反應物有哪些？生成物是什麼？", "反應物的總質量要等於生成物的總質量。"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "把鎂的質量當成氧氣的質量。", "B": "把生成物氧化鎂的質量當成答案。", "C": "把兩個質量相加，而不是相減。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8B-1-03', 'SC-8B-1', 'mass-conservation', '小芸做兩組實驗：甲組在開口燒杯中讓小蘇打和醋反應，反應後燒杯與內容物的總質量減少；乙組把相同的藥品放在瓶口套緊氣球的密閉瓶中反應，反應後總質量不變。下列推論何者最合理？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "乙組質量不變是因為在密閉容器中，小蘇打和醋根本不會發生反應"}, {"key": "B", "text": "甲組的反應不遵守質量守恆定律，只有乙組在密閉容器中的反應才遵守"}, {"key": "C", "text": "甲組質量減少是因為部分原子在反應過程中消失了，所以總質量變少"}, {"key": "D", "text": "甲組質量減少是因為生成的二氧化碳氣體逸散到空氣中，兩組反應都遵守質量守恆定律"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '所有化學反應都遵守質量守恆定律。小蘇打和醋反應會產生二氧化碳氣體，在開口燒杯中氣體跑到空氣裡，沒有被稱到，所以秤得的質量變少；在密閉容器中氣體留在裡面，總質量就不變。乙組氣球會脹大，表示反應確實有發生。', '["這個反應會產生什麼狀態的物質？", "開口和密閉的差別在於：生成的物質能不能被一起稱到。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "以為質量守恆只在某些條件下成立，其實是秤量時漏掉了逸散的氣體。", "C": "以為原子會在反應中消失，其實原子只是重新排列組合。", "A": "忽略氣球脹大代表有氣體產生，反應確實有發生。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8B-1-04', 'SC-8B-1', 'balancing', '氫氣燃燒的反應式為 a H₂ + O₂ → b H₂O，若 a、b 為最簡整數，則 a、b 分別是多少？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "a = 1、b = 2"}, {"key": "B", "text": "a = 1、b = 1"}, {"key": "C", "text": "a = 2、b = 2"}, {"key": "D", "text": "a = 2、b = 1"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '左邊 O₂ 有 2 個氧原子，所以右邊要 2 個 H₂O，b = 2；2 個 H₂O 有 4 個氫原子，左邊需要 2 個 H₂，a = 2。平衡後為 2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O。', '["先數一數左右兩邊的氧原子數目。", "氧原子平衡後，再讓氫原子也相等。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "沒有平衡氧原子，左邊 2 個 O、右邊只有 1 個 O。", "D": "只平衡了氫原子的一半，右邊 1 個 H₂O 只有 2 個 H 和 1 個 O。", "A": "右邊 2 個 H₂O 有 4 個 H，但左邊只有 2 個 H。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8B-1-05', 'SC-8B-1', 'balancing', '丙烷燃燒的反應式為 C₃H₈ + a O₂ → b CO₂ + c H₂O。平衡後（最簡整數），a + b + c 等於多少？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "12"}, {"key": "B", "text": "9"}, {"key": "C", "text": "13"}, {"key": "D", "text": "10"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '先平衡碳：b = 3；再平衡氫：8 = 2c，c = 4；最後平衡氧：右邊氧原子 = 3 × 2 + 4 × 1 = 10，所以 a = 5。a + b + c = 5 + 3 + 4 = 12。', '["建議先平衡只出現在一種反應物中的碳和氫。", "最後才平衡氧，右邊的氧原子共有幾個？"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "把氧原子數 10 當成 a，或是把係數算錯。", "C": "氧原子計算時多算了一個。", "B": "把 c 算成 8 ÷ 2 以外的數，或漏算一項。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8B-1-06', 'SC-8B-1', 'balancing', '關於反應式 2CO + O₂ → 2CO₂ 的意義，下列敘述何者正確？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "反應前後分子的總數目不變"}, {"key": "B", "text": "2 公克一氧化碳與 1 公克氧氣反應，生成 2 公克二氧化碳"}, {"key": "C", "text": "反應後生成了新的原子種類"}, {"key": "D", "text": "每 2 個一氧化碳分子與 1 個氧分子反應，生成 2 個二氧化碳分子"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '反應式中的係數表示粒子（分子）數目的比例，也就是莫耳數的比例，不是質量比。反應前有 2 + 1 = 3 個分子，反應後有 2 個分子，分子數可以改變，但原子的種類和數目不變。', '["係數代表的是粒子數目還是質量？", "數一數反應前、後各有幾個分子、幾個原子。"]'::jsonb, '{"B": "把係數誤當成質量比。", "A": "把「原子數目不變」誤記成「分子數目不變」，實際上 3 個分子變成 2 個。", "C": "化學反應只是原子重新排列，不會產生新的原子種類。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8B-1-07', 'SC-8B-1', 'mole', '已知原子量 C = 12、H = 1、O = 16，葡萄糖 C₆H₁₂O₆ 的分子量是多少？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "96"}, {"key": "B", "text": "168"}, {"key": "C", "text": "29"}, {"key": "D", "text": "180"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '分子量等於分子中所有原子的原子量總和：12 × 6 + 1 × 12 + 16 × 6 = 72 + 12 + 96 = 180。', '["分子量要把每一個原子都算進去。", "分別算出 6 個碳、12 個氫、6 個氧的原子量總和。"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "只把 C、H、O 各一個的原子量相加（12 + 1 + 16）。", "A": "只算了氧的部分。", "B": "漏算了 12 個氫原子。"}'::jsonb, 1, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8B-1-08', 'SC-8B-1', 'mole', '甲烷燃燒的反應式為 CH₄ + 2O₂ → CO₂ + 2H₂O。已知原子量 C = 12、H = 1、O = 16，8 公克甲烷完全燃燒，可生成多少公克的水？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "8 公克"}, {"key": "B", "text": "36 公克"}, {"key": "C", "text": "18 公克"}, {"key": "D", "text": "9 公克"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '甲烷分子量 = 12 + 4 = 16，8 公克甲烷是 8 ÷ 16 = 0.5 莫耳。由係數比 CH₄ : H₂O = 1 : 2，生成水 1 莫耳。水的分子量 18，所以生成 1 × 18 = 18 公克。', '["先把 8 公克甲烷換算成莫耳數。", "係數比就是莫耳數比，CH₄ 和 H₂O 的比是多少？", "最後把水的莫耳數乘上水的分子量。"]'::jsonb, '{"D": "忘了乘上係數 2，以為甲烷和水的莫耳數相同。", "B": "把甲烷當成 1 莫耳。", "A": "以為反應物和某一個生成物的質量相同。"}'::jsonb, 3, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8B-1-09', 'SC-8B-1', 'periodic-table', '下列哪一組元素在週期表中屬於同一族，化學性質相似？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "碳、氮、氧"}, {"key": "B", "text": "氫、氦、碳"}, {"key": "C", "text": "鋰、鈉、鉀"}, {"key": "D", "text": "鈉、鎂、鋁"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '週期表中同一直行稱為「族」，同族元素的化學性質相似。鋰、鈉、鉀都在第 1 族（鹼金屬），都很活潑、容易和水反應。碳、氮、氧和鈉、鎂、鋁都是同一橫列（同一週期），不同族。', '["週期表的「族」指的是直行還是橫列？", "哪一組都是非常活潑、會和水劇烈反應的金屬？"]'::jsonb, '{"A": "碳、氮、氧是同一週期（橫列），不是同一族。", "D": "鈉、鎂、鋁是同一週期（橫列），不是同一族。", "B": "氫、氦、碳分別在不同族，性質差異很大。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null),
  ('SC-8B-1-10', 'SC-8B-1', 'periodic-table', '氖（Ne）位於週期表最右邊的一族。有關這一族元素的敘述，下列何者正確？', '[{"key": "A", "text": "都能和氧迅速結合形成氧化物"}, {"key": "B", "text": "化學性質很不活潑，稱為惰性氣體（鈍氣）"}, {"key": "C", "text": "常溫下都是具有延展性的固體金屬"}, {"key": "D", "text": "很容易和水劇烈反應產生氫氣"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '週期表最右邊一族是惰性氣體（鈍氣），如氦、氖、氬，常溫下都是氣體，化學性質非常穩定，很難和其他物質反應，所以氖可用在霓虹燈、氦可用來填充氣球。', '["週期表中金屬多在左邊還是右邊？", "霓虹燈裡的氖氣為什麼安全、不會燃燒？"]'::jsonb, '{"C": "最右邊一族是非金屬氣體，不是金屬。", "D": "這是第 1 族鹼金屬（如鈉、鉀）的性質。", "A": "惰性氣體很難和氧反應。"}'::jsonb, 2, 'original', null, null)
